1 RELI Robert Moon served as churchwarden at St Michael's in Kirkham around 1714 and 1715; one of the bells at St Anne's Church in Copp came from Kirkham and is inscribed with the names of the churchwardens, “Robert Moon, James Gradwell, A.R. 1714.”
2 DATE 1715
2 PLAC St Michael's Church, Kirkham, Lancashire, England, Kingdom of Great Britain
2 OBJE @O8833@
1 DEAT
2 DATE Jan 1750
2 PLAC Horse Stone House, Eccleston, Lancashire, England, Kingdom of Great Britain
2 SOUR @S1493367339@
3 _APID 1,7249::100510858
2 NOTE In his will, made 22 July, 1735, he is described as yeoman of Eccleston near Croston, and it was in Eccleston at Horse Stone House he spent his latter years where he was overseer of the poor for that parish 26 April, 1736.
1 BURI
2 DATE 15 Jan 1750
2 PLAC St Mary the Virgin Church, Eccleston, Lancashire, England, Kingdom of Great Britain
2 SOUR @S1493367339@
3 _APID 1,7249::100510858
2 OBJE @O4774@
2 NOTE Robert Moon was 76 when he died, and was buried on 15 Jan 1750 in the north aisle of Eccleston church next to the pulpit; the burial place of the Horse Stone house estate.
