2 NOTE In his will 21 Aug., 1817, he is described as yeoman of Eccleston. He gave his leasehold house, outbuildings, cottage and land in Wrightington occupied by Thomas Smith as tenant, to his son Peter Moon, who also was the miller of Eccleston.
1 OCCU He was tenant of the water corn mill of Eccleston, had a tenement near Nursery house in Parr Lane, and Tanner’s farm, now Springbank in Wrightington, near Appley Bridge (38.0.38 acres. op­posite the end of Skull Lane).
