2 OBJE @O8431@
2 NOTE Charged for "wilful murder" of his wife Margaret on 15th July 1876 who he kicked to death and committed to a trial at Liverpool Assizes.
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Change of verdict
2 DATE 18 Jul 1876
2 PLAC Liverpool Assizes, Liverpool, Merseyside, England, United Kingdom
2 NOTE Andrew McKerney was instead charged with 'manslaughter' rather than 'wilful murder' when he appeared at the magistrates; it was determined that McKerney did not have the intention of killing his wife; he was sent to Kirkdale Gaol, Liverpool to awai
3 CONC t trial.
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Trial
2 DATE 21 Jul 1876
2 PLAC Liverpool Assizes, Liverpool, Merseyside, England, United Kingdom
2 NOTE Andrew McKerney pleads guilty to manslaughter, not murder of his wife; the prosecution agreed to accept the plea; it was then the task to determine why the original verdict of wilful murder was incorrect; McKerney was sentenced to 15 months hard la
3 CONC bour.
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Release from prison
2 DATE Oct 1877
2 PLAC Kirkdale Gaol, Liverpool, Merseyside, England, United Kingdom
2 OBJE @O1213@
2 NOTE Andrew McKerney is released from prison after serving fifteen months of hard labour by committing manslaughter against his wife Margaret on 15th July 1876.
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Chilling True Tales of Old Preston
2 DATE Sep 1990
2 PLAC Wigan, Lancashire, England, United Kingdom
2 OBJE @O459@
2 NOTE Keith Johnson's book features the story of the murder of Margaret McKerney by her husband Andrew as featured in the Preston Chronicle in July 1876.
