3 _APID 1,8054::1096745
1 EVEN
2 TYPE Travel
2 DATE 5 Oct 1850
2 PLAC Salt Lake City, Salt Lake County, Utah, USA
2 NOTE On 28 May, 1850, Henry’s family left Iowa, crossed the Mis­souri 21 June, the south fork of the Platt River 29 July, and arrived in Salt Lake City 5 October of that year.
1 RELI Henry Moon was ordained High Priest and set apart as a Bishop by President Brigham Young, 21 October, 1855.  Thus the youthful pioneer and farmer became the third bishop of the first Ward, now Duncan Ward, Liberty Stake, an office which he held 1
2 CONC 4 years.
2 DATE 21 Oct 1855
2 PLAC  Salt Lake City, Salt Lake County, Utah, USA
1 RESI
2 DATE 1856
2 PLAC Duncan Ward, Utah County, Utah, USA
2 NOTE He acquired 160 acres of land in Sugar House area and grew corn; and it is said that when wheat was $24.00 a hundred he allowed, as bishop, each family to have 100 pounds of wheat for $6.00 a hundred.
1 OCCU Bishop Henry Moon was a school board member for many years and it was a major principle of his policy to establish schools and improve education.
2 DATE 1860
2 PLAC  Salt Lake City, Salt Lake County, Utah, USA
1 RESI
2 DATE 1860
2 PLAC Great Salt Lake City Ward 1, Great Salt Lake City, Great Salt Lake, Utah Territory, USA
2 SOUR @S1500780222@
3 PAGE Year: 1860; Census Place: Great Salt Lake City Ward 1, Great Salt Lake, Utah Territory; Page: 86
3 _APID 1,7667::34759731
