2 NOTE John Moon died on the evening of 12th July 1850 when his company of waggons were ten miles east of Fort Kearny. According to William Snow's journal, on 5th July, Moon was found in bad health and unable to walk and on the 7th was "baptised for his h
3 CONC ealth."
