2 CONC dder or steep stairs provided the only exit. During a storm, the quarters were &amp;ldquo;hatched down&amp;rdquo; to prevent water from flooding the hold. The poorly ventilated constantly rocking cabins soon filled with smoke from a few dimly lit l
2 CONC amps. The terrible smells from seasick passengers only added to the suffocating smoke. Buckets or chamber pots took care of personal needs if they could be reached in time. Groaning land-lovers, whining babies, crashing waves and howling winds adde
