2 TITL Obituary for Sarah Ann Dudley Rasmussen
1 _OID 076096c4-f401-4b27-97be-847fe1e761b5
1 DATE 28 Jan 1942
1 PLAC Vernal Express
1 _DSCR Obituary for Sarah Ann Dudley Rasmussen
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Funeral Services Held at Lapoint for Mrs. Rasmussen.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;LAPOINT (Special) -- Funeral services were held Monday at 1:00 p
2 CONC .m. at the Lapoint Chapel for Mrs. Sarah Ann Dudley Rasmussen under the direction of Bishop Harvey Hullinger. The opening selection by the Lapoint choir was &amp;quot;Softly Tenderly.&amp;quot; Invocation was offered by Verdin R. Johnson. Rex and C
2 CONC ynthia Taylor favored us with a duet, &amp;quot;When It&amp;#39;s Lighting Time in the Valley.&amp;quot;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;The speakers were J. C. Hacking and Archie Johnson. Orloa Reynolds played a piano solo. Ou
2 CONC r Own Red, White and Blue in honor of Mrs. Rasmussen&amp;#39;s son, Lloyd, who is now overseas with the U.S. Marines. Bishop Hullinger gave closing remarks and the closing selection, &amp;quot;Sweet Hour of Prayer,&amp;quot; was by the choir. Bened
2 CONC iction was by Warren Billings.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Interment was at the Vernal Memorial Park under the direction of the Swain Funeral &amp;#39;Home.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Mrs. Rasmusse
2 CONC n was born November 3, 1871 in Spanish Fork, the daugther of Andrew and Mary Markham Dudley. She was married to Ephraim Rasmussen December 31, 1891 at Jensen. The couple moved to Lapoint in 1907, residing here until 1938 when they moved to Salt Lak
2 CONC e City to make their home with their daughter, Mrs. Mary Sessions.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Both Mr. and Mrs. Rasmussen were active in LDS church work. Mr. Rasmussen preceded his wife in death October 25, 1942.&lt;/font&g
2 CONC t;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Besides her daughter, Mrs. Sessions, Mrs. Rasmussen is survived by four sons, Grand and Thurmer Rasmussen of Lapoint, Ollie Rasmussen of Roosevelt and Louis Lloyd Rasmussen of the U. S. Marines; eleven gran
2 CONC dchildren; five brothers, Andrew , Joseph and Sanford Dudley of Jensen, and Steven and Osmar Dudley of Canada; and three sisters, Mrs. Guyletta Campbell and Mrs. Julina Butcher of Vernal, and Mrs. Parney Witherall of Kansas City, Kansas.&lt;/font&g
2 CONC t;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Those attending the service from distant points were Andrew Dudley, Mr. and Mrs. Joseph Dudley, Mary Ellen Wilkins, Mr. and Mrs. Jesse Butcher, A. DeMar Dudley, George E. Wilkins, Mr. and Mrs. Harland Wilki
2 CONC ns, Orvil Dudley, Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Hall, Mr. and Mrs. William Ashby, Mr. and Mrs. Wells Ashby, Mr. and Mrs. Warren Billings, Mrs. Sam Hatch, Mr. and Mrs. L. H. Woodard, Verdin R. Johnson, Archie Johnson, Ernest M. Johnson, Mrs. Effie Powell, Mrs
2 CONC . A. T. Johnson, Mrs. J. W. Bastian, Mrs. Eleanor Chew and Dean Bigelow.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;-Vernal Express, January 28, 1943, transcribed by Rhonda Holton&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metad
2 CONC ataxml>
