1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #000066; font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11px; -webkit-border-horizontal-spacing: 2px; -webkit-border-vertical-spacing: 2px"&gt;After Peter Charles and Lydi
2 CONC a were married, they lived in Kanesv&lt;br&gt;ille, Now Council Bluffs, where he spent two and a half years le&lt;br&gt;arning the Wheel-Right orwagon makers trade and carpenty. Hi&lt;br&gt;s salary was $7.50 a week. After learning his trade he sta
2 CONC rte&lt;br&gt;d out on his own. He moved his family to Tabor Iowa in1867 an&lt;br&gt;d lived there until 1870, where he worked at his trade. In Marc&lt;br&gt;h of1870 he moved his famly to Feeders Mill, now known as Har&lt;br&gt;d Scratch, HarrisonC
2 CONC o. Ia. There he also worked at his trade f&lt;br&gt;rom 1870-73. In 1872 he bought 80 acres of land at $2.00 per ac&lt;br&gt;red near the center of Union Twp., Harrison County, Iowa, and move&lt;br&gt;d to this location in 1873 and started farming
2 CONC . He built a smal&lt;br&gt;l house 14 feet by 16 feet of native black walnut and kept addin&lt;br&gt;g to thehouse as the family increased and continued to purchas&lt;br&gt;e more land until he had 320 acres. All fenced in hog tight wir&lt;br&gt;
2 CONC e netting. He owned this farm until his death on april 28 190&lt;br&gt;1 In 1896 Charles retired from farming and moved to Woodbine, Ha&lt;br&gt;rrison Co. Ia where he and his sons Frank, Nathan and Curtis bui&lt;br&gt;lt a beautiful house on Norma
2 CONC l Street, moving in before the hous&lt;br&gt;e was completed. He worked on the house for a year or two whe&lt;br&gt;n he became ill. In January 1901 it was discovered that he ha&lt;br&gt;d dropsy. In March he went to California thinking it would b
2 CONC e g&lt;br&gt;ood for him, but returned and died in April 28, 1901,at his hom&lt;br&gt;e in Woodbine, Ia at the age of 57. He was buried at Valley Vie&lt;br&gt;w Cemetery, Persia, Harrison County, Ia.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&
2 CONC gt;&lt;p&gt;http://www.whosyerdad-e.com/families-m/individual.php?pid=I17515&amp;amp;ged=second.ged&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
