1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;John Moon held the leasehold estate of Whinneyfield from th
2 CONC e Warrens of Poynton, the superior lords of Woodplumpton. This property contained approximately 105 acres in 1839 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;but was probably larger before the construction of the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span styl
2 CONC e="font-family: times;"&gt;canal and redistribution of fields, and was called Bartle Crown. The land lies between \/Voodplumpton village and Crown lane, Swillbrook. The old house was de&amp;shy; molished some years ago by the late Mr. T. Barron an
2 CONC d new buildings erected. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
