1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; margin: 0px"&gt;Ezra Kent of Suffield married Elizabeth Gillet on November 8, 1750 in the Congregational Ch
2 CONC urch in Windsor CT by Rev Hezekiah Bissell.&amp;nbsp; The area later become Bloomfield, CT.&amp;nbsp; Listed in &amp;ldquo;Early Connecticut Marriages&amp;rdquo; complied by Frederick W. Bailey 1997.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal norma
2 CONC l 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; margin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; margin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal norma
2 CONC l 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; margin: 0px"&gt;Tombstone in Old Southwick Cemetery says &amp;ldquo;Elizabeth, wife of Ezra Kent&amp;rdquo; died 1803.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; m
2 CONC argin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; margin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; margin: 0px"&gt;Tw
2 CONC o different family history books list Elizabeth&amp;rsquo;s birth in May 1732 in Wintonbury/Windsor, CT.&amp;nbsp; (This area is now called Bloomfield.)&amp;nbsp; They list her parents as Sargeant Jonah Gillett (born Oct 18, 1708) and Elizabeth Gra
2 CONC nger (born Nov 2, 1709).&amp;nbsp; These books look well put together but does not provide the source of information for Jonah and Elizabeth&amp;rsquo;s family.&amp;nbsp; I suspect you will find Elizabeth&amp;rsquo;s baptism record in the records o
2 CONC f the above church where she was married.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; margin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; mar
2 CONC gin: 0px"&gt;These books both trace Jonah as the great grandson of Jonathan Gillet (and Mary Dolbiar/Dolbere) who arrived in Massachusetts in 1630 aboard the ship &amp;ldquo;Mary and John.&amp;rdquo;&amp;nbsp; He is listed as a &amp;ldquo;foundin
2 CONC g father&amp;rdquo; of Windsor, CT, the first settlement in that state and where the family lived through the birth and marriage of Elizabeth.&amp;nbsp; The book shows Thomas Barbour, another Windsor founding father, as another of Jonah&amp;rsquo;
2 CONC s great grandfathers.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; margin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; margin: 0px"&gt;These b
2 CONC ooks say the Gillets were originally French Hugenots who immigrated to Britain after the St Bartholomew Day Massacre of Protestants in 1532.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min-height: 13px; margin: 0p
2 CONC x"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; margin: 0px"&gt;1 - &amp;ldquo;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Gillette Families (Gillet-Gillett-Gillette) Including Some of the Descenda
2 CONC nts of the Immigrants Jonathan Gillet and Nathan Gillet, Brothers from Chalcombe, Somersetshire, England&amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt; by Bertha Bortle Beal Aldridge 1955.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; min
2 CONC -height: 13px; margin: 0px"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p style="font: normal normal normal 11px/normal 'lucida grande'; margin: 0px"&gt;2 - &amp;ldquo;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Genealogical Data Concerning the Families of Gill
2 CONC ett - Gillett - Gillette&amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt; by Ester Gillett Latham 1953&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
