1 _DSCR The Griswold family, England-America: Edward of Windsor, Connecticut, Matthew of Lyme, Connecticut, Michael of Wethersfield, Connecticut / compiled by Glenn E. Griswold. v.2
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: center;" align="center"&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'tim
2 CONC es new roman','serif'; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;His Will&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0in 0in 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman
2 CONC ','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;In the name of God, Amen, I, Isaac Griswold of Killingworth, in the county of New London, and Colony of Connecticut, in New England, finding my health an
2 CONC d strength to decline and being sensible of my frailty and mortality, yet through Divine Goodness at this time, of sound mind and memory, do now this twenty-second day of May, Anno Domini, one thousand seven hundred and twenty-three, make this my l
2 CONC ast will and testament, Imprimis:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I will an
2 CONC d bequeath my soul into the hand of God, my merciful and faithful creator, hoping for acceptance through the merits and moderation of Jesus Christ, my dear and suggicient redeemer, and my body to the dust, to be buried as my executor shall order, h
2 CONC oping for a glorious resurrection, and as touching such goods and worldly estate with which God hath been pleased to bless me, and after just debts and funeral defrayed I dispose of will and bequeath as followeth:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line
2 CONC >&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I give and bequeath to my beloved wife one third part of all my moveable effect
2 CONC s that shall be found at my decease and to the use and improvement of all remainder of the removable effects during her natural life, and what shall remain, that is to say, two thirds that she has the improvement of, at her decease, I give to my so
2 CONC n Isaac, I also give to my loving wife the use and improvement of the house and homestead where I now dwell and the improvement of one third part of the other old improved lands, if she hath need of it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&
2 CONC lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I will and bequeath to my oldest son Michael Griswold the whole of that land where he no
2 CONC w dwells being sixty four acres with house and barn thereon standing, as also the land at Meadow, being sixty acres together with what hath since been added thereto as also the acres of Salt Marsh lying in the further quarter, also half my Marsh ly
2 CONC ing in the Broad Meadow, also half the land lying above the Long Meadow belonging to me. As also one pasture on the Rocky Hill over the way opposite to the house where I now dwell, as also twenty eight acres of my land lying near Hammonasset Rive
2 CONC r in the additional Grant of I should not have occasion to sell it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&
2 CONC amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Item: I will and bequeath to my son Isaac Griswold all the land adjoining to the land of Gersham Palmer both within and without the common fence and the house standing thereon, also my land in the neck both upland and meadow
2 CONC , also my land at a place called Nod, also the one half of my Marsh lying in Broad Meadow, also the whole of my meadow lying in the Cove. Also half my land lying above Long Meadow, as also the remainder of my land lying in the additional Grant nea
2 CONC r Hammonasset River if I should not have occasion to sell it, also the two thirds of my removable estate of which I have given my wife for improvements as above the legalities hereafter mentioned being by him first paid.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</lin
2 CONC e><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Item: I will and bequeath to my daughter Hannah Griswold my house and ho
2 CONC me lot where I now dwell and to the heirs of her body, and for what of issue to return to her brothers and sisters and to the heirs of their bodies, also twenty pounds which I order her brother Isaac to pay her.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&
2 CONC lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Item: I will and bequeath to my daughter Elizabeth Hull forty acres of land, to b
2 CONC e layout in the next division upon my property to her and to her heirs of her body and for what of issue to her brothers and sisters and to their heirs of their bodies, as also forty pounds to be paid to her by her brother Isaac.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p
2 CONC &gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;For due execution of this my Last Will &amp;amp; Testament I d
2 CONC o hereby constitute &amp;amp; appoint my two sons Michael &amp;amp; Isaac to be my executors and do order my son Isaac to pay his sisters the legacies above mentioned. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%
2 CONC ; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Signed, Sealed, Pronounced &amp;amp; Declared to be my Last Will &amp;amp; Testament in the presence of witnesses.&lt;/spa
2 CONC n&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0in 0in 10pt; text-align: center;" align="center"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Isaac Gr
2 CONC iswold&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin: 0in 0in 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Jared Elliot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;
2 CONC /p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Jonathan Franklin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new rom
2 CONC an','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Samuel Parmalee &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; The following distribution being exhibited i
2 CONC n Court was approved and ordered to be recorded.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; A distribution of the Estate formerly of Mr. Isa
2 CONC ac Griswold of Killingworth, deceased, which was by Will given to his daughter Hannah, according to Court order divided s followeth: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','ser
2 CONC if'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; To Michael Griswold; to Lydia Nichels; to Elizabeth Davis; to Sybil Davis; to Rebina Chatfield, to heirs of Elizabeth Hull, deceased; to Stephen Griswold.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span sty
2 CONC le="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; Distribution Completed Feb. 2, 1760.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: 'times new roman','serif
