1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;LANCASTER GAZETTE SUPPLEMENT PUBLISHED&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;MAY 19th 1869 for the week ending MAY 22nd 1869&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Many of our fellow townsmen will regret to see the nam
2 CONC e of &amp;nbsp;Mr. George Danson in our present obituary. In Mr. Dansons death the Conservative cause in Lancaster will have to lament the departure of one of&amp;nbsp; the most steady, consistent, and eminently useful member of the Conservative Pa
2 CONC rty here. We have known him from his boyhood, and can testify to the immense &amp;nbsp;service he has been enabled to do the good cause, owing to his intimate aquaintance with the constituency. He was, besides, a very respectable tradesman, and, a
2 CONC s we have said, will be much lamented.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Obituary reads -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;On the 16th inst. very suddenly, Mr George Danson, Autioneer and Sherrifs Officer, aged 53 years. Deeply regretted.&lt;/
2 CONC p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
