2 TITL Richard Rigby&#39;s Army  Service
1 _OID 19237ec6-fc0d-4a08-b9bb-3118bce744c8
1 _DSCR Brindle Palls
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;RICHARD RIGBY enlisted at Blackburn on the 10th October 1915, being mobilised as Driver161774 in the ROYAL ENGINEERS. He served abroad from the 29th April 1917 with leave back to Britain between the 26th Februar
2 CONC y and the 14th March 1918. After the Armistice he was in hospital at the 1st Canadian Field Hospital until the 4th January 1919. He left the army on the 21st September 1919 having been medically examined at Bonn in Germany four days previously. Thi
2 CONC s ties in to his service record which showed that he had served &amp;quot;in Germany&amp;quot; with the &amp;quot;EE Cable Section&amp;quot;. He was known to have returned to Brindle after the war.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Richards service record survive
2 CONC s in the National Archives but that of his brother does not.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
