2 TITL August Hjorth History
1 _OID 19d56c3d-bd3c-4389-a57e-c3b576b69532
1 DATE 1847-1935
1 _DSCR History 
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line /><line>&lt;tbody&gt;</line><line>&lt;tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;td class="gr" style="font-size: 13px; padding: 4px; background: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br&gt;Conquerors of the West: Stalwart Mormon Pioneers, volume 2&amp;nbsp;&lt;
2 CONC br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Name: August Adrainus Hjorth&lt;br&gt;Birth Date: 04 Mar 1847&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Birth Place: Love, Soro, Denmark&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Parents: Niels Peter and Dorthea Ancena Jorgensen Hansen Hjorth&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Death Date: 16 J
2 CONC un 1935&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Death Place: Salt Lake City, Utah&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Arrival: 22 Sep 1861, John A. Wooley Co.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Spouse: Hulda Content Terry&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Marriage Date: 17 Oct 1872&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Marriage Place
2 CONC : Salt Lake City, Utah&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Spouse's Birth Date: 02 Jul 1852&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Spouse's Birth Place: Union Fort, Salt Lake, Utah&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Spouse's Death Date: 23 Jan 1925&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Spouse's Death Place: Indianola
2 CONC , Sanpete, Utah&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;August was an Indian Scout to Colonel Patriarch E. Conner and a veteran of the Black Hawk Indian War. He made two trips back to Missouri to bring immigrants to Utah in 1866 . He served a mission to the U
2 CONC te Indians in 1877 . He was first brakeman of the first train that ran from Promontory to Echo Canyon and was present at the driving of the Golden Spike. He served as the only doctor in Indianola, Utah . He was a farmer by occupation. They lived i
2 CONC n Fairview, Sanpete, Utah , until about 1879 when they moved to Clinton, Utah . He died in Salt Lake City .&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Children: Lillian Loana , b. 8 Jul 1873 , Fairview, Sanpete, Utah . Md. 7 Nov 1895 , George Samuel Pickerin
2 CONC g . D. 9 Nov 1945 , Payson, Utah . Therissa Alzina , b. 28 Mar 1875 , Fairview, Utah . Md. 13 Feb 1895 , Wallace Crandall . D. 9 Feb 1965 , Springville, Utah . Myra Estella , b. 19 Aug 1877 , Fairview, Utah . Md. 20 Jan 1898 , S. Edward Hancock . D
2 CONC . 5 Jan 1959 , Salt Lake City, Utah . August Adrainus , Jr, b. 17 Sep 1879 , Clinton, Utah . Md. Charlotta Neibur . D. 19 Aug 1969 , Bel Air, California . William Herman , b. 6 Jun 1881 , Fairview, Utah . D. 8 Jan 1882 , Clinton, Utah . Infant. Lav
2 CONC ee Vilate , b. 15 Jul 1883 , Clinton, Utah . Md. 19 Mar 1902 , Oliver Emery Tanner . D. 16 Jul 1962 , Paul, Idaho . Hulda Priscilla , b. 6 Sep 1886 , Clinton, Utah . Md. 9 Dec 1910 , William Gale . D. 6 May 1974 , St. George, Utah . Otis Algerno
2 CONC n , b. 4 Dec 1888 , Clinton, Utah . Md. 15 Feb 1915 , Velma Miner . D. 28 Feb 1976 , Provo, Utah .&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Written by Carlos Hjorth&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tbody&gt;</line><line /><line>&lt
2 CONC ;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-center; color: #666666;"&gt;Added by:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="minus1" style="font-size: 11px; color: #666666;"&gt;Burnt Almond Fudge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br st
2 CONC yle="font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-center; color: #666666;"&gt;6/01/2012&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 13px; line-height: norma
2 CONC l; text-align: -webkit-center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; text-align: -webkit-center; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
