1 _OID 1b403631-5df6-4b3a-a5dc-dc70959cf01d
1 DATE 1557
1 PLAC Whittington in Lonsdale,Lancashire
1 _DSCR Will of Richard Newton of Whittington 
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;THE WILL OF RICHARD NEWTON OF WHITTINGTON,CO. LANCASHIRE,1557&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p
2 CONC &gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;AUGUST 12 1557,I RICHARDE NEWTON of the parishe of Whittington in the countye of Lancashire.My bodye to be buryed in the parishe church of Whittington in the south ile ,near unto Sayn
2 CONC t Nicholas aullter. To Marmaduce my sonne my tenament in the parishe of Sedbarghe,called castellhalle ,in land of the annuell rent of xlvj viij and also the tenament of Bryan Neuton in Whittington of the yearlye rent of x iid for the terme of his n
2 CONC aturall lyve.&amp;nbsp; To my sonne Richard Newton twoe tenements in Catton&amp;nbsp; of the yearlye rent of xxvj viij and a tenement in Toddguyll for the yearlye rent of viij and a tenement in Dockare of the yearlye rent of viij ,a tenemen in the&
2 CONC amp;nbsp; holding of William Battie of Nether burrow ,of the parishe of Tunstall and a tenement in the holding of Richard Wilson and Roger Ullothrones for the annual rent of xij , to my sonne Thomas Neuton viij oxenn with plughe and plow geare an
2 CONC d allso waynes and wayne geare with whealls and also vj syllver sponnes with a salt of syllver. Item to the said Thomas , for to be heirelomes at the house, iij great arckes in a moallt chamber , with a great arcke and a Knoppe in the barne ,with t
2 CONC he leyd, a great brasse potte , two long iron spits and an allmarye in the butre , a great presser in the great chamber and a chist in the parlor. Item i geave and bequeath to Sir Richard Godshallf preste x to praye for me and myne . Item i geave a
2 CONC nd bequeath to Miles Huddlestone two sillver sponnes. Item i geave and bequeath to Mr Frauncis Tunstall a dispar board cloith contayninge by estimacon v yards long and two yeards broad. To William Neuton my servant xx or ells a new callvett cowe ,o
2 CONC ver and besydes his wayges. To Elsabethe my wyff , and Marmaduce and Richard Neuton my sonnes , the remaynder or leaue of my parte of goods, and to Thomas my sonne all my tenements and fermhollds . Mr. Frauncis Tunstall ,supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/s
2 CONC pan&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[proved at Richmond ,25 November 1557 ]&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
