2 TITL Possible Saint in the family?
1 _OID 1b7b020a-30bf-4ab4-b32b-0bdd0b537b78
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;There seems to be at least Two possible baptisms for Richard Norcross. One on the 2nd July 1682, to a John Norcross of Ribchester, and another on 2?th July 1668, to a James Norcross of Dilworth. If the answer i
2 CONC s James, then it is possible that we might have an Uncle who was ordained a saint.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;James, the son of Richard of Ribchester, seems to have married an Alice White, the daughter of Christopher [Expher], in 1654, in Goosn
2 CONC argh. Alice then seems to have died in childbirth, whilest giving birth to a Christopher [Expher] Norcross on the 12th May 1662. He was probably named after her Father. She was buried in Ribchester on the same date as Christopher's baptism and note
2 CONC d as being James's wife. Also, Christopher was noted as being the son of James of Dilworth.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;James then seems to have married an Elizabeth Pleasington 'Plessington', in Garstang, on 26th September 1666. She was noted a
2 CONC t her burial, on 15th March 1681, in Ribchester, as being the wife of James of Dilworth. Elizabeth Plesington was baptised on 26th August 1633, in Garstang, to a Robert Plessington. Who was probably the Robert Plessington of Dimples Hall in Garstan
2 CONC g. He was the Father of John Plessington 'Pleasington', who was a Catholic priest, who was executed for being so and then later ordained a saint by the church. &amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
1 _CREA 2020-08-26 21:16:42.000
