2 TITL Amanda Moon&#39;s recollection of her father Henry Moon
1 _OID 1c103494-a02d-4e7a-80b1-c8c0d22bac67
1 DATE 1963
1 PLAC Neola, Duchesne County, Utah, United States
1 _DSCR Extract from The Moons of Amounderness
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Mrs. Amanda Duncan, one of Henry Moon's children, and stil
2 CONC l living at Neola, Utah, aged 93 years, has &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;written, &amp;ldquo;We were all taught to work in our youth. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;There were no idle hands around our h
2 CONC ome, hours &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;were never set for us but we worked early and late. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;We all helped to work on clearing brush, picking&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;spa
2 CONC n style="font-family: times;"&gt;rocks, milking cows and herding them, and churning butter. We had to go to Kamas, 6 miles, to our nearest store and post oilice. Our schools were primitive in&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times
2 CONC ;"&gt;those days, we all went together in one small room and one teacher. I think it is a wonder we did secure any education at all under those circumstances. We did not have the lovely clothes and good food that exists &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=
2 CONC "font-family: times;"&gt;nowadays. My father said that when he first came&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;to Utah, and worked upon his farm, he ate and lived on roots or any foodstuff that was palatable. One thing &lt;
2 CONC /span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;that we had in my early days was respect for those &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;over us and especially our parents. They were kind and lived in peace and harmony giving prais
2 CONC e to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Lord for his many blessings . . &amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;
2 CONC span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Mrs. Duncan had heard her father say: &amp;ldquo;All my life &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;has been spent in service for others and I am not sorry fo
2 CONC r it; for we get the most pleasure in doing good.&amp;rdquo; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;<
2 CONC /line></content></metadataxml>
