1 DATE Nov 1959
1 PLAC Vernal Express
1 _DSCR Obituary for Jemima Moon Dudley
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Final Tributes Paid Mrs. Dudley In Tuesday Rites.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Funeral services for Mrs. Jemima Moon Dudley, 79, who died Novembe
2 CONC r 7 at 10 a.m. at her home of a heart condition was held Tuesday, November 10 at 11 a.m. in Naples Ward Chapel under the direction of the Jensen Ward bishopric.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Prayer at the mortuary was by Geral
2 CONC d Ross. The opening song at the chapel was &amp;quot;I Know That My Redeemer Lives,&amp;quot;sung by Frank Walker, Don Walker, Ralph Walker and Lois Erickson. Driver E. Smith offered the invocation. &amp;quot;Hold Thou My Hand,&amp;quot; was sung b
2 CONC y Gerald and Margaret Caldwell. First speaker was Les Murphy. A Tribute to Mother,&amp;quot; was read by Irwin Moon. &amp;quot;That Wonderful Mother of Mine,&amp;quot; was sung by LuRae Caldwell. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt
2 CONC ;Second speaker was Archie Johnson. Closing song was &amp;quot; Say Goodnight Here and Good Morning Up There,&amp;quot; by Mrs. Lois Erickson and Mrs. LuRae Caldwell. Closing prayer was offered by Wesley Robertson.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&l
2 CONC t;font size="4"&gt;Pallbearers were Charles Dudley, Mack Holmes, Dennis Hatch, Carl Alder, Jay Alder and Devier Dudley. Burial was in the Jensen Cemetery where the grave was dedicated by Osmer Dudley.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4
2 CONC "&gt;Mrs. Dudley was born January 29, 1880, in Salt Lake City, Utah, a daughter of John Thomas and Catherine Duncan Moon. She married Joseph S. Dudley in Jensen, Utah on March 5, 1902. The marriage was solemnized in the Salt Lake Temple on Septembe
2 CONC r 12, 1905. During recent years Mrs. Dudley and her husband have done Temple work in the Salt Lake, Canadian, Idaho Falls, Logan, Manti, St. George and Mesa Temples.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;She is survived by her husband
2 CONC , two sons, four daughters, Curtis and Orvil of Jensen; Mrs. Gerald (Katherine) Ross, Murray; Mrs. Wesley (Mary) Robertson, Provo; Mrs. David (Alta) Alder, Manti; Mrs. Earl (Veda) Hatch, Vernal; five brothers, Moroni Moon, Jensen; Charles Irvin Moo
2 CONC n, Orem; Harold Moon, Compton, California; Albert Moon, Oxnard, California; three sisters, Mrs. Edith Druwell, Blith, California; Mrs. Lea Hiener, Heyburn, Idaho; Mrs. Florence Brown, 21 grandchildren, seven great-grandchildren.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&
2 CONC gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;-Vernal Express, November 1959&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
