2 TITL Logan Utah Temple
1 _OID 21e26438-8842-48bf-b5a8-9dead2266715
1 _DSCR Ruwaine was born on 23 Sep 1865 in Saint George, Washington, Utah. She died  on 1 Mar 1900. She was born in the covenant she was baptized on 23 Sep 1898. She was endowed on 17 Nov 1904 in the Logan Utah temple.
2 CONT 
2 CONT In Mormonism, the endowment is an ordinance (ritual ceremony) designed to prepare participants to become kings, queens, priests, and priestesses in the afterlife. As part of the ceremony, participants take part in a scripted reenactment of the Bibl
2 CONC ical creation and fall of Adam and Eve. They also are taught highly symbolic gestures and passwords, thought to be needed to pass by angels guarding the way to heaven, and are instructed not to reveal these gestures and passwords. The ceremony als
2 CONC o includes a washing and anointing, and receipt of a "new name" which they are not to reveal to others except at a certain part in the ceremony, and the receipt of the temple garments, which Mormons then are expected to wear under their clothing da
2 CONC y and night throughout their life. As practiced today in The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS Church), the endowment also consists of a series of covenants (promises to God) which participants make, such as a covenant of consecratio
2 CONC n to the LDS Church. All Latter-day Saints who choose to serve as missionaries for the LDS Church or who choose to contract a celestial marriage in an LDS Church temple must first complete the endowment ceremony.
