1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;My mother, LaRetta and Arnold&amp;#39;s sister, told me that in the day when Arnold was born, women would wrap a sheet around the woman who was giving birth and use it to help the child come out the birth cana
2 CONC l by pulling hard on the sheet.&amp;nbsp; Apparently, they pulled too hard, and it cut off oxygen to the baby and Arnold was born black.&amp;nbsp; People thought Grandma had been with a black man.&amp;nbsp; When Arnold recovered, they realized tha
2 CONC t he was deaf.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I was told that Arnold spent most of his life in Ogden going to a deaf school and that where he met his wife Zelma who was also deaf.&amp;nbsp; She was a wonderful person.&amp;nbsp; They died one soon after the othe
2 CONC r.&amp;nbsp; They were great people.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2 April 2009 -- Maralyn Payne Harmston&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
