1 _DSCR Obituary for Sanford Hyrum Dudley
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Funeral Held in Colorado For S. H. Dudley.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Funeral services were held Saturday in Grand Junction, Colorado for Sanfor
2 CONC d Hyrum Dudley, 71, who died at the Veterans Hospital there following a heart attack.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;He is the father of Orvil, DeMarr and Lynne Dudley of Jensen and a brother to Joseph Dudley, also of Jensen wh
2 CONC o all attended the services.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Mr. Dudley is also survived by his wife, Victoria and two sons, Hyrum T. Dudley and Robert Dudley serving in the Navy, who were unable to come home and one daughter, M
2 CONC argaret.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;There are four step children, Dean, Albert, Vera and Irene who survive and a sister Juline Butcher.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Also attending the services from Ve
2 CONC rnal was Mrs. May Woodard Rowley.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;-Vernal Express, April 27, 1961, transcribed by Rhonda Holton&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
