2 CONC N AT JENSEN CHAPEL&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;JENSEN (SPECIAL) -- Funeral services were conducted at the Jensen Chapel on Dec. 12 for George Richardson, a former Jensen resident, who died after a lingering illness at his home at Pleasant Grove on Dec. 9.&l
2 CONC t;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Songs were as follows, "Softly and Tenderly" by a ladies chorus, consisting of Mary Gardner, Josephine Stewart, Gertrude Turner, Veda Hatch and Lavon Wall; "Whispering Hope", by Naomi Dudley and Carwin Snow and "Oh My Father," Lad
2 CONC ies chorus, Naomi Dudley accompanied on the piano.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Opening prayer was by Grant Case and benediction by Wallace Moon. Speakers were Driver Smith of Vernal, Bishop Ross Merrell of Naples and a cousin of Mr. Richardson, James McPhi
2 CONC e of Provo. Closing remarks were by Bishop Moon.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pallbearers were his father-in-law, Murray Merkley and five brothers-in-law, Paul Watkins, Floyd Reynolds, Roy Oaks, Acel Walker and Boyd Price.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interment was i
2 CONC n the Jensen Cemetery. Joseph Dudley dedicated the grave.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mr. Richardson was born near Heber Feb. 13, 1895, the son of John T and Isabelle Muie Richardson. The family moved to Jensen when George was three, where he made his hom
2 CONC e until last spring when he moved to Pleasant Grove with his wife and two small daughters.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was married to Elizabeth Chase July 21, 1915. She died July 23, 1926. To this union three daughters and two sons were born: Mrs. Emma M
2 CONC erkley, Kamas; Mrs. Alta Stewart, Jensen; Mrs. Donna Chivers, Leadville, Colorado; Lavell of Los Angeles, California and Carl of Paonia, Colorado. He was married to Dora Merkley August 28, 1937 and they have two daughter, Georgia and Frances. He le
2 CONC aves in addition to his family, three stepsons: Virgil and James MacMickell of Pleasant Grove and Marion MacMickell of Naples. He also leaves three brothers, Thornton, Nampa, Idaho; Will, Pleasant Grove and Roy, Kamas; one sister, Mrs. Maggis Bel
2 CONC l Moon, Jensen and eight grandchildren.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-Vernal Express, Dec. 19, 1948, transcribed by Rhonda Holton&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Family links:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;Parents:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a cl
