1 _OID 30b54d9f-2c8a-4651-a444-d4c5ca00cbb4
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ogden Standard-Examiner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Saturday, March 7, 1970&lt;br&gt;page nine&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;OBITUARIES&lt;br&gt;MARY ASHTON JONES&lt;br&gt;Cherry Creek, Idah
2 CONC o - Mrs. Mary Emma Ashton Jones, 79, of Cherry Creek, died Thursday of natural causes at her home.&lt;br&gt;Mrs. Jones was born Dec. 30, 1890, in Portage, Utah, a daughter of Hyrum and Emma Ella John Ashton.&lt;br&gt;On March 25, 1914, she was marr
2 CONC ied to Brigham W. Jones in Woodruff, Idaho.&lt;br&gt;She was educated in Woodruff Schools.&lt;br&gt;She was a member of the LDS Church and Relief Society visiting teacher.&lt;br&gt;Surviving are her husband, three sons and five daughters, Leland A
2 CONC . Jones, Malad; M. Sgt. Cleland A. Jones, U.S. Air Force (ret.), Sunset; Avon L. Jones, Mrs. Kenneth (Sylvia Marie) Hefflefinger, Mrs. Glen (LaWana Lou) Spiers, all of Ogden; Mrs. Dale (Alta Mae) Moon, Cherry Creek; Mrs. Ronald (Faye Louise) Jones
2 CONC , Clearfield; Mrs. John (Norma Rae) Everett, Pineville, La.&lt;br&gt;Also surviving are 24 grandchildren, 13 great-grandchildren, three brothers and one sister, Joseph Elias Ashton, Pocatello; Warren V. Ashton, Cherry Creek; Harvey Willis Ashton, M
2 CONC rs. Hugh (Merle) McLane, both of Ogden.&lt;br&gt;Funeral services will be held Monday at 1 p.m. in the Cherry Creek Ward Chapel with Bishop Cordell Williams officiating.&lt;br&gt;Friends may call at the Benson Funeral Home in Malad Sunday evening a
2 CONC nd at the Cherry Creek Ward Relief Society room Monday after 10 a.m. Burial in the Malad Cemetery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
