1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;William was the son of Joseph Aldridge Junior and Mary Earl. Raised by his Maternal grandparents as well as hi
2 CONC s father. Travelled across the United States and finally settled in Alberta. Married twice. First wife was Mary Ann Davis , which he divorced. Both remarried and stayed married to their Subsuquent spouses. He had 3 children by his first wife ( Eliz
2 CONC abeth , Joseph William and William ). These children stayed with their mother. William Aldridge Married Annie ( Anna ) Rolph on 18 Oct 1881 in Garden City, Rich County, Utah. They had 15 Children ( David, Mary Sophia, Oliver, Charlie, Albert, Eleth
2 CONC ine, Amy, Herman, Frank, Annie Diantha, John William, Sterling, Alexander, Alta Matilda, and Lettie). William was predeceased by 3 Children, William ( by his First Marriage ), Elethine and Alexander 9 By his second Marriage ).William and his son Ol
2 CONC iver found the first Oil in Alberta in Cameron Creek, Waterton Lakes National Park.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line
2 CONC -height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Owned the first theatre in Cardston. He would play his fiddle up and down the street to let people know that the movie would be starting soon. When children could not afford a ticket they would ge
2 CONC t a little push into the theater. He figured no child should have to miss a movie. He passed away on 19 June 1916.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
