1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;"He left to his two sons, William and Thomas, &amp;pound;400 each, both were unde
2 CONC r age, and out of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;the interest they were to be maintained and educated&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;and receive the capital on attaining their majority. &lt;/span
2 CONC &gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;He left to Mary Roberts, alias Roberts Wynter, a free born Mulatto woman of the parish of Kingston, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Jamaica, &amp;pound;40, and to each of her two daug
2 CONC hters, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Hannah and Olive, &amp;pound;40; whether servants or illegiti&amp;shy; mate issue is not stated, but the latter seems more probable. To his nephew Henry (son of Richard Moon of Catforth, h
2 CONC is brother) of Kingston, Jamaica, &amp;pound;100. He desired that his executors, namely, John Swarbrick, late, of Kingston, but then of Lancaster, merchant&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;and Richard Moon, should fin
2 CONC d the most speedy way of selling his negroes, lands, houses, furniture and all &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;the property. The residue of both real and personal &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;estate wa
2 CONC s to be divided equally amongst his brothers and sisters living at the time of his decease. The will annuls all former settlements and is signed E. Moon, and witnessed by Richard Moon (his nephew, of Catterall, son of his brother Richard) and Rober
2 CONC t Moon&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;(nephew, son of his brother William, of Clifton) and Thomas Turner."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></meta
2 CONC dataxml>
