2 CONC S (8), son of JAMES (4), resided in Killingworth. He married in 1750, &lt;span style="font-variant: small-caps"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Trial &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-variant: small-caps"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ward &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;o
2 CONC f Killingworth, daughter of Ira and Lydia [Parmelee] &lt;span&gt;Ward &lt;/span&gt;of that place. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-indent: 1em"&gt;&lt;font face="times new roman,times" size="3"&gt;She died after 1762, and he married 2d, .Ja
2 CONC nuary 8, 1767, &lt;span style="font-variant: small-caps"&gt;Abigail &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-variant: small-caps"&gt;Stonk, &lt;/span&gt;who died April 15, 1769. He died at Killingworth, May 30, 1812, in his 87th year.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&g
