1 _OID 3d107c2f-ca3c-49c7-bbbd-60420000fa14
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Ezra Kent of Suffield married Elizabeth Gillet on November 8, 1750 in the Congregational Church in Windsor, CT by Rev. Hezekiah Bissell.&amp;nbsp; The area later became Bloomfield, CT.&amp;n
2 CONC bsp; Listed in &amp;quot;Early Connecticut Marriages&amp;quot; compliledby Frederick W. Bailey 1997.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Tombstone in Old Southwick Cemetery says &amp;quot;Elizabeth, wif
2 CONC e of Ezra Kent&amp;quot; died 1803.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Two different family history books list Elizabeth&amp;#39;s birth in May 1732 in Wintonbury/Windsor, CT.&amp;nbsp; (This area is no
2 CONC w called Bloomfield).&amp;nbsp; They list her parents as Sargeant Jonah Gillett (born Oct. 18, 1708) and Elizabeth Granger (born Nov 1709).&amp;nbsp; These books look well put together, but does not provide the source of information for Jonah and E
2 CONC lizabeth&amp;#39;s family.&amp;nbsp; I suspect you will find Elizabeth&amp;#39;s baptism record in the records of the above church where she was married.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;These book bo
2 CONC th trace Jonah as the great grandson of Jonathan Gillet(and Mary Dolbair/Dolbere) who arrived in Massachusetts in 1630 aboard the ship &amp;quot;Mary &amp;amp; John&amp;quot;.&amp;nbsp; He is listed as &amp;quot;Founding Father&amp;quot; of Windsor
2 CONC , CT, the first settlement in that state and where the family lived through the birth and marriage of Elizabeth.&amp;nbsp; The book shows Thomas Barlow, another Windslow founding father, as mother of Jonah&amp;#39;s great grandfathers.&lt;/font&gt;
2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;These books say the Gillets were originally French Hugenots who immigrated to Britain after the St. Bartholomew Day Massacre of Protestants in 1532.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt
2 CONC ;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Books mentioned above are : &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;quot;Gillette Families (Gilllet-Gillett-Gillette) Including Some of the Decemdants of the Immigrants Jonathan G
2 CONC illet and Nathan Gillet, Brother from Chalcombe, Sommersetshire, England&amp;quot; by Bertha Bortle Beal Aldridge 1955&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;quot;Genealogical Data Concerning the Families of Gillet-Gillett-Gillett
