1 _DSCR Richard Grant Udy thinks this picture was taken in the Fall of 1942. He remembers going down to Utah in the fall to get fresh fruit. They drove a 1941 Ford Coup. They always went through Malad, Garland and Farmington to visit the Potter's. The Pott
2 CONC er's were first cousins to Grandpa Grant Udy. It would take a long time to get Grandma and Grandpas because they had to stop and visit everyone besides the fact that they probably only drove 50 MPH.
