2 TITL First to Arrive in America
1 _OID 454adec4-0cc1-46e3-8ddb-31ab7d970252
1 DATE 1774
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Richard Turner was the first generation of Turner to live in America. He was born in England in 1714. Died in Maine in 1796. He married Eleanor (Nellie) Cowal, daughter of Earl of Cowal of Blackmoor near Preston, England
2 CONC . She died in 1790. In 1774 they came to America. "They were attracted to the Sheepscot region (Maine) by the immense growth of pine timber. They cam farther up the river than any previous settlers and located on the western bank upon a tract of la
2 CONC nd one mile wide, about a half mile above King's Mills, in Whitefield, Maine. There they build a large colonial house. They possessed an ample fortune." Old burial plot on property but since plowed under. </line></content></metadataxml>
