1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Walter Knight Shirley, 11th Earl Ferrers&lt;/strong&gt; (5 June 1864 &amp;ndash; 2 February 1937) was a British architect and nobleman.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<
2 CONC /line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Born at Christ Church, Oxford, where his father was a professor and canon, Shirley was the second but only surviving son of Rev. Walter Waddington Shirley (d. 1866) and his wife Philippa Kn
2 CONC ight.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="fon
2 CONC t-size: small;"&gt;Educated at Winchester College and New College, Oxford, whence he took a B.A. in 1887,&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: s
2 CONC mall;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; Shirley entered the profession of architecture and was articled to Basil Champneys.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span styl
2 CONC e="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; Part of the Arts and Crafts Movement, he was an active member of the Society for the Protection of Ancient Buildings and the Art Workers Guild. He designed a large addition to 35 Victoria Road, Ke
2 CONC nsington in 1896.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&l
2 CONC t;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; Shirley's obituary described him as "a most conscientious architect...over-exacting, if anything, in his own work".&lt;s
2 CONC up&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: sm
2 CONC all;"&gt;On 9 July 1890, Shirley married Mary Jane Moon (d. 10 Jan 1944), daughter of the barrister Robert Moon and the sister of Edward Robert Pacy Moon, by whom he had five children:&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&
2 CONC lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Lady Margery Joan Shirle
2 CONC y (25 November 1891 &amp;ndash; 1 June 1952), married Lancelot Sackville Fletcher on 22 September 1920&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Elizabeth Mary Shirley (30 December 1892 &amp;ndash; 9 Novemb
2 CONC er 1893)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Robert Shirley, 12th Earl Ferrers (1894&amp;ndash;1954)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Lady Phillida S
2 CONC hirley (4 November 1896 &amp;ndash; 26 December 1985), under the name of Sister Mary Phillida a recluse at the Anglican shrine to Our Lady of Walsingham&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Hon. Andre
2 CONC w Shirley (29 December 1900 &amp;ndash; 20 June 1958), married Ethel Muriel Lewis on 30 April 1927 and had issue, art historian&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</line><line>&lt;/ul&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;In 1912, Shir
2 CONC ley succeeded his childless fourth cousin as Earl Ferrers, and largely retired from architecture to tend the family estates. He died at the family seat of Staunton Harold Hall in 1937.&lt;sup&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&
2 CONC lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
