1 _DSCR Obituary for Mary Lucy Markham Dudley
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Sudden Death.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Just as we go to press we learn of the death of Mary L. Dudley, wife of Andrew Dudley, Sr., of Jensen
2 CONC , which occurred yesterday at 11:30 o&amp;#39;clock a.m. after a brief illness of only a few days&amp;#39; duration. Death was due to some internal complication, the nature of which is not certain. &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&
2 CONC gt;The deceased was born at Spanish Fork fifty years ago, and was a daughter of Stephen Markham of that place. With her husband she came to Uintah County and settled at Jensen in 1887, where the family has since resided. She leaves quite a large fa
2 CONC mily, five of whom are still living at home, three girls and two boys, the youngest being five years of age, The funeral will take place tomorrow.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;-Vernal Express, September 9, 1903, transcribed b
2 CONC y Rhonda Holton&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
