1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Mary Atta married Henry James Chatwin in 1900 and was well known in the Jensen area by the &amp;quot;Hotel Atta&amp;quot; which she and Henry built soon after their marriage. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;quot;Aunt Atta&amp;q
2 CONC uot; played hostess to many weary traveler at her hotel where she lived and which she operated until her death in 1941. In 1945 it was sold to Curt Dudley and he made it into apartments. In 1947 it was sold to Mr. and Mrs. Richard Hoffman and late
2 CONC r sold to Lester White. His daughter and husband are living in it at the present time. </line></content></metadataxml>
