1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>The Dewhursts of Dutton and Alston within the parish of Ribchester were gentry for a time. They returned a pedigree during the Visitations of Lancashire of 1613 and 1664-65 and married within the circle of families whic
2 CONC h made up the Lancashire gentry at that time, such as Houghtons, Southworths and Townleys.&amp;nbsp; A Robert Dewhurst had married an earlier Catherine Houghton, daughter of Sir Richard Houghton of HoghtonTower early in the century.&amp;nbsp; It i
2 CONC s not possible to know whether he was a direct ancestor of the Dewhursts of Dutton but they would have been related.&amp;nbsp; </line></content></metadataxml>
