1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Jacob Secrist &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="fon
2 CONC t-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Born: August 15, 1850, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake County, Utah, USA&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans m
2 CONC s,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Died: November 5, 1906, Plymouth, Box Elder County, Utah, USA&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: sm
2 CONC all;"&gt;Son of Jacob Foutz Secrist and Anna Eliza Logan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Married: Polly Estella Smith, September 1
2 CONC 3 1869, Salt Lake City, Utah&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Married: Monica Amelia Potter, September 1, 1881, Salt Lak
2 CONC e City, Utah&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Married: Hannah Priscilla Bourne Potter, April 29, 1903, Salt Lake City, Uta
2 CONC h&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Jacob Moroni Secrist, Bishop of Farmington, Davis County, Utah, was born Aug 15, 1850, in Salt Lake City, Utah, th
2 CONC e son of Jacob Foutz Secrist and Eliza Logan.&amp;nbsp; His parents were natives of Pennsylvania, but later they settled in Illinois, where they resided about two years, until the exodus of the Saints from Nauvoo in 1848.&amp;nbsp; With the main bo
2 CONC dy of the Church they then moved to Winter Quarters on the Missouri River and came to Utah in 1847.&amp;nbsp; The first few years they spent in Salt Lake City, where Jacob Moroni was born.&amp;nbsp; Later the family settled in Davis County.&amp;nbs
2 CONC p; In 1852 the father was called on a mission to Great Britain and on his return from said mission, died while crossing the plains. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'comic sans ms', sans-serif; fo
2 CONC nt-size: small; line-height: 1.3;"&gt;Jacob Moroni married Miss Polly Estella Smith, September 13, 1869.&amp;nbsp; She was the daughter of Thomas Smith and Polly Clark, and was born December 12, 1852.&amp;nbsp; She became the mother of six children
2 CONC .&amp;nbsp; Jacob was baptized May 3, 1861, by Thomas Grover; ordained a Seventy, March 31, 1868, by Elias Van Fleet, and ordained a High Priest and Bishop July 2, 1882 and set apart to preside over the Farmington Ward.&amp;nbsp; He occupied the po
2 CONC sition of Bishop until his death, which occurred at Garland, November 5, 1906.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Jacob's first wife, Polly, died December 12, 188
2 CONC 2, and he later married Monica A. Potter (daughter of Gardner Godfrey Potter and Eveline Hinman), who was born September 2, 1856, at Springville, Utah; she bore her husband two children and died in October, 1902.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</l
2 CONC ine><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;In 1903 (April 29th) Jacob married H. Priscilla Bourne Potter (daughter of Charles Bourne and Jane Alder &amp;amp; former wife of Ernest Potter), who wa
2 CONC s born September 21, 1854, in Salt Lake City, Utah.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Besides taking an active part in Church affairs, Jacob Secrist he
2 CONC ld many positions of a secular nature in the interest of his fellow-citizens.&amp;nbsp; Thus he was president of the Farmington Commercial &amp;amp; Manufacturing Company and a director in the Davis County Bank of Farmington.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: comic sans ms,sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;*LDS Biographical Encyclopedia, Andrew Jenson, Vol. 3, p. 233&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
