2 CONC ;Spouse's Death Date&lt;/strong&gt;: 23 Jan 1925 &lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spouse's Death Place&lt;/strong&gt;: Indianola, Sanpete, Utah &lt;br&gt;August was an Indian Scout to Colonel Patriarch E. Conner and a veteran of the Black Hawk Indian War. H
2 CONC e made two trips back to Missouri to bring immigrants to Utah in 1866 . He served a mission to the Ute Indians in 1877 . He was first brakeman of the first train that ran from Promontory to Echo Canyon and was present at the driving of the Golden S
2 CONC pike. He served as the only doctor in Indianola, Utah . He was a farmer by occupation. They lived in Fairview, Sanpete, Utah , until about 1879 when they moved to Clinton, Utah . He died in Salt Lake City . Children: Lillian Loana , b. 8 Jul 187
2 CONC 3 , Fairview, Sanpete, Utah . Md. 7 Nov 1895 , George Samuel Pickering . D. 9 Nov 1945 , Payson, Utah . Therissa Alzina , b. 28 Mar 1875 , Fairview, Utah . Md. 13 Feb 1895 , Wallace Crandall . D. 9 Feb 1965 , Springville, Utah . Myra Estella , b. 1
2 CONC 9 Aug 1877 , Fairview, Utah . Md. 20 Jan 1898 , S. Edward Hancock . D. 5 Jan 1959 , Salt Lake City, Utah . August Adrainus , Jr, b. 17 Sep 1879 , Clinton, Utah . Md. Charlotta Neibur . D. 19 Aug 1969 , Bel Air, California . William Herman , b. 6 Ju
2 CONC n 1881 , Fairview, Utah . D. 8 Jan 1882 , Clinton, Utah . Infant. Lavee Vilate , b. 15 Jul 1883 , Clinton, Utah . Md. 19 Mar 1902 , Oliver Emery Tanner . D. 16 Jul 1962 , Paul, Idaho . Hulda Priscilla , b. 6 Sep 1886 , Clinton, Utah . Md. 9 Dec 191
