2 TITL Astley family of Stakes Hall
1 _OID 59c2ad2b-bcfd-4668-8921-c2b45c0a3c0b
1 DATE 3  Centuries
1 PLAC Enlgand
1 _DSCR Astley family of Stakes Hall
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;source:http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~jmbhome/dewhurstslancashire.htm&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="color: #7959f7; font-family: 'times new roman'; font-size: medium; background-color: #f7f3ce;" al
2 CONC ign="center"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #255037; font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakes Hall, Blackburn&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="color: #7959f7; font-family: 'times new roman'
2 CONC ; font-size: medium; background-color: #f7f3ce; margin-: 5px; margin-: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;" align="justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;Stakes Hall was situated on the south bank of the River Darwen, which wa
2 CONC s the northern boundary of the Livesey township. After the Astleys the Stakes Hall estate was purchased by the firm of Turner &amp;amp; Co. who built a print works on the site, who in turn sold it in 1843 to Joseph Eccles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</l
2 CONC ine><line>&lt;p style="color: #7959f7; font-family: 'times new roman'; font-size: medium; background-color: #f7f3ce; margin-: 5px; margin-: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;" align="justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;Th
2 CONC e Astley family were in the 16th &amp;amp; 17th century the chief resident proprietors in Witton, amongst them some who lived at Witton Old Hall. This Astley family were seated at Ewood &amp;amp; Stakes for over 3 centuries and are believed to hav
2 CONC e descended from the Astley family of Astley at Chorley, however there seems to be no record of how they obtained the estate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="color: #7959f7; font-family: 'times new roman'; font-size: medium; backgro
2 CONC und-color: #f7f3ce; margin-: 5px; margin-: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;" align="justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;George Astley son of William Astley married Jane Stanley the daughter James Stanley, Knight residin
2 CONC g at Cross Hall. They had four sons namely; Thomas, William, Gilbert &amp;amp; Richard (died 25th Feb 1635-36), and three daughters namely; Elizabeth, Rosamund, and Anne. In Georges will dated 24th August 1573. He left his house in Witton to his wi
2 CONC fe, and the Manor house of Livesey to his son Thomas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="color: #7959f7; font-family: 'times new roman'; font-size: medium; background-color: #f7f3ce; margin-: 5px; margin-: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;" a
2 CONC lign="justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;Thomas Astley (died Sept 3rd 1617) elder brother of Dr. Richard Astley married Mary Livesey (died July 1623) daughter of Richard Livesey of Fernehurst in 1574. Thomas &amp;
2 CONC amp; Mary had five sons and one daughter namely; Thomas, William, Randle, Richard, Edward and Millicent who married William Banester, B.A. Randle Astley (died Feb 1640-41) second son of Thomas was a yeoman farmer in Eccleshill, married Margery (die
2 CONC d Nov 1618) had three sons Thomas, George Astley of Witton and James Astley of Mellor, together with four daughters namely; Elizabeth, Alice, Margaret, and Millicent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="color: #7959f7; font-family: 'tim
2 CONC es new roman'; font-size: medium; background-color: #f7f3ce; margin-: 5px; margin-: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;" align="justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;Thomas (died 1623) the eldest son of Thomas and Mary, marri
2 CONC ed Ellen daughter of Thomas Osbaldeston, and had one son and seven daughters namely; Thomas (died 1663), Mary (born 1601), Margaret (baptised May 20th 1611), Elizabeth, Alice (wife of Thomas Snape of Balderston), Helen (wife of John Marsden of Blac
2 CONC kburn), Jane (wife of Roger&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Dewhurst&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;of Livesey), and Ann (wife of John Helme of Ribchester).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial; font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
