2 CONC lt;tr&gt;&lt;td valign="top"&gt;Death:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt;May 18,  1973&lt;br&gt;Vernal&lt;br&gt;Uintah County&lt;br&gt;Utah, USA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" valign="top"&gt;&lt;img src="ht
2 CONC tp://www.findagrave.com/icons2/trans.gif" alt="" width="3" height="13"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong style="width: 100%; text-align: center"&gt;LAST RITES HONOR FORMER UINTAH COUNTY COMMISSIONER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Curtis  was born Januar
2 CONC y 20, 1905 in Jensen to Joseph S. and Jemima Moon  Dudley, married Jessie Davis, March 27, 1930 at Duchesne.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was  Uintah County Commissioner for eight years, Director of the Uintah  County Water Conservancy District from 1956
2 CONC . President of the Jensen  water district; director of the Moon Lake Electric Association for 10  years; on the board of the New Life Training Center; director of the  Uintah AAA Foundation. While he was commissioner he worked to get the  antenna T
2 CONC . V. into the basin. He was a member of the LDS Church.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Survivors:  widow, sons, daughters, Charles, California; Mrs. Donald (Dorothy)  Martinsen, Mrs. Mac (Marian) Holmes, Mrs. Norma Rae Anderson, all of  Vernal; Mrs. Duane (Mau
2 CONC rine) Anderson, Denver; 11 grandchildren, 2  great-grandchildren, sisters, Mrs. Gerlad (Katherine) Ross, Murray  Davis, (Elta) Alder, Manti; Mrs. Earl (Veda) Hatch, Vernal.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Funeral services honored Curtis Duncan Dudley May 21 a
2 CONC t the Jensen Ward. Wade Slaugh officiated. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bishop  Mac Holmes offered prayer at the mortuary. May Ann Snow played the  prelude and postlude music. &amp;quot;Some Where My Love&amp;quot; was sung by Verdin  Goodrich and Norman Ha
2 CONC slem. Invocation offered by Bishop Ross Merrill.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bishop  Wade Slaugh presented short remarks of Mr. Dudleys service to the  community and life. Bishop Hyrum Slaugh presented short remarks of Mr.  Dudleys service to the communit
2 CONC y and life. Bishop Hyrum Slaugh and Vern  Wilkins were speakers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;quot;Beautiful Isle of Somewhere&amp;quot;  was sung by  Frank and Don Walker, Marva Lent and Lois Erickson, Lurae Caldwell and  Virginia Ewell sang &amp;quot;
2 CONC That Silver Haired Daddy of Mine.&amp;quot;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A. DeMar Dudley offered the benediction. Dedication of the grave was by Ray Nash.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pallbearers,  Jody Massey, Devier Dudley and Dennis Hatch, all nephews of the  decea
2 CONC sed, Ervin Wilkins, Blake Peterson and Richard Peterson. Honorary  pallbearers were the Moon Lake Directors, Uintah Water Conservancy  District directors, Uintah Basin Alcoholism Foundation Directors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interment was in the Maese
2 CONC r Cemetery. The Jensen Relief Society assisted with the flowers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Out-of-town  guests Mr. and Mrs. Duane Anderson and family, Denver; Mr. and Mrs.  Gerald Ross and daughter, Murray; Mr. and Mrs. Wes Robinson, Orem; Mr.  and Mrs. D
2 CONC ave Atler, Manti; Mr. and Mrs. George Massey, Mr. and Mrs.  Jerry Massey, Marge Allen, Springville; Mr. and Mrs. Jody Massey, Lehi;  Mr. and Mrs. Kilton Massey, Provo; Mr. and Mrs. Rulon Anderson. Orem.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kilton  Davis, Watsonville
2 CONC , California; Mr. and Mrs. Eilz Stewart, Provo; Mr.  and Mrs. Vern Wilkins, Brigham City; Reva Watkins, Salt Lake City; Donna  Jensen, West Jordan and other friends and relatives is the Roosevelt  and surrounding areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-Vernal E
