2 TITL Mass of Longmeanygate – 28th May 1977
1 _OID 5e57790c-5785-4531-9bc3-7943ae11b75a
1 DATE 28 May 1977
1 PLAC 222 Longmeanygate, Midge Hall, Leyland, Lancashire, England, United Kingdom
1 _DSCR Catholics join in forbidden Mass. Roman Catholics from all over the country were today celebrating the outlawed Tridentine Mass in a Leyland house. They were members of the St Pius V Association which hopes to bring back the traditional Latin Mas
2 CONC s dropped by the Church in favour of a modern version. The service was held in the house of a member in Longmeanygate. Fr Peter Morgan, from Newbury, stepped in at the last moment to officiate when the priest who was to have celebrated the Mass fel
2 CONC l ill. A spokesman for the group said they were determined to keep up their fight to re-introduce the traditional Latin Mass. "There are thousands of people all over the country who would like to get back to the old style of worship. They are unhap
2 CONC py with the present system where everyone is allowed to do as they wish. We will continue our fight to bring the Church back to the faith as we were always taught it," said the spokesman.
