2 TITL Oswald Airey 2nd marriage
1 _OID 5e8e8254-ff60-44c6-8585-d91acc8435de
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;The Dent records have a marriage of an Oswald Aiery and an Ann Jackson 6 August 1715 this Oswald could well be the son of Oswald b1675 but we consider it more likley to have been a second marriage. Firstly Oswal
2 CONC d was recently widowed his wife Margaret having died in 1714 (buried in Kirkby Lonsdale). Ann Jackson at 40 was of a similar age. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ann Jackson and her family appear to have been natives&amp;nbsp;of Dent whereas Oswald seems to hav
2 CONC e come from Low Biggins just south of Kirkby Lonsdale son Charles was born there.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Their first son Robert&amp;nbsp; had the same name as Ann Jacksons father a possible clue again as to a second marrige&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
