2 TITL John Airey 1766
1 _OID 5f6297a4-f998-498d-843e-f0d4b3604a23
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;From the baptism record of John b1798 his Father was a John Airey a cooper&amp;nbsp;from Sedbergh Yorkshire (now Cumbria) there is a record of his death (in Spring Lane South Shields) in 1835 at a recorded deat
2 CONC h of 71yrs.This would give a date of birth of 1764.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John b 1798 mother was Ann Mills, but a John Airey married an Ann Bates in 1794 the transcribed&amp;nbsp;records for their children record their Father John as a cooper from &amp
2 CONC ;quot;Barnsdale&amp;quot;these records are not&amp;nbsp;very clear.&amp;nbsp;We have assumed that this is our&amp;nbsp;John (the cooper link) and he&amp;nbsp;did marry twice. The record of Barnsdale is we consider&amp;nbsp;a transcription error fo
2 CONC r &amp;quot;Garsdale&amp;quot; a village in the parish of Sedbergh. Barnsdale is an area in South Yorkshire not a place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;the potential candidates for John Airey born c1764 from Sedbergh are&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John c 1762 Sedbergh s
2 CONC on of John and Dorothy Dawson&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John c 1766 Garsdale parish of Sedbergh son of Oswald and Elizabeth Harper&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John c 1768 Sedbergh son of Richard and Jane Holmes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John,Oswald and Richard wer
2 CONC e bothers sons of Charles Airey&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;a John c 1770 son of John and Ann Ratson has been discounted.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Of the three candidates none&amp;nbsp;have the 1764 birth date.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John c 1762 was christened January 1
2 CONC 7th and could have been born in the previous year. John and Dorothy lived in Briggflatts and were quakers that did not appear to follow on with John in South Shields&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;John c 1766 father Oswald&amp;nbsp;was a cooper as was his fathe
2 CONC r Charles. Again the dates are baptisms and with rural communities with no church births could be&amp;nbsp;much earlier.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is little information regarding John c 1768&amp;nbsp;or his father Richard he was the eldest and theref
2 CONC ore more likley to have remainedin the locality&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;On the basis of the above the best &amp;quot;fit&amp;quot; is John c 1766 son of Oswald irrespective the common ancestor is Charles&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&
2 CONC amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
