2 CONC ;strong&gt;4. Daniel McKay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Alfred Randal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Jerry Root&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7. Almerin Root&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt; John Calvert&lt;/stro
2 CONC ng&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. John C.Whittle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Wm Barnet [Barrett]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7.Phares Wells&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Elbridge Tufts Seargt 9
2 CONC th com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;John Calvert&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. [--] Phares Wells &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Sch[u]yler Jennings&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Thomas Chappall&lt;/strong&g
2 CONC t;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Thomas &amp;lt;Edward&amp;gt; P. Chappall&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Alfred D. Young&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7. Oliver Bess&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8. Isaac Furgerson [Ferguson]
2 CONC &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Benjamin F. Mitchell Seargt 10th company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;[--]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Elias Gardner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Walt
2 CONC er E[lias]. Gardner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. John W. Tuttle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. George Teeples&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Alvah Tippets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7. John H. Tippets&lt;/
2 CONC strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8. Hiram Tippets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thursday [June] 15th Passed the old &amp;amp; new Pawnee Missionary Station &amp;amp; camped on Cedar creek&amp;mdash;The Siox have burne
2 CONC d their new Missionary house that was built last summer! The Lord intends the Saints shall have a free passway through this region so he has removed our enemies this being the third time they have been burned out by the Sioux! To day Juhu [Jehu] Co
2 CONC x's Daughter [Lucretia Cox] 6 years old was killed by a Waggon running over it&amp;mdash;Camped near an old Indian Town in ruins&amp;mdash;A tremendous Storm of rain, thunder &amp;amp; lightning accompanied with wind &amp;amp; hail &amp;amp; but ou
2 CONC r encampment being formed[,] our cattle remained quietly within our Corell by close watching. A. Griffins company being on Guard&amp;mdash;a messengers arrived from Br Brigham's camp &amp;amp; informed that his company crossed over the Loup Fork ab
2 CONC out noon.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Friday 16th It rained the fore part of the day but we journeyed on to the ford of the Loup, &amp;amp; in the evening we had another tremendous Storm of wind &amp;amp; rain&amp;md
2 CONC ash;which was severe on our sick&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 17th All the Brethren that came on are encamped on the right bank of the river &amp;amp; they sent over about a hundred yoke of oxen t
2 CONC o assist us to move over &amp;amp; by the middle of the afternoon we had moved over 225 Waggons &amp;amp; several hundred head of [&lt;em&gt;illegible&lt;/em&gt;] cattle &amp;amp;c[,] Sheep &amp;amp;c herds without any accident&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p
2 CONC &gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunday 18th The Saints gathered midway beween the camps on the bank of the river for worship[.] Br Brigham opened the meeting by Prayer &amp;amp; then addressed the Saints on the object that should be constan
2 CONC tly kept in view on this journey[,] the building up of the Kingdom of God on the Earth, that an individual might believe mormonism to be true &amp;amp; be all his life in the midst of the Saints &amp;amp; be damned &amp;amp; go to hell at last beca
2 CONC use they did not keep &amp;amp; retain the influence of the Holy Ghost within their own breast to govern &amp;amp; rule the whole man&amp;mdash;Br Kimball &amp;amp; some others spoke when the President proposed the following order of march from her
2 CONC e. Br Snow's company first four Wagons abreast[,] Perkins &amp;amp; Pulsiphers forming one company next[,] his own next &amp;amp; Br Kimbals in the rear[.] which motion was carried when meeting was dismissed by E. Snow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</lin
2 CONC e><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday [June] 24th Encamped near the head of Grand Island&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunday 25th Remained encamped and were visited by Eight Soldiers from where they ar
2 CONC e building a fort 10 or 12 miles below here on the South side of Grand Island.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Friday 30th Killed the first Buffalo at the head of the Pawnee Swamps a few miles below the forks of the rive
2 CONC r&amp;mdash;This was a pell mell hunt, a small Band being started down the Swamps toward the river, came running up &amp;amp; dashed through our line &amp;amp; receiving showers of bullits &amp;amp; being pursued by men[,] women &amp;amp; children&
2 CONC amp;mdash;until most of the Buffalo were destroyed&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday first of July moved on 12 or 15 miles &amp;amp; camped on the river above the fork, 383&amp;frac12; miles from Winte
2 CONC r Quarters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunday 2nd remained encamped &amp;amp; attended meeting &amp;amp; received excellent instruction from President Young. In the evening our com[pany] was called together &amp;amp
2 CONC ; selected six hunters all others to abstain from Killing game&amp;mdash;There was also a reorganizing of the Guard by appointing a sufficient number of Seargents of the Guard with Elias Gardner captain which relieved me from the duties of that off
2 CONC ice on account of the sickness of my Son as I have to attend upon him every night&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Friday 7th Halted at camp creek &amp;amp; remained here two days &amp;amp; hunted Buffalo on Sa
2 CONC tturday &amp;amp; killed four or five&amp;mdash;Bro Brigham &amp;amp; Br Morley came back 17 miles on Sunday to visit our camp &amp;amp; gave information that some men had met their camp from the "Valley" who gave encourageing information concernin
2 CONC g the prospects for a crop there&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 15th Arrived in the vicinity of Chimney Rock late in the evening &amp;amp; encamped with Br Brighams camp about a mile from us&amp;mda
2 CONC sh;last Friday we met Br Roundy with 12 Teams from the Valley, he having left a number more at Ft John unable to come farther on account of lameness&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunday 16th Arrangements wer
2 CONC e made for dividing these two camps into 8 companys &amp;amp; also to send three men as an Express to the Valley for more Teams to meet us at Green river&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tuesday 18th Br Heber'
2 CONC s camps crossed over the Platte by fording about half way between Chimney Rock &amp;amp; Scot[t]s Bluffs while Br Brighams camp continued their rout[e] up the North side&amp;mdash;our camp now consi[s]ts of four Tens under Capt Her[r]iman&lt;/stron
2 CONC g&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Friday 21st encamped about 10 o clock near Racheau's camp 20 miles below Fort John&amp;mdash;Br Kimbal[l]s companys having encamped here last night&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&
2 CONC lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 22nd Br Kimbals company went on ahead but we hired Racheau's Blacksmith tools built a coal pit &amp;amp; made arrangements for Br Pugmire to do our Smith work here &amp;amp; we understand that Br Brighams company cro
2 CONC ss yesterday about 8 miles above here&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tuesday 25th We moved on after having set about [&lt;em&gt;illegible&lt;/em&gt;] Waggon tires passed Fort John&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</li
2 CONC ne><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wednesday 26th overtook some of Hebers company on Bitter Creek&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Friday 28th we remained here two days to receive our Teams &amp;amp; make tar&amp;mdash;The f
2 CONC eed in the Black Hills much scarser than it was last year&amp;mdash;made our way through them safely &amp;amp; camped on Deer creek 3 miles above the roads&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday the 5th day of Augus
2 CONC t remained here Sunday &amp;amp; were obliged to stop Monday on account of the sickness of Br Claytons wife who was delivered of a Daughter [Olive Diantha]&amp;mdash;Br Jesse Folks also had a Daughter [Frances] born Tuesday the first of August on t
2 CONC he La Bonte river in the Black Hills&amp;mdash;On Wednesday the 9th we overtook all of Br Kimbals companys about noon encamped on the Platte a few miles below the ford&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On Frida
2 CONC y the 11th &amp;lt;This morning Br Whittle Baptized Oliver in the Platte&amp;gt; crossed the river&amp;mdash;moved on to 12 mile creek &amp;amp; encamped in one corell with Br Kimbal[.] here our cattle began to get Poison either from some vegetabl
2 CONC e or mineral[.] I had one ox verry sick but he recovered&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sunday 13th moved on from the Willows Spring over in the Sweetwater Valley &amp;amp; camped on Grease&amp;mdash;Wood cre
2 CONC ek eight miles, N. East from the Independance Rock&amp;mdash;here my Son Oliver Bar Jacob died on Monday the 14th of August &amp;lt;(at 8 oclock A M)&amp;gt; after having suffered incredibly for above three months with Black Scurvy, Black canker &a
2 CONC mp;amp; liver complaint all of which he bore with great patience &amp;amp; resignation&amp;mdash;he was a good Boy and a verry promising Youth[.] Aged 14 years 7 months &amp;amp; 9 days&amp;mdash;We buried him on a small eminence near our camp &amp
2 CONC ;frac12; miles S. East of the road &amp;amp; marked the spot with a heap of rough Stones &amp;amp; a lettered Board&amp;mdash;here with services &amp;amp; mourning we left him to rest in the Wilderness&amp;mdash;(Having been worn out, a Martyr to t
2 CONC he cause of righteousness&amp;mdash;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 19th Being unwilling longer to travel in so large a company we remained encamped on the Sweet water while Br Kimbal's company went on xxxxxx
2 CONC x remained Sunday&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monday 21st moved on 8 miles leaving 7 waggons so many cattle having died &amp;amp; for several days we were obliged to halt occasionally &amp;amp; send back &amp;lt;our&
2 CONC amp;gt; Teams to bring up those whose teams were deficient the &amp;lt;cattle&amp;gt; dying every day until &lt;span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Sunday&lt;/span&gt; the 3rd day of Sept. Teams having arrived to our assistance from the Val
2 CONC ley etc &amp;amp; moved on over the South Pass&amp;mdash;&amp;amp; camped at the Pacific Springs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 9th encamped on Black's Fork having made 91 miles in 7 days!&amp;mdash;Sunday rem
2 CONC ained encamped&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 16th Encamped a mile below Riden's Cave on Echo creek &amp;amp; remained over Sunday&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Satturday 23rd Enc
2 CONC amped at the mouth of the Kanyon[.] in Valley everything appears much more fresh &amp;amp; green than last year. Their having been plenty of rain this season. Arrived in the Valley Sunday [September] 24th [1848]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line
2 CONC >&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
