1 _OID 663db65b-14ac-4cd6-a487-4b3db2154fbd
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The pretty market town of Garstang,&amp;nbsp;Wyre,&amp;nbsp;nestles at the foothills of scenic Bowland Fells, and as a regular winner of Britain in Bloom awards, its streets are lined with colourful f
2 CONC lower displays. Garstang&amp;rsquo;s existence is first detailed in the Doomsday Book and you can explore the area&amp;rsquo;s past with a visit to the ruins of Greenhalgh Castle, built by the 1st Earl of Derby in 1490. It sits proudly atop a hills
2 CONC ide above the town, offering fabulous views of the picturesque town and surrounding countryside. For a different perspective, take a day trip along Lancaster Canal, which runs through the centre of town on its way from Leeds to Lancaster. Garstan
2 CONC g is the perfect starting point for walking and cycling enthusiasts; it&amp;rsquo;s on the edge of the Forest of Bowland and is surrounded by unspoilt countryside and woodland. Garstang&amp;rsquo;s weekly Thursday Market has been going since 1310
2 CONC ! Both at the market and in town, local produce is sold alongside a much higher than average number of Fairtrade products. That&amp;rsquo;s because Garstang battled hard to become the world&amp;rsquo;s first Fairtrade Town, meaning that all local b
2 CONC usinesses and the local council have pledged to use and promote Fairtrade products when reasonably practicable. You can sample the great local produce and Fairtrade goods in Garstang&amp;rsquo;s many cafes and restaurants.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;
2 CONC div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;What&amp;#39;s On&amp;nbsp;in Garstang and Wyre&lt;p&gt;Visit the market town of Garstang any time of year an
2 CONC d you&amp;rsquo;ll probably happen upon a festival or celebration of some kind! Don&amp;rsquo;t miss the Children&amp;rsquo;s Festival in spring, or the Garstang Walking Festival which takes place 9-17 May 2009. In August choose to enjoy the Arts &
2 CONC amp;amp; Music Festival during the last week, or the traditional Agricultural Show. Stock up on all your Christmas goodies at the Garstang Victorian Christmas Festival, which takes place mid-December each year.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/
2 CONC div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
