2 TITL Article of the Katocation
1 _OID 68f968a6-5854-4978-8064-72914af7b672
1 DATE 9 Oct 1975
1 PLAC 222 Longmeanygate, Midge Hall, Leyland, Lancashire, England, United Kingdom
1 _DSCR In the mid-1970s, Irene Mary Taylor and Derrick Taylor transformed their kitchen and dining room into a chapel for the regular performance of the Traditional Latin Mass for Catholics across Lancashire and beyond. This article from the Lancashire Ev
2 CONC ening Post published Thursday 9th October 1975 details how Derrick Taylor's disillusionment by the reforms of the Second Vatican Council spared him on to continue with Latin Mass even if this meant turning his own home into a church. The article me
2 CONC ntions that these masses taking place at Longmeanygate were a regular occurrence during the mid-1970s and were performed by Father Peter Morgan, the first District Superior of the SSPX in Great Britain. In the context of Irenianism and the Causes f
2 CONC or Beatification of Irene Mary & Derrick Taylor, their action of turning of one's home into a chapel and the series of masses conducted inside Longmeanygate during this period are collectively referred to as the Katocation. This is part of their gr
2 CONC andson Cometan's theological terminology for Irene Mary and Derrick Taylor's activities.
