1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>Violet P Kearl  Salt Lake Tribune  June 2, 1974  Smithfield- Violet Pitcher Kearl, 83, of Smithfield died May 31, 1974 in a Salt Lake hospital of causes incident to age.  Born Sep 21, 1890 Smithfield, to William and Eliz
2 CONC abeth Thornley Pitcher.  Married George Robinson Kearl Jan. 15, 1908, Logan Temple.  He died May 4, 1962.  Member LDS Church; member Smithfield Farm Bureau.  Survivors: sons, daughters; Caltyon; Mrs. Sam (Gwen) Demmen: Mrs. Robert (Laurie) Monson
2 CONC ,  all Salt Lake City: Robert Payson; Cysril , Tremonton: Mrs. Mrs Wilda Taggart. Smithfield; Mrs. Rex (Phyllis) Elwood; Mrs. Ronald (Donna) Bergener, both Idaho Falls, Idaho; Mrs Gene (Beverly) Hansen, Ogden: 27 granchildren; 37 great-grandchildre
2 CONC n, brother, Leroy Smithfield.  Funeral Monday, 12 noon. Smithfield Third Ward. Friedns call Nelson Funeral Home in Smithfield Sunday 7-9 p.m. and Monday after 10 a.m. Burial Smithfield City Cemetery.  </line></content></metadataxml>
