1 DATE 1640
1 PLAC Mass Bay Colony
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;William Wellman (1624-1671) immigrated from England to America during the summe
2 CONC r of 1640. They sailed into Plymouth Harbor and settled at Green Harbor in Marshfield in Plymouth Colony. They stayed there for about a year. Reverend Richard Blinman was the spiritual leader of this group.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line
2 CONC ><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;In 1641 the Blinman party including William Wellman moved to Goucester in the Massachusetts Bay Colon
2 CONC y. William Wellman had Gloucester lots "in the Harbor" and in "Fishermoans Field". William Wellman was a seaman trading about the new country and he called Gloucester home for about 9 years. He married Elizabeth Spencer of Hartford, CT in 1649.&lt;
2 CONC /span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;In 1651 Reverend Blinman was to begin pastoring at the Pequot P
2 CONC lantation (soon New London) and William Wellman and his wife moved to New London at the same time. William Wellman was there for the first land division and received a homelot in 1651. He continued seafaring and trading. He became a Freeman in 165
2 CONC 8 in Connecticut.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;At some point William Wellman moved his fa
2 CONC mily and his homebase to Killingworth, CT. William Wellman's will was written there 14 March 1669. He left everything to his wife and to his children at her death. His will mentions that his daughters Mary and Martha are married and makes some othe
2 CONC r provisions for the children. Daughter Mary married Thomas Howard in 1667. &lt;strong&gt;Daughter Martha is not known to have married Clement Minor until 1673, so perhaps she had an earlier marriage, too.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&l
2 CONC t;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;William Wellman had accumulated a large number of debts "trading at sea". The Court rej
2 CONC ected his will and his estate went to satisfy his debts. It isn't known how much was left for his family.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;
2 CONC span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;Widow Elizabeth Spencer Wellman married second Jacob Joy in 1672 and they had 4 children at Killingworth, CT.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&l
2 CONC t;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&gt;Daughter Martha Wellman (1652-1681) married Clement Minor (1638-1700) as his second of three wives and they had 1 child, Phebe Minor (1679-1751) who mar
2 CONC ried John Stebbins (1666-1756) raised 7 children at Lyme, CT.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times new roman;"&g
2 CONC t;Sources: &lt;span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Descendants of Thomas Wellman&lt;/span&gt; by J. W. Wellman, 1918; &lt;span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;History of the Town of Gloucester&lt;/span&gt; by J. J. Babson, 1860; &lt;
2 CONC span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Genealogy and History of the Wellmans&lt;/span&gt; by J. Wellman, 1867; &lt;span style="text-decoration: underline;"&gt;Genealogical Notes&lt;/span&gt; by N. Goodwin, 1969; &lt;span style="text-decoration
2 CONC : underline;"&gt;Ancestors of Evelyn Wood Keeper&lt;/span&gt; by J. C. Frost, 1939&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
