1 DATE 2010
1 PLAC Orem, Utah, Utah
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div style="absolute;: -1999px;"&gt;Ruby Taylor Gourley 8/11/1920 ~ 5/22/2010 Together Again Memories After a valiant battle with health issues and one never to complain, Ruby Taylor Gourley left this mortal existenc
2 CONC e to pass on to a far better place. The angels held their arms open to greet her. One of those angels was her eternal companion.She was born in Colonial Juarez, Chihuahua, Mexico to Edwin Adolphin Taylor and Ruby Evadna Pierce. She was sixth of sev
2 CONC en children. She came to Utah to attend BYU where she met her true love, Rex Stanley Gourley. They were married on September 20, 1940 in the Mesa Arizona Temple. She has three children, Jimmy Rex Gourley (Robin), Carol Nielson (Carl), and Steven Le
2 CONC e Gourley (LeAnn). Ruby was much loved by her 16 grandchildren and 13 great-grandchildren. Her legacy will continue forever. She was a loved second-grade school teacher who taught at Central Elementary in Pleasant Grove, Utah and Lindon Elementar
2 CONC y in Lindon, Utah. She was very active in the church holding many callings from being ward librarian, counselor in the Primary, and Young Women's President, to name a few. She was a devoted wife, mother, grandmother, and great grandmother. She i
2 CONC s a bright light to her family. She is a woman full of charity, compassion, and forgiveness. She taught us hope. Ruby was preceded in death by her husband, Rex S. Gourley; her two brothers, Lamar Taylor and Edwin "Ike" Taylor; her three sisters, Co
2 CONC rilla Taylor, Fawn Taylor, and Ada McDonald; grandson, Tommy Rex Gourley; and great-grand daughter, Mercydez Haws. A cheerful, inspiring light in our hearts, you will be greatly missed. We know you are reunited with loved ones and we can't wait t
2 CONC o be with you again. We all love you, our sweet Mom, Grammie, Grandmother, Aunt Ruby. Funeral services for Ruby will be held Thursday May 27, 2010 at 11:00 a.m. in the Lehi North 23rd LDS Ward Chapel, 3200 North 600 East, Lehi, Utah. Friends may ca
2 CONC ll at the ward chapel Wednesday evening from 6:00-8:00 p.m. and Thursday morning from 10:00 -10:45 a.m. prior to services. Interment, Orem City Cemetery. Funeral Directors - Warenski Funeral Home of American Fork, Utah. &lt;/div&gt;</line></content
2 CONC ></metadataxml>
