2 CONC : 'times new roman'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: en-us; mso-fareast-language: en-us; mso-bidi-language: ar-sa;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 8.0pt; font-family: 'arial','sans-serif'; ms
2 CONC o-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman'; color: #333333; mso-ansi-language: en-us; mso-fareast-language: en-us; mso-bidi-language: ar-sa;"&gt;Roger sailed to America with his father and two sisters. His mother had been hidden by her brother unti
2 CONC l the ship sailed. She joined them in America three and a half years later. His father made a home for them in Heber City in a dirt-roofed cabin. His father and his sisters, as well as himself, were very good singers and they were often called on t
2 CONC o perform at gatherings. Roger continued to use his musical talents all his life. He played a bass viola. He provided music for choirs, dances, and programs. He was a music director for 30 years and taught many to sing and play the organ and cello
2 CONC . They were a healthy family as both parents and all eleven children lived into their eighties and nineties. Roger followed his father's vocation as a weaver of carpets and rugs. He also engaged in farming. He was called to serve a mission in Engla
2 CONC nd in 1894 . He was of medium build with sandy red hair. They lived in Heber all their lives, after coming to Utah . Children: John James , b. 1868 . Sarah Ann , b. 1869 . Roger , b. 1871 . Joseph , b. 1873 . William , b. 1876 . Thomas , b. 187
2 CONC 8 . Franklin , b. 1880 . David , b. 1882 . Alice , b. 1885 . Laverna , b. 1887 . Brigham , b. 1890 . Donna Bell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
