1 _DSCR SOURCES: City Bountiful; History of Fillmore, LDS Church Libery ref Millard Stake ward; Gems of Reminiscence, Vol XVII, Faith promoting series, compiled by George C Lambert, Salt Lake City 1889 page 109; Heart Throbs of the West. Greatgrandson Carv
2 CONC ell Smi
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;1810 born in Fletcher Twp, Franklin, Vermont&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Family moved to Madison Ohio On the shores of Lake Erie (family belonged to the Methodist Church in Madison, Lake, Ohio.)&lt;/p
2 CONC &gt;&lt;p&gt;1831 Heard the gospel by John Murdock in 1831, after arriving at Kirtland OHIO, he was baptised by William Smith the brother of the prophet&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;03 OCT 1833 Married 1st wife Madison, Lake, Ohio &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1836 21s
2 CONC t of May, he was confirmed in the Kirkland temple by David Whitmer who was one of the three witnesses of the Book of Mormon. He was administered to for an impediment of speech that was relieved. (taken from his own hand written history) baptized hi
2 CONC s wife, his father&amp;#39;s family and 30 other Methodist assoicates. Handwritten journal, Carvill Smith has the orginal I have a copy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ordained an Elder and taught the gosepl to his old neighbors and assoiciates. Ordained to th
2 CONC e lst quorum of Seventies on Feb 1836.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Went to Kirkland&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Went on a Mission to Ohio&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1838 Went to Far West Caldwaell County (July 1838. His farm was on the Grand River 30 miles from Adam-ondi-Aham.
2 CONC )&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Bought farm in Ramus IL, mobs burned him out and he moved to Nauvoo.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1846 Left Nauvoo with the Saints for the west&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1848 arrived in Salt Lake City. Sept 19, 1848 in Brigham Young&amp;#39;s 5t
2 CONC h company, he was a captian over 10 men. He was accompanied by his first wife Mary Flint, &amp;amp; his Parents. &amp;amp; Sibblings&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1848 arrived Sept one of the orginal settlers of Bountiful, Utah&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1850 called a
2 CONC s Bishop of North Kaynon Ward (now Bountiful, UT)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1850 established Parawan, UT Oct 1850;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1851Married Ann Mariah Bowen Nov 1851;Married 2nd wife because 1st wife too ill to go to new settlement &amp;amp; establish
2 CONC ed Pauvan Valley (Fillmore, UT), &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1854 established Call Fort, (north of Brigham City, Box Elder, UT monument is on the old state hwy before you get to Honeyville) fall 1854;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1856 established Carson Valley, (Sout
2 CONC h of Reno north of Carson City, NV) April 1856;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1857 rescued the Willie Handcart Company, Married 2 handcart surviors Margaretta Unwin Clark, &amp;amp; Emma Summers&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1858 when John Army came, He constructed fortif
2 CONC icaton in Echo Cayon. Guarded the homes&amp;#39;s in Bountiful &amp;amp; helped supply Conner&amp;#39;s men.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1860 frederal Census in Bountiful&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1861 Brother died married his widow Henrietta Caroline Williams Cal
2 CONC l moved her family from Filmore to Bear River, UT (northwest of Brigham City, UT)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1864 Callville, AZ (located just west and north of Hoover Dam. Location is now underwater but plaque &amp;amp; Marina are there.) Oct 1864 there wa
2 CONC s a warehouse and a town to ship things via the Colorado River.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1870 married last wife Ann Clark Census in Bountiful Utah Territory&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1872-1877 Bishop of East Bountiful Ward 1872-1877.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1874 Branc
2 CONC h of the United order formed there he was the President&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1877 He was called as councler in the Davis Stake Presidency till his death.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1880 CENSUS OF BOUNTIFUL&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1890 Death at home in Bountiful&lt;/
2 CONC p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
