2 TITL Hiram James Clayton
1 _OID 7f9c3cb5-a5bd-489f-9d1a-36f4eef94876
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;HIRAM JAMES CLAYTON.&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Well&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;spa
2 CONC n style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;known among the residents of Butte County in the vicinity of Chico and equally well liked by those who know him, Hiram James Clayton is among the old settlers and recalls many i
2 CONC nteresting episodes of the earlier days.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He wa
2 CONC s born, November 12, 1846, in Nebraska (at that time a territory), at a place called Winter Quarters,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;now&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font
2 CONC -size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;known as Florence, near Omaha.&amp;nbsp;He lost his father, James Clayton, at Winter Quarter, when but a child of six months.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-fa
2 CONC mily: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #ff0000;"&gt;His mother,&lt;span style="color: #000000;"&gt; in maidenhood&lt;/span&gt
2 CONC ; Lydia A. Moon&lt;/span&gt;, a native of England, came from that country to America when thirteen years of age, with her parents.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/sp
2 CONC an&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;After James Clayton&amp;rsquo;s death, his widow married &lt;span style="color: #ff0000;"&gt;Thomas L.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; f
2 CONC ont-family: 'times new roman', serif; color: #ff0000;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Munjar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;, and, in 1851, they crossed the plains to Salt Lake, where Hiram James Clayton wa
2 CONC s brought up on a ranch from a boy riding the range and learning to rope and brand cattle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt
2 CONC ; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;In those early days in the far West education advantages were not what they are now, and his education was necessarily limited.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'time
2 CONC s new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He recalls incidents of life in Utah at that early day, when the Indians gave the settlers much trouble, and describes th
2 CONC e town of Tooele, in those days having an adobe wall fifteen feet high with a bastion on each corner, surrounding the town, as a protection from the Indians, but the wall is now all cleared away.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.
2 CONC 5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;In 1861 the family moved to Butte County, Cal., with ox teams, going in the large train known as&lt
2 CONC ;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Dyers&amp;rsquo;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;train, for protection from the I
2 CONC ndians.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;They were three months in Nevada and th
2 CONC ence came on to California.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;The parents locate
2 CONC d on a farm east of Shasta Road, remaining there until they died.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Hiram James Clayton, remained at home, helping on the ra
2 CONC nch and working at milling on Rock Creek, until his marriage, January 17, 1875, to Miss Melissa&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Roney&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt
2 CONC ; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;, who was born near Napa, Cal., and was a daughter of John&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Roney&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size
2 CONC : 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;, a native Missourian, who, at the age of seventeen, crossed the plains with ox team in the year 1849, and who, after a few years returned to Missouri, afterwards returning to the Pacific slope w
2 CONC ith Dr. Hugh Glenn.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He farmed for a few years
2 CONC , then went to Yolo and Solano Counties, and then located in 1872 at Pine Creek, Butte County, where he farmed, later going to Rock Creek, where he resided until his death at the age of sixty-two.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13
2 CONC .5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He was married after he came to California, to Mary True, who was born in Indiana, and who crosse
2 CONC d the plains with her parents at the age of fifteen.&amp;nbsp;She died in Butte County, ten years ago.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-s
2 CONC ize: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Of their eight children, six are living, of whom Mrs. Hiram J Clayton is the oldest.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nb
2 CONC sp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;She was reared in California.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&
2 CONC lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Mr. and Mrs. Clayton are the parents of six children, five of whom grew up, namely:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman'
2 CONC , serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Ida Belle, now Mrs. Charles L. Crowder, of Chico;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif
2 CONC ;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Gue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;E., a graduate of Stockton Business College, now a salesman for Gage and Company, handling the Ford cars; Minnie, a graduate o
2 CONC f Stockton Business College, who afterward became Mrs. Allen and who died in 1915; Clara, a graduate of Chico Business College, now Mrs. Coon, of Durham; Leo, a graduate of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roma
2 CONC n', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Heald&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Business College of San Francisco, now auto engineer with the Chico Steam Laundry.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><li
2 CONC ne>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/sp
2 CONC an&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;After his marriage Mr. Clayton ran the old Keefer flour mill on Rock Creek for five years.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'ti
2 CONC mes new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;In 1880, he began farming, preempting one hundred sixty acres, twelve miles north of Chico, and homesteading another on
2 CONC e hundred sixty acres; he also bought two hundred forty acres of railroad land, owning altogether five hundred sixty acres.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&
2 CONC lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He put the first plow into this land, and improved, fenced, cross-fenced it, and built a residence and barns, and raised grain and stock of all kinds; he also leased lan
2 CONC d for grain-raising, putting in large crops.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;H
2 CONC e continued harvesting his own and other people&amp;rsquo;s grain for twenty-eight summers, harvesting as many as nineteen hundred acres in a year, with a combined harvester.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'ti
2 CONC mes new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;In 1910 he sold the ranch, and then bought and moved onto his present place of ten acres, which he improved, setting ou
2 CONC t prune and peach orchards, building a residence and making other improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-famil
2 CONC y: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He was school trustee, for fifteen years, and part of the time clerk of Antelope School District.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;
2 CONC "&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;M
2 CONC r. Clayton as a young man was one of six men who, after the Indian massacre on Rock Creek, went to Rock Creek Canyon and hunted till they found the bodies of the two Hickok girls who were killed by the Indians.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=
2 CONC "font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;In 1911, Mr. and Mrs. Clayton made a trip to his old home in Salt Lake.&amp;nbsp;&lt
2 CONC ;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;He noted many changes, the country where he once herded cat
2 CONC tle being now under a high state of cultivation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-s
2 CONC ize: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;
2 CONC strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Transcribed by Sharon&amp;nbsp;Walford&amp;nbsp;Yost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt
2 CONC ; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman'; color: #333333;"&gt;Source: "History of Butte County, Cal.," by George C. Mansfield,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; m
2 CONC so-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman'; color: #333333;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman'
2 CONC , serif;"&gt;Pages 1161-1163&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; mso-fareast-font-family: 'times new roman'; color: #333333;"&gt;, Historic Record Co, Los Angeles, CA
2 CONC , 1918.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;div style="text-align: center;" align="center"&gt;&lt;hr align="center" size="2"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-fami
2 CONC ly: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;copy; 2009&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;stron
2 CONC g&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Sharon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;Walford&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'times new roman', serif;"&gt;Yost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&l
2 CONC t;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~npmelton/btclay.htm&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
