1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Robert Moon&amp;rsquo;s will is dated 29 June, 1766. He gav
2 CONC e the following legacies: to Mary Cooper, the late James Brandwood&amp;rsquo;s daughter, &amp;pound;10; to be used for buying her meal every year whilst the money should last. To his nephew, John Brandwood, &amp;pound;20, on condition he paid off t
2 CONC he money that he, Robert Moon, stood bound with him, the same to be settled at Candlemass next, other&amp;shy; wise the same &amp;pound;20 to go to his brother, James Brand&amp;shy; wood. To his sister, Agnes Brandwood (Moon), &amp;pound;20. To hi
2 CONC s niece, Isabel Bwe, &amp;pound;5; and William Bwe, her husband, 15. if demanded. To his brother&amp;mdash;in-law, John Arkwright, 15. if demanded; Richard Arkwright, his&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;nephew &amp;pou
2 CONC nd;20, including that which he owes him by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;virtue of his father&amp;rsquo;s will (John Moon, 1768), when he attained 21 years; To John Wareing, who married his niece Ann, &amp;pound;5; to his mot
2 CONC her &amp;pound;8 to be added to &amp;pound;7 his father left her, paid quarterly for life; (she was Isabel Worsick of Salwick); Robert Adamson, &amp;pound;30; Alexander Worsick &amp;lsquo;one guinea; John Bell his watch; to his nephew Robert Moon o
2 CONC f Liverpool, if alive, &amp;pound;8; the estate called Whinneyfield house he left to Robert Moon his&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;nephew, and James Brandwood, equally between&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="fo
2 CONC nt-family: times;"&gt;them, but if Robert Moon was dead, his share to go&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;equally amongst all his nephews and nieces. He de&amp;shy;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;si
2 CONC red James Brandwood to pay his brother John &amp;pound;20,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;when his mother (Agnes Moon) died. The residue he&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;requested Rober
2 CONC t Adamson to give to his poor relations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;as he considered proper. He and John Bell were appoin&amp;shy; ted executors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><
2 CONC line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
