1 _OID 841ab93f-d1f5-4f9e-9e2d-ca9b364ce528
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;HISTORY:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1810 born in Fletcher Twp, Franklin, Vermont&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Family move
2 CONC d to Madison Ohio On the shores of Lake Erie (family belonged to the Methodist Church in Madison, Lake, Ohio.)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1831 Heard the gospel by John Murdock in 1831, after arriving at Kirtland OHIO, he wa
2 CONC s baptised by William Smith the brother of the prophet&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;03 OCT 1833 Married 1st wife Madison, Lake, Ohio &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1836 21st of May, he was confirmed in t
2 CONC he Kirkland temple by David Whitmer who was one of the three witnesses of the Book of Mormon. He was administered to for an impediment of speech that was relieved. (taken from his own hand written history) baptized his wife, his father&amp;#39;s fa
2 CONC mily and 30 other Methodist assoicates. Handwritten journal, Carvill Smith has the orginal I have a copy.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Ordained an Elder and taught the gosepl to his old neighbors and assoiciates. Ordained t
2 CONC o the lst quorum of Seventies on Feb 1836.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Went to Kirkland&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Went on a Mission to Ohio&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1838 W
2 CONC ent to Far West Caldwaell County (July 1838. His farm was on the Grand River 30 miles from Adam-ondi-Aham.)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Bought farm in Ramus IL, mobs burned him out and he moved to Nauvoo.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&
2 CONC gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1846 Left Nauvoo with the Saints for the west&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1848 arrived in Salt Lake City. Sept 19, 1848 in Brigham Young&amp;#39;s 5th company, he was a captian over 10 men. H
2 CONC e was accompanied by his first wife Mary Flint, &amp;amp; his Parents. &amp;amp; Sibblings&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1848 arrived Sept one of the orginal settlers of Bountiful, Utah&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;fon
2 CONC t size="2"&gt;1850 called as Bishop of North Kaynon Ward (now Bountiful, UT)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1850 established Parawan, UT Oct 1850;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1851Married Ann Mariah Bowe
2 CONC n Nov 1851;Married 2nd wife because 1st wife too ill to go to new settlement &amp;amp; established Pauvan Valley (Fillmore, UT), &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1854 established Call Fort, (north of Brigham City, Box Elder, U
2 CONC T monument is on the old state hwy before you get to Honeyville) fall 1854;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1856 established Carson Valley, (South of Reno north of Carson City, NV) April 1856;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;
2 CONC font size="2"&gt;1857 rescued the Willie Handcart Company, Married 2 handcart surviors Margaretta Unwin Clark, &amp;amp; Emma Summers&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1858 when John Army came, He constructed fortificaton in Ech
2 CONC o Cayon. Guarded the homes&amp;#39;s in Bountiful &amp;amp; helped supply Conner&amp;#39;s men.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1860 frederal Census in Bountiful&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1861 Brother d
2 CONC ied married his widow Henrietta Caroline Williams Call moved her family from Filmore to Bear River, UT (northwest of Brigham City, UT)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1864 Callville, AZ (located just west and north of Hoover Dam
2 CONC . Location is now underwater but plaque &amp;amp; Marina are there.) Oct 1864 there was a warehouse and a town to ship things via the Colorado River.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1870 married last wife Ann Clark Census in Bou
2 CONC ntiful Utah Territory&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1872-1877 Bishop of East Bountiful Ward 1872-1877.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1874 Branch of the United order formed there he was the President&lt;/f
2 CONC ont&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1877 He was called as councler in the Davis Stake Presidency till his death.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;1880 CENSUS OF BOUNTIFUL&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2
2 CONC "&gt;1890 Death at home in Bountiful&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;BIOGRAPHY: MARRIAGE 1ST 6 children&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;MARRIAGE 2ND 6 children&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"
2 CONC &gt;MARRIAGE 3RD 6 children&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;MARRIAGE 4TH 5 CHILDREN&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;MARRIAGE 5TH No children&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;MARRIAGE 6TH N
2 CONC o children&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Conquerors of the West: Stalwart Mormon Pioneers, volume 1 &lt;br&gt;Name: Anson Call &lt;br&gt;Birth Date: 13 May 1810 &lt;br&gt;Birth Place: Fletcher, Franklin, Vermont &lt;br&gt;Pare
2 CONC nts: Cyril and Sally Tiffany Call &lt;br&gt;Death Date: 31 Aug 1890 &lt;br&gt;Death Place: Bountiful, Davis, Utah &lt;br&gt;Arrival: 19 Sep 1848, Brigham Young Co. &lt;br&gt;Spouse: Mary Flint &lt;br&gt;Marriage Date: 03 Oct 1833 &lt;br&gt;Marriag
2 CONC e Place: Madison, Lake, Ohio &lt;br&gt;Spouse&amp;#39;s Parents: Rufus and Hannah Haws Flint &lt;br&gt;Spouse&amp;#39;s Birth Date: 27 Mar 1812 &lt;br&gt;Spouse&amp;#39;s Birth Place: Braintree, Orange, Vermont &lt;br&gt;Spouse&amp;#39;s Death Date
2 CONC : 08 Oct 1901 &lt;br&gt;Spouse&amp;#39;s Death Place: Bountiful, Davis, Utah &lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Married 2nd: Anna Maria Bowen Date: 15 Apr 1851 , Utah Born: 3 Jan 1834 , New York Died: 26 Jul 1924 , Uta
2 CONC h &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Married 3rd: Margaretta Unwin Clark Date: 7 Feb 1857 , Utah Born: 28 May 1828 , England Died: 12 Dec 1908 , Utah&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Married 4th: Emm
2 CONC a Summers Date: 24 Feb 1857 , Utah Born: 5 Aug 1828 , England Died: 22 Sep 1912 , Utah &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Married 5th: Henrietta Caroline Williams Date: 9 Apr 1861 , Utah Born: 26 Sep 1826 , New York &lt;/font&gt;&
2 CONC lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Married 6th: Ann Clark (Waldrus) Date: 24 Jan 1870 , Utah Born: 26 Sep 1826 , New York &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="2"&gt;Died:&amp;nbsp; After the martyrdom of the Prophet, Anson was calle
2 CONC d to assist Sheriff Backenstoes in helping prevent the mob from committing outrages against the saints. He was bishop in three wards in Bountiful, Utah, from 1849-1851, 1874-77. In 1851 he was called to help settle Parowan, Utah, and was Justice o
2 CONC f Peace there. He was appointed Probate Judge of Millard County and Utah territory Legislator. Brigham Young called him to help settle Fillmore and Anson was a postmaster and Deputy Marshall while there. He was then called to help settle Carson Val
2 CONC ley, Nevada. With his sons, he took part in the Echo Canyon during the Utah War with Johnson Army. He founded Calls Fort in Box Elder County, Utah. He was a counselor to President William R. Smith at the organization of Davis Stake. He was an adjut
2 CONC ant general&amp;nbsp;in the Silver Grays (Mountain Sharps) and helped in the rescue of the Martin Handcart Company. He was a successful merchant and farmer and helped with the construction of the railroad. He was a loyal member of the church. Child
2 CONC ren of 1st wife: Anson Vasco, b. 9 Jul 1834. Md. 1st, 28 Jan 1853, Charlotte Holbrook. Md. 2nd 10 Nov 1856, Eliza Catherine Kent. d. 4 Aug 1867. Mary Vashta, b. 27 Mar 1836. Md. 10 Apr 1853, Ira Curtis Parke. d. 11 Aug 1920. Cyril Moroni, b. 6 Fe
2 CONC b 1838. d. 9 Jul 1846. Chester, (twin), b. 13 May 1841. Md. 1st, 12 Jan 1860, Agnes Melissa Loveland. Md. 2nd, 6 Jul 1869, Mary Angeline Packer. Md. 3rd, 9 Dec 1872, Sarah Maria Dickson. Md. 4th, 16 Jun 1886, Pamela Elizabeth Barlow. d. 26 Jan 1908
2 CONC . Christopher, (twin), b 13 May 1841. d. 13 May 1841. Child. Hyrum, b. 14 Nov 1845. d. 15 Jun 1846. Child. Ruth Piede , b. abt 13 May 1849. md 25 Dec 1864, James Henry Davids. d. 19 Sep 1919. (Bought from the Indians in Fillmore, Utah. Children o
2 CONC f 2nd wife: Vilate, b. 27 Jul 1852. d. 10 Jun 1862. Israel, b 2 Jul 1854, Md. 1st, 21 Dec 1874, Medora White. Md. 2nd, 11 Jun 1880, Jane Lucinda Judd (Knight). d 23 Nov 1938. Children Vententia, b. 14 Feb 1856. d 19 Apr 1862 . Child. Viola, b. 16 J
2 CONC un 1858. Md 6 Nov 1879, James George. d. 2 Oct 1929. Anson Bowen, b. 20 Oct 1863. Md. 1st, 4 Nov 1885, Mary Theresa Thompson. Md. 2nd, 13 Dec 1890, Harriet Casier. Md. 3rd, 11 Mar 1898, Dora Pratt. Md. 4th, 21 Jan 1903, Julia Sarah Abegg. d. 2 Ja
2 CONC n 1958. Harriet Louisa, b. 8 Apr 1856. Md. 9 Sep 1885, William Charles Mann. d. 16 Nov 1932. Children of 3rd wife: Mary, b. 24 May 1858. Md 28 Jan 1874, Thomas Waddoups. d. 4 Dec 1916. Cylista, b. 4 Apr 1860. Md. 19 Oct 1876, Mark Waddoups. d. 3 Ju
2 CONC l 1907. Samantha Eveline, b. 25 Nov 1861. Md. 4 Mar 1880, William Charles Mann. d. 28 Apr 1848. Cynthia, b. 20 Feb 1864. Md. 16 Dec 1880, Thomas Waddoups. d. 8 Jan 1946. Willard, b. 25 Apr 1866. Md. 1st, 19 Apr 1886, Adelaide White. Md. 2nd Leah Pr
2 CONC att. d. 18 Jun 1945. Aaron, b. 3 Jul 1868. Md. 24 Sep 1890, Samantha A. Willey. Children of 4th wife: Ann, b. 22 Mar 1858. Md. 24 Jan 1876, Keplar Sessions. d. 8 Oct 1926. Fanny, b. 11 Aug 1860. Md. 28 Nov 1878, Truman Heap Barlow. d. 30 May 1916
2 CONC . Lucina, b. 8 Apr 1863. Md. 13 Apr 1882, Jasper Newton Perkins. D. 23 Jul 1957. David, b. 20 Jun 1868. Md. 2 Dec 1891, Eliza Dittmore. d. 16 Sep 1943 . Sarah, b. 8 Dec 1870. Md. 30 Jun 1887, Truman Heap Barlow. d 7 May 1944 . Submitted by: Junit
