2 TITL Sgt. Josiah Higley: An Industrious Person
1 _OID 850d4872-624f-4913-850f-ba6e860d577b
1 PLAC Simsbury, Connecticut
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Josiah lived, as far as it is known, little beyond Winsor and Simsbury. He was known to be an honorable person,&amp;quot;a good citizen, a worthy son of a worthy father.&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;He&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC was known to have served upon important town committees although not a leader in public affairs.&amp;nbsp; His father, Captain John Higley, a pillar of the community, died when Josiah was only thirteen.&amp;nbsp; At the age of 14, he chose in cour
2 CONC t to&amp;nbsp;Thomas Moore of Windsor to be his guardian.&amp;nbsp; At the age of 23, on new year&amp;#39;s eve, he married Dinah Gillett (Gillette).&amp;nbsp; She was from a family of excellent standing,&amp;nbsp;the Gillett&amp;#39;s being amon
2 CONC g the first grantees of land in Simsbury.&amp;nbsp; The couple settled in the parish of Turkey Hills, then a part of Simsbury (now&amp;nbsp;East Granby.)&amp;nbsp; There they lived having many children and granchildren.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;During hi
2 CONC s life, Josiah was employed doing &amp;quot;Surveying of the Highways&amp;quot;.&amp;nbsp; He was instrumental in the formation of the ecclesiastical parish known as North Society. (More will be added later)&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
