1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td valign="top"&gt;Birth:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt;Nov. 3,  1873&lt;br&gt;Spanish Fork&lt;br&gt;Utah County&lt;br&gt;Utah, USA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;
2 CONC td valign="top"&gt;Death:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt;Jan. 21,  1943&lt;br&gt;Salt Lake City&lt;br&gt;Salt Lake County&lt;br&gt;Utah, USA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" valign="top"&gt;&lt;img src="htt
2 CONC p://www.findagrave.com/icons2/trans.gif" alt="" width="3" height="13"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Funeral Services Held at Lapoint for Mrs. Rasmussen.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;LAPOINT  (Special) -- Funeral services were held Monday at 1:0
2 CONC 0 p.m. at the  Lapoint Chapel for Mrs. Sarah Ann Dudley Rasmussen under the direction  of Bishop Harvey Hullinger. The opening selection by the Lapoint choir  was &amp;quot;Softly Tenderly.&amp;quot; Invocation was offered by Verdin R. Johnson. Re
2 CONC x  and Cynthia Taylor favored us with a duet, &amp;quot;When It&amp;#39;s Lighting Time in  the Valley.&amp;quot;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The speakers were J. C. Hacking and Archie Johnson.  Orloa Reynolds played a piano solo. Our Own Red, White and Blu
2 CONC e in honor  of Mrs. Rasmussen&amp;#39;s son, Lloyd, who is now overseas with the U.S.  Marines. Bishop Hullinger gave closing remarks and the closing  selection, &amp;quot;Sweet Hour of Prayer,&amp;quot; was by the choir. Benediction was by  Warre
2 CONC n Billings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interment was at the Vernal Memorial Park under the direction of the Swain Funeral &amp;#39;Home.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mrs.  Rasmussen was born November 3, 1871 in Spanish Fork, the daugther of  Andrew and Mary Markha
2 CONC m Dudley. She was married to Ephraim Rasmussen  December 31, 1891 at Jensen. The couple moved to Lapoint in 1907,  residing here until 1938 when they moved to Salt Lake City to make their  home with their daughter, Mrs. Mary Sessions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;
2 CONC br&gt;Both Mr. and Mrs. Rasmussen were active in LDS church work. Mr. Rasmussen preceded his wife in death October 25, 1942.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Besides  her daughter, Mrs. Sessions, Mrs. Rasmussen is survived by four sons,  Grand and Thurmer Rasmus
2 CONC sen of Lapoint, Ollie Rasmussen of Roosevelt and  Louis Lloyd Rasmussen of the U. S. Marines; eleven grandchildren; five  brothers, Andrew , Joseph and Sanford Dudley of Jensen, and Steven and  Osmar Dudley of Canada; and three sisters, Mrs. Guylet
2 CONC ta Campbell and  Mrs. Julina Butcher of Vernal, and Mrs. Parney Witherall of Kansas City,  Kansas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Those attending the service from distant points  were   Andrew Dudley, Mr. and Mrs. Joseph Dudley, Mary Ellen Wilkins, Mr. and  Mr
2 CONC s. Jesse Butcher, A. DeMar Dudley, George E. Wilkins, Mr. and Mrs.  Harland Wilkins, Orvil Dudley, Mr. and Mrs. Thomas Hall, Mr. and Mrs.  William Ashby, Mr. and Mrs. Wells Ashby, Mr. and Mrs. Warren Billings,  Mrs. Sam Hatch, Mr. and Mrs. L. H. Wo
2 CONC odard, Verdin R. Johnson, Archie  Johnson,  Ernest   M. Johnson, Mrs. Effie Powell, Mrs. A. T. Johnson,  Mrs. J. W. Bastian, Mrs. Eleanor Chew and Dean Bigelow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-Vernal Express, January 28, 1943, transcribed by Rhonda Holton&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Family links:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;Parents:&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;amp;GRid=23053001" class="NoUnderline12point"&gt;Andrew Dudley (184
2 CONC 4 - 1925)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;amp;GRid=23053019" class="NoUnderline12point"&gt;Mary Lucy &lt;em&gt;Markham&lt;/em&gt; Dudley (1853 - 1903)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;n
