1 _OID 89bd1bc8-6c71-40f1-828b-2ac9fa1a4bc7
1 DATE 26 May 1911
1 _DSCR JOHN JOHNSON THAYN PASSES  Another of the pioneers has passed in the person of John Johnson Thayn, who died at the home of his son, E. H. Thayn, at Wellington on Saturday afternoon last at the advanced age of 85 years.  Deceased was born at Paisle
2 CONC y (Scotland) in the year 1824, coming to the United States an infant in arms.  He is survived by seven daughters and seven sons, besides numerous relatives throught the state.  The remains were interred at Wellington last Tuesday, the funeral bein
2 CONC g one of the very largest ever held there and showing the esteem in which he was held by the entire community.  Location: Eastern Utah Advocate 1910-05-26
