2 TITL Obituary for Veda Dudley Hatch
1 _OID 8ad04675-c00b-42cb-bd5b-30bb7a8932ac
1 DATE 27 Jun 2004
1 PLAC Deseret News
1 _DSCR Obituary for Veda Dudley Hatch
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Veda Dudley Hatch passed away on June 24, 2004 following a long illness.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;She was born in Jensen, Utah on January 26
2 CONC , 1923 to Joseph S. and Jemimah Moon Dudley. Veda spent her early life on the family farm in Jensen. She married Earl E. Hatch June 27, 1941. They had four children including, Aloma, Dennis, Annette and Shanna.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;fo
2 CONC nt size="4"&gt;Veda had countless energy and was recognized in the community for her beautiful flower and vegetable gardens. She served a LDS Ute Indian Mission in Randlett, Utah. She was also called to do work in the Provo and Vernal Temples. Sh
2 CONC e held numerous positions in her church. In her later years, &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Veda discovered a talent for oil painting. She created many beautiful and prized paintings of the local area. Veda loved to laugh an
2 CONC d always enjoyed a funny joke. At age 70 she was active in a clogging group that entertained the community.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Veda is survived by Aloma (Al) Rios, Dennis (Jan) Hatch, Annette and Shanna (Adam) Angel
2 CONC . She had 13 grandchildren and 21 great grand- children. A Heavenly welcoming committee will include her parents, sisters and brothers, Merle, Joseph, Curtis, Katherine, Mary, Orvil and Elta. Along with her husband, Earl and granddaughter Allissa W
2 CONC ignall.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;The family would like to thank Applegate Hospice, Betty, Charlotte, Ashlie and Myra who took incredible care of our mother.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Services wil
2 CONC l be held in the Naples 2nd Ward LDS Chapel, on Monday, June 28, 2004 at 2:00 p.m. Family and friends may call from 7:00-9:00 on Sunday, June 27, 2004 at the Thomson-Blackburn Vernal Mortuary, and also one hour prior to the services at the chapel i
2 CONC n Vernal, Utah. Burial will be at the Vernal Memorial Park under the direction of Thomson-Blackburn Vernal Mortuary.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;-Deseret News, June 27, 2004&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></conten
2 CONC t></metadataxml>
