2 TITL Alice Moon&#39;s Will
1 _OID 8c746603-015c-4bfb-b220-592af26f9416
1 DATE 16 Jun 1666
1 PLAC Whinneyfield House, Woodplumpton, Lancashire, Kingdom of England
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Alice Moon's will 16 Iune, 1666 provides a number of family linkages. She is described as Alice Moon of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="
2 CONC font-family: times;"&gt;Catforth within Woodplumnton, sninster, and desired to be buried in the church of Woodplumpton. She gave &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;to Richard, her brother, all the money which &amp;ldquo;is mean &l
2 CONC t;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;and undivided between him and mee". To the two&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;youngest children of her uncle, John Charnley, each &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-fa
2 CONC mily: times;"&gt;205.; to Robert, Ann and Richard Charnley, children of the said lohn each 5s.: to Robert Kellet, son of William&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Kellet, her godson, 30s.; to be put at interest until h
2 CONC e is 21 years old: to Ann Kellet, daughter of William. her chest; to Priscilla Brewer, widow, all she owes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;testator, but stipulated that she bought John loley a waistecoate out of the same; to he
2 CONC r sister Elizabeth &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Kellet all her linen and woollen apparel; to the wife of Thomas Eccleston, Ann Willisey and Thomas Newsham&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;sp
2 CONC an style="font-family: times;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;the younger, each 12 pence; to Elizabeth Charnley 25.; to Margaret Barton, Alice Hudson the elder, Elline Leach, widow, and Margaret Kerbie, each 25.
2 CONC ; All the residue of her goods, cattle and chattels were to be divided, one third to her brother Robert (of Whinney~ Held) and his children, one third to William Kellet, her brother&amp;mdash;in&amp;mdash;lawand his children, begotten of his wife E
2 CONC lizabeth (testator&amp;rsquo;s sister), and one third to her brother Richard Moon; Robert Moon, her brother and William&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Kellet, brother&amp;mdash;in&amp;mdash;law, to be executors. The w
2 CONC ill is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;signed by a mark and witnessed by Richard Moon and Edmund Billington, who both sign.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><li
2 CONC ne>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;The uncle ]ohn Charnley named in this will is probably the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Charnley who married G
2 CONC race Moon the daughter of Alice Moon's&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;uncle, ]ohn Moon, senior, of Hollowforth, and named in the latter&amp;rsquo;s will. They were married at Woodplumflon 13 April, 1642. Grace &lt;/sp
2 CONC an&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;was baptized 21 Oct., 1612&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
