1 _OID 8d4f1eef-0f39-4456-823c-b9e103163127
1 DATE 27 Dec 1941
1 _DSCR Obituary of Eliza Catherine Thayn Jones                                                                   GRIM REAPER OF EMERY COUNTY CALLS PIONEER    Castle Dale - Mrs. Eliza Catherine Thayn Jones, 83, Castle Dale Pioneer, died Friday at her hom
2 CONC e in this city. Mrs. Jones suffered a fall on December 113, which owing to her advanced age, indirectly caused her death. She was born July 28, 1858 at Lynn County, Iowa a daughter of John Johnson and Sidney Bower Thayn. She was married to Elisha A
2 CONC llen Jones, June 9, 1875. They resided at Woodland for nine years then moved to Castle Valley. Surviving are a daughter and six sons; Mrs.    Ida Wall, Elisha Allen, John Edward, Lindley Elmer, Marvin Leroy, Wallace Raymond and Arthur Herbert Jone
2 CONC s all of Castle Dale. Three brothers, Alvin and Edwin Thayn, Wellington, and Edgar Thayn of Salt Lake City. 45 grandchildren and 41 great grandchildren. Funeral services were held Monday conducted by EA. Nelson. The opening song was offered by th
2 CONC e ward quartet and the opening prayer by Hans Wickman. A vocal duet by Mrs. Merle Johansen and Mrs. Erma Lowry. First speaker was Seth Allen, vocal solo by Nola Jones Stilson, second speaker Louis P. Oveson, quartet number, closing prayer by Leo Pe
2 CONC tersen. The grave was dedicated by Carl Bott. Burial was directed by Wallace Mortuary.
