1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;span style="min-width: 200px; display: inline-block; width: 615px"&gt;Pauline E. Lahuta, 94, of Northampton, PA, died Saturday, May 7, 2011, at Lehigh Valley Hospital - Muhlenberg Campus in Bethlehem, PA. Pauline wa
2 CONC s the wife of the late Walter Lahuta who died in 1983. Born in Whitehall- Cementon, PA, she was the daughter of the late John and Veronica (Bankos) Cesanek. Pauline was a member of the Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary R.C. Church, Northampton
2 CONC , PA. She was former member of the Traveler Protection Agency- (T.P.A.)Ladies Auxiliary Post L, Allentown, PA; and a former member of the Northampton Business Professional Womens (B.P.W.) Club, Northampton, PA. &lt;strong&gt;Survivors:&lt;/strong&g
2 CONC t; She is survived by her daughter, Patricia wife of Joseph Polakovich of Allentown, PA; five grandchildren, Regina wife of Chris Lilly, Paula Polakovich, Alicia wife of Sean Deppe, Krista Kresh and fiance Steve Jones; and Joe Polakovich and fianc
2 CONC e Jen Bringenberg; four great-grandchildren, Janelle, Natalie, Tyler, and Payton. She was preceded in death by five sisters and a brother. &lt;strong&gt;Services:&lt;/strong&gt; A Mass of Christian burial is scheduled for 10 a.m., Thursday, May 12
2 CONC , 2011 at Assumption of the Blessed Virgin Mary Church, 22nd and Washington Avenue, Northampton, PA. 18067, with calling hours 7-8:30 p.m., Wednesday, May 11, 2011 and Thursday, May 12, 2011 from 8:30-9:30 a.m. both at the Schisler Funeral home, 21
2 CONC 19 Washington Avenue, Northampton, PA 18067. Fr. Francis Straka will preside over the mass and the prayers at the funeral home 9:15 a.m. Interment will follow the mass at Assumption B.V.M. Cemetery in Northampton, PA. &lt;strong&gt;Contributions: &
2 CONC lt;/strong&gt;Assump. B.V.M. Church Memorial fund C/O the funeral home. Online condolences may be offered to the family at www.schislerfuneralhomes.com&lt;/span&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
