2 CONC h, USA&lt;/td&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;td colspan="2" valign="top"&gt;&lt;br&gt;RITES HELD FOR ROGER HORROCKS, BASIN PIONEER&lt;br&gt; Funeral rites were held for Roger Horrocks, September 11, in the Neol
2 CONC a LDS Ward Chapel.&lt;br&gt; Mr. Horrocks, age 89, a Uintah Basin pioneer, died Friday night at the home of a son, Victor, of caused incident to age. He was born Dec 23, 1872, in Heber to Roger and Sarah Ann Taylor Horrocks. He married Eliza Ann Mo
2 CONC on, Dec 4, 1895 in the Salt Lake Temple. She died March 26, 1926. He then married Girilda Wilkerson, March 17, 1927, in the Salt Lake Temple. She died November 14, 1959. &lt;br&gt; Survivors of the late farmer, stockman, and businessman are eight s
2 CONC ons, Walter, Santaquin; Theron and Victor, Neola; Lloyd and LaVell, Salt Lake City; James, Houston, Texas; Ray, Bigpine California; and Ervin, Wichita, Kansas. Four daughters, Mrs. Blaine (Florence) Lee, Mrs. Ward (Reva) Merkley, Vernal; Mrs. Joh
2 CONC n (Mary) Gerber, Chula Vista, California; Mrs. Lyle (Sarah) Glines, Salt Lake City; 40 grandchildren; 70 great-grandchildren. &lt;br&gt; There are five brothers, Thomas, Heber; Brigham, Blackfoot, Idaho; Frank, Rangely, Colorado; and David and Jose
2 CONC ph, Salt lake City; one sister, Mrs. Frank (Vernie) Epperson, Heber.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tbody&gt;</line><line /></content></metadataxml>
