1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;Will: The will of Theophilus Redfield, made 22 September 1738 and&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; proved 6 March 1759 give
2 CONC s his wife Priscilla her thirds; gives&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; personal estate to his daughters, all unnamed, and directs that the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&a
2 CONC mp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; land be divided among his nine sons. He appoints his wife and son&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Daniel as executors. The inventory taken 31 March 1759 includes&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the date of his death. During his lifetime he had kept a list of&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; advancements to his older six sons and hi
2 CONC s eighth son Josiah and&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; these were taken into account in the distribution which names the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ; sons and daughters in sequence (but the latter without married&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; names). Division of the land was made among the nine sons: the&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&
2 CONC amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; heirs of Daniel his deceased eldest son, Richard, Ebenezer,&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Theophilus, Peleg, George, William, Josiah and James.&lt;/span&gt;&l
2 CONC t;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
