1 _OID 8f71751e-61ce-450b-a53d-129fd0238751
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;Elias Smith Marriages&lt;/div&gt;  	 		 			&lt;p&gt;Compiled by Judith W. Hansen, AG&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a record of  marriages performed in Utah by Elias Smith as taken from his Journals.  Smith was Pro
2 CONC bate Judge of Salt Lake County, Utah Territory, from 1851  to 1884. The marriages were not recorded in Salt Lake County Probate  Court minutes probably because most happened in the evenings at Smith&amp;rsquo;s  residence or in other homes in the a
2 CONC rea rather than at the court  building. During this period there was no law in Utah Territory which  required marriages to be recorded.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Source: Taken from &lt;em&gt;Marriages  in Utah Territory, 1850-1884, from the Deseret News 18
2 CONC 50-1872 and The  Elias Smith Journals 1850-1884&lt;/em&gt;, compiled by Judith W. Hansen, AG  and Norma Lundberg. UGA monograph Series, No.4, Published by Utah  Genealogical Association, 1998.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compiler&amp;#39;s notes: Smith note
2 CONC d  other marriages in his Journals besides those for which he was  officiator. These are &lt;em&gt;not &lt;/em&gt;listed here. The marriages are listed  in two groups, a full extraction alphabetically by  &lt;strong&gt;Grooms&amp;#39;  Names&lt;/st
2 CONC rong&gt; (with comments), and a record of marriages alphabetically  by Brides&amp;#39; Names (without comments).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Newell Horace CLAYTON to Miss Alice Rose ELLERBECH 13 Oct 1873 Both of 17th ward.&lt;/p&
2 CONC gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
