2 TITL Ellen Breakel Neibaur&#39;s Precious Shoes
1 _OID 90c184d9-e3e8-4de5-ac1a-f5fb851afca6
1 DATE 1849
1 PLAC Salt Lake City, Utah
1 _DSCR Ellen Breakel gives up her shoes to help Pioneers entering Salt Lake Valley
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: inherit;"&gt;Ellen and Alexander Neibaur both came from wealthy families, so their needs were always met.&amp;nbsp; When the gospel came to their little town of Preston England, the
2 CONC y came to know of it's truthfulness and joined the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints in 1838.&amp;nbsp; They were some of the first to immigrate to America, to join the Saints gathering to Zion.&amp;nbsp; They settled in Nauvoo, home of t
2 CONC he Prophet Joseph Smith.&amp;nbsp; They became good friends with Joseph and Emma Smith.&amp;nbsp; Alexander, fluent in 7 languages, taught Joseph German and Hebrew.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="font-family: inherit;"&gt;&lt;br&gt; When t
2 CONC he Saints were driven from their homes in Nauvoo by angry mobs in 1846, Ellen had a ten-day old baby and six other children.&amp;nbsp; Ellen was in no condition to travel and soon became sick.&amp;nbsp; When they reached safety in Winter Quarters
2 CONC , a sister cared for Ellen, putting her to bed and caring for her baby until she was better.&amp;nbsp; They joined the Brigham Young Company crossing the plains.&amp;nbsp; Ellen drove a pair of lead cows most of the way, standing next to them to gu
2 CONC ide them along.&amp;nbsp; Some of the time, she held that tiny baby in her other arm, as the baby was...&amp;nbsp; (Read the rest of the story at http://storiesoffaithandcourage.blogspot.com/2011/07/ellen-breakell-neibaurs-precious-shoes.html)&lt;b
2 CONC r&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
