1 _DSCR Published in the Salt Lake Tribune Newspaper
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div style="line-height: 21px;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: normal; font-family: 'comic sans ms'; font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Venice Moon&lt;/
2 CONC span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&
2 CONC lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Van Wagoner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;spa
2 CONC n style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;1922 ~ 2013&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=
2 CONC "line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Venice Moon Van Wagoner left this life on October 26th 2013 surrounded by her loving family to join her eternal companion Ferrin Dean Van Wagoner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height
2 CONC : 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; f
2 CONC ont-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;She was born August 8th 1922 in Woodland Utah, to Heber and Emily Moon. She and her twin sister Florence were the only girls born in a family of 7 boys. She attended Tabiona High School where she met, fell i
2 CONC n love with, and married Ferrin Dean Van Wagoner.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br styl
2 CONC e="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Among her many accomplishments, she played saxophone with her sister Florence (they were known as the "Twin Tooters fro
2 CONC m Tabiona"), she was a member of the singing group "The Choralettes", served as the state PTA director,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px
2 CONC ; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;reporter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;and corre
2 CONC spondent for the Deseret News. By far her most important accomplishment was her family.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: t
2 CONC imes; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;She was an active member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints and s
2 CONC erved in many capacities with her favorite being a primary teacher for 30 plus years.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: tim
2 CONC es; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;She is survived by her children; Annette (Jay) Casper, Gordon (Kris), Kendall (Pam)
2 CONC , Sherilynn (LeeRoy) Farrell, Kerry (Coralee) and Brett (Tamra). 27 grandchildren, 78 great-grandchildren, and 2 great-great grandchildren and her dear friend and neighbor Ki Kiholm.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times
2 CONC ; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;br style="line-height: 22px; padding: 0px;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 22px; font-family: times; font-si
