1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td valign="top"&gt;Birth:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt;Mar. 2,  1892&lt;br&gt;Spanish Fork&lt;br&gt;Utah County&lt;br&gt;Utah, USA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;
2 CONC td valign="top"&gt;Death:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt;Dec. 9,  1962&lt;br&gt;Roosevelt&lt;br&gt;Duchesne County&lt;br&gt;Utah, USA&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" valign="top"&gt;&lt;img src="http://www
2 CONC .findagrave.com/icons2/trans.gif" alt="" width="3" height="13"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong style="width: 100%; text-align: center"&gt;FUNERAL HONORS EX-RESIDENT IN ROOSEVELT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Funeral  services were conducted Wednesday a
2 CONC t 11 a.m. in the Roosevelt LDS Stake  Chapel, for a former Vernal resident, Mrs. Jasper O. (Julina) Butcher,  70, who died Sunday at 3:30 a.m. in the Roosevelt Hospital after a long  illness.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mrs. Butcher was born March 2, 1892 i
2 CONC n Jensen, Utah, a  daughter of Andrew and Lucy Markham Dudley. She was married to Jasper O.  Butcher, February 27, 1911 in Vernal and was an active member of the  LDS Church.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She is survived by her husband and sons and  daughters
2 CONC , Otis D., Perry Andrew, Lile T., all of Roosevelt; Mrs. Earl  (Catherine) Gillespie, Moab; James A., Evanston, Wyoming; Mrs. Herman  (Jessie) Baumgaertel, Kearns; Sanford L., Sidney, Nebraska; 15  grandchildren, four great-grandchildren; brothers
2 CONC , Joseph S. Dudley,  Jensen and Hosmer Dudley, Salt Lake City.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;-Vernal Express, December 13, 1962, transcribed by Rhonda Holton&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Family links:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;Parents:&lt;br&gt;&
