1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 20pt"&gt;William Aldridge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new r
2 CONC oman','serif'; font-size: 20pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 20pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;s
2 CONC pan style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;In 1888, William Aldridge (he was known as &amp;ldquo;Uncle Bill&amp;rdquo; by all who knew him) heard of the vast prairies of Canada with grass, belly deep to a horse wit
2 CONC h lots of water.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Having a large herd of livestock he decided to move north to the new country.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He made the trip in about three months, arriving in July with his wife and four sma
2 CONC ll children.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They settled at Whiskey Gap on the Milk River.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Bill was of a roving nature so they never lived in one place very long.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They then m
2 CONC oved south east of Cardston on the St. Mary River.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Albert was born there on September 4, 1888.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size
2 CONC ="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;The next move was further down the S. Mary River on the east bank just below where Lee Creek empties in
2 CONC to the river.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This was the year 1890.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Elethine was born May 13, 1890. &lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;She died June 19. 1890.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The river wa
2 CONC s in flood at this time so she was buried there.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The house was built at the mouth of a coulee and during a terrible hailstorm, which hit the district, the house was flooded.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;So t
2 CONC he next move was to Rush Lake, now in the Woolford District.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;While building this home a prairie fire came through and they had to fight back fire to save the family and home from being burned.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ; &lt;/span&gt;This disclosed the rocks on the land so in 1891 they moved to Taylorville, where he put up hay on the Vaughn Meadows and freighted it to Lethbridge and sold it to I.G. Baker Company.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;
2 CONC span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Amy was born on October 12, 1891 wh
2 CONC ilethey were living in Taylorville.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family
2 CONC : 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;In 1889 William Vaughn and his family moved from Idaho to Canada.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;With them they brought the herd of Hamiltonian horses that Joseph Aldridge had left to Bill an
2 CONC d his sister Elethine.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new ro
2 CONC man','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;The next move was down on the north branch of the Milk River, where Bill did some prospecting and discovered coal.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This he developed, hired a miner and sold blacksmith coal t
2 CONC o the public.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Not a very big market however as the country was so sparsely settled at the time.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font siz
2 CONC e="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;While they lived at the Milk River, they had a Chesapeake dog named Beaver because of his brown coat.&
2 CONC lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He had been taught to take the miner&amp;#39;s dinner to him and this he would do.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;One time in the winter Bill started out to the Police Barracks and he lost one of his mitts.&lt
2 CONC ;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The dog found it and brought it to the house and scratched on the door.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Annie went to the door and the dog looked toward the direction that Bill had gone and Annie nodded her hea
2 CONC d yes and he took off and caught up with Bill and gave him the mitt.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;They fed the horses oats one day and it was the dog
2 CONC s job to bring them in.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He did this on a dead run.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;When they moved back to Cardston, Annie would give him a note to take downtown and find Bill.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&g
2 CONC t;He would bring back whatever Bill had purchased that she wanted from downtown.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;When they moved to Waterton they took him with them, however when they moved from there he was too old to travel so he was left wit
2 CONC h another family that lived there at the time.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="fo
2 CONC nt-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;When Bill moved to Milk River he had taken his share of the horses with him so he went into the ranching business in earnest.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;As there was no timber cl
2 CONC ose, Bill with the aid of the older children built corrals of large flat stones that were from two to five inches thick.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;In large slabs they carried these down the steep hills from the cliffs.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ; &lt;/span&gt;Here they made the coulee corral by blocking the mouth of the coulee, the sides of which were so steep nothing could scale them.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This they divided with another fence of stone and made a branding cor
2 CONC ral, chute and all.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;At the ranch home they built a cow and calf corral fenced with these flat stones from a foot to two and half feet wide, piled like bricks but without mortar.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;To amuse themselves
2 CONC , the boys and girls gathered wild geese eggs and hatched them under the hens.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;In the fall these wild ones flew south with the rest of the wild geese, but to their surprise the next spring several of these geese c
2 CONC ircled first and they alighted in the ranch yard.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Dave was the goose caller and they came right to him.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This was repeated several years or until they left Cardston.&lt;/font&gt;&
2 CONC lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&g
2 CONC t;On July 4, 1893 Herman was born and on March 21, 1895 Frank was born at Milk River.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
2 CONC &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;One day Bill was impressed with the idea that some day if he continued there with the boys doing the riding and the on the round up that one of the
2 CONC m would meet with a fatal accident as there were many badger holes.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;In riding to round up and care for wild horses, fast riding was necessary and bronco busting was dangerous, either as sport or as in this case
2 CONC , a necessity.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He traded his horses and &amp;ldquo;Slipper Brand&amp;rdquo; across for 64 head of cattle.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;When the round up came, they found the Vaughns owned 200 head of purebre
2 CONC d horses which they sold during the Spanish American War for $100.00 a head to the US government.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&
2 CONC lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Next Bill moved his family to Whiskey Gap where he built a house by the big spring.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This spring ha
2 CONC d almost ice-cold water.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;An inch and a half stream poured out.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They built what they called the springhouse over this.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They also built another h
2 CONC ouse to live in.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They didn&amp;#39;t live here very long, but were on the move again.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This time they moved to Cardston, where for the first time the older children were able to g
2 CONC o to school.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Previous to this Annie had taught the children.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt
2 CONC ;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;At Cardston, Annie Diantha was born March 5, 1897 and John William on August 28, 1898.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;
2 CONC span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;In 1897 they move to Kootenai Lakes
2 CONC , now called Waterton Lakes and settled at what was known as Aldridge Bay.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This is the Bay by what is now Linnet Lake.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They built a log house with dirt floor, flour sack window a
2 CONC nd a canvas for a door.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They took with them 75 head of cattle, workhorses and the necessary belongings for a large family.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They never tired of the beautiful scenery but as Bill s
2 CONC aid &amp;ldquo;You can&amp;#39;t live on scenery and climate&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&l
2 CONC t;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;When Bill moved the cattle he had made arrangements with a man to put up hay for him, but he failed to put up what he had agreed to and there was an extra sever
2 CONC e winter with a great deal of snow.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Nearly all the cattle and horses died.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They tried to save them by cutting branches of trees and brush but to no avail.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &
2 CONC lt;/span&gt;To make things even worse, a lot of the wild animals died that winter which made game very scarce and hard to get.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;During the winter the family survived on bread, water gravy, fish and a few frozen pot
2 CONC atoes.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;font size="3"&gt;At this time Waterton Lakes was filled with large Mackinaw Lake Trout.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Some weighing up to 35 pounds which the older boys would catch with set lines.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They p
2 CONC ut up ice in the wintertime so that the fish could be packed in ice and straw and delivered to Cardston even in the summer in good condition.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&
2 CONC lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;The family became close friends with Kootenai Brown and his Indian wife.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nb
2 CONC sp; &lt;/span&gt;She was a jolly, happy person and they all loved her dearly.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;She kept her home spotlessly clean and very neat.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Kootenai had a pet Indian name for his wife, &amp;
2 CONC ldquo;Nichymoose&amp;rdquo; which meant Lovely Lady and that is what they all called her.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;She had an Indian name for each of the children. Oliver who was small she called &amp;ldquo;Big Man&amp;rdquo;.&lt;span&gt;
2 CONC &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Annie was a baby with two teeth so she called her &amp;ldquo;Kneeswapatishis&amp;rdquo; which meant &amp;ldquo;Little Two Teeth&amp;rdquo;.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Frank had long curly hair and she called him &amp
2 CONC ;ldquo;Tipowest&amp;rdquo; which meant &amp;ldquo; Little Curly Head&amp;rdquo;.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Several times Nichymoose and Kootenai Brown saved them from going hungry with gifts of food.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt
2 CONC ;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;One time when the famil
2 CONC y was out of meat, an elk started to cross the narrows and fell through the ice.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Bill and the boys were able to get it and it helped with the food supply&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span styl
2 CONC e="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Bill and the boys built a lime kiln in the b
2 CONC ank near their home.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They hauled the limestone from the other side of the lake on the ice and fired the kiln with wood night and day.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;All the boys took their turn and it was ver
2 CONC y tiring task, but they accomplished this great task without complaining.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;When the ice broke up in the spring, they discontinued the lime kiln.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This lime was sold in the surround
2 CONC ing country.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="
2 CONC font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Annie was doctor, dentist and nurse for the family during all the years that they moved from one place to another.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;One time when Bill&amp;#39;s teet
2 CONC h started to ache very badly and he could not leave to go to Cardston to have them pulled.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Kootenai Brown came by with a bottle of rum and told him to drink plenty of it and then they could pull his teeth withou
2 CONC t them hurting to badly.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He drank the rum and then Annie started to pull his teeth, but he fought so hard that the older boys had to hold him down and tie him to the bed.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Annie p
2 CONC ulled the worst of his teeth as he was bleeding so badly that she was afraid to pull them all.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;She got the ones that were aching.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The next morning he woke up and said &amp;ldquo;
2 CONC Annie, my teeth don&amp;#39;t ache anymore&amp;rdquo; She then told him that he didn&amp;#39;t have any teeth to ache.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Ano
2 CONC ther time when David had pneumonia and they thought he would not live, Annie doctored him and took care of him and he recovered.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size=
2 CONC "3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;In the wintertime they played on the ice in their bare feet.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;At one t
2 CONC ime the older boys corned a bobcat on the ice.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The cat would slip but the boys could run in their bare feet.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Finally they threw an axe and killed it.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/s
2 CONC pan&gt;The skin was used to make a muff for Mary.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;font face="System"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;font face="Arial"&gt;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
