2 TITL William Ayrey/Airey's of Dent
1 _OID a1d87857-c108-4d1d-9e9f-11c395d72a84
1 PLAC Dent, Yorkshire
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;There are two William Aireys recorded in Dent in the late 1700&amp;#39;s&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;William son of Charles b1735 d1820. A Farmer at Baxtongill (Dent)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Will
2 CONC iam son of Robert (who was the son of Oswald b 1696 who could well have been&amp;nbsp;the s of Oswald b1675) b1739 d 1779&amp;nbsp; reference is made to a cooper in the Dent records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Most records have William 1735 having 3 wife&am
2 CONC p;#39;s Elizabeth Ashburner, Alice Thistlethwaite and Elizabeth Lindsey&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This Tree has Alice Thistletwaite as the wife of William b1739 for the following reasons&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There is no Death recorded for E Ashburner&lt;/p&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;p&gt;Alice&amp;#39;s third child and 1st son was called Robert, in line with the naming convensions the 1st son was usually called after the father or G/father. There is no Robert in the family line of William b 1735, whereas the Father of wil
2 CONC liam b1739 was Robert.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
