2 TITL OUR FAREWELL TRIBUTE TO MOTHER
1 _OID a6443ddc-d523-4702-ba95-9ff55eb7b841
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div style="color: #333331; font-family: verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&amp;nbsp;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="font-size
2 CONC : 17px; line-height: 28px; margin-: 22px; margin-bottom: 0px; font-family: verdana; color: #4f4f4c; letter-spacing: -0.1px; white-space: pre-line;"&gt;Composed and dedicated to her Grandmother MARY ANN DAVIS MOON by Eva Hoskins Sweetest mother, a
2 CONC s now you see us Gathered round you here today, In our parting with you, dearest, There is much we&amp;rsquo;d like to say. Oh, deeply we appreciate The things that you have done The true devotion of your life Brings thanks from everyone. Your love
2 CONC &amp;mdash;a mother&amp;rsquo;s love&amp;mdash; The greatest gift of all We know shall linger with us No matter what befall. The dear, sweet music of your voice Your gentle words of love Cannot be stilled, altho transferred To brighter realms above
2 CONC . Their memory now is cherished And in each heart held dear And as we think about the past Their echoes we shall hear. An Emigrant from o&amp;rsquo;er the seas Who reached a foreign strand And pioneered across the lonely plains To be in Zion&amp;rs
2 CONC quo;s land Not by a flowery sermon Was piousness professed But by a quiet, useful life Your creed was best expressed. The path of virtue you defined You taught us to be true And all of worth we might achieve We&amp;rsquo;ll owe, dear one, to you. W
2 CONC ith willing hands and cheerfulness You helped in every way Such service as you rendered then We cannot find today. So tenderly and graciously You soothed our cares away We&amp;rsquo;d ask you, Mother, could you speak How can we best repay? Still wa
2 CONC tching and still waiting Till we have crossed Death&amp;rsquo;s sea And then to guide and love us Through all eternity&amp;mdash; We&amp;rsquo;ll see you thus in fancy As parting time draws nigh, So, only for a little while, Brave one, dear heart
2 CONC , Good-bye. Retyped by Lynn Ellis Wood, July 2013 (Eva Hoskin&amp;rsquo;s Grandaughter)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
1 _CREA 2021-05-12 16:10:18.000
