2 TITL The Will of Elizabeth Moon
1 _OID a974f561-6e3f-49e6-98a3-d308ab848762
1 DATE 1 May 1799
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Elizabeth Moon, daughter of Richard of Catforth, &lt;/span&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;had an illegitimate son, Edward Moon, to whom &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;she devised all her property and personal estate, but if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&g
2 CONC t;he died before the age of 21 years then as follows: to her niece Sarah Waterworth &amp;pound;5, as soon as she was old&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;enough to give a release for the same, and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span
2 CONC &gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;residue equally to her three brothers, Henry of&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Kingston, Jamaica, Robert of Catterall, and Edward, and to her sister Mary Moon. Rob
2 CONC ert Moon of Catterall&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;and William, son of Thomas Houghton of Lewth, were executors, the will is signed, Elizabeth Moon, and dated 1 May, 1799; it was proved 5 July, 1800.&lt;/span&gt;&lt
2 CONC ;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
