2 CONC pan style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Married 1857 Anna Moon b. 1830 only daughter of James Moon of Hillside House, Liverpool.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, hel
2 CONC vetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;They had the following children:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;1.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Hercules Jame
2 CONC s b.1860 d.3 Feb 1869 of diptheria,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;2.&amp;nbsp; Mary Isabella b.30 May 1862 d.29 Jan 1869 of diptheria,&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;3.&amp;nbsp; Helen b.12 Sep 1863 d.4 Feb 1869 of diptheria,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;spa
2 CONC n style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;4.&amp;nbsp; Edward Uchtred b.2 Feb 1865 d.1 Feb 1869 of diptheria,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-
2 CONC serif; font-size: small;"&gt;5.&amp;nbsp; Anna Katherine b.10 Jun 1868,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;6.&amp;nbsp; Margaret Rose de Noel b.25 D
2 CONC ec 1869. Died 25 Nov 1954 "Leithfield" Fordoun, Kincardineshire, Scotland. Msrried 14 Jul 1897 Montrose, an advocate Edward&amp;nbsp; Hercules Robertson b&amp;nbsp; 24 Jan 1867 Forfar, Angus d 21 Sep 1915 Angus. One dtr Freda&amp;nbsp; Robertso
2 CONC n b 1901&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Latter two daughters survived their father.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="
2 CONC font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;----------------------------------------------------------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;div style="mso-element: para-border-div; border: none; border-bottom: dotted windowte
2 CONC xt 3.0pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 3.75pt; line-height: normal; border: none; mso-border-bottom-alt: dotted windowtext 3.0pt; padding: 0cm; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;&lt;span style="font
2 CONC -family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Parish Surveys 1863 :- "Parish of Montrose: Hedderwick- the property of Lord Benholme (Hercules Scott)."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 3.75pt; line-height
2 CONC : normal; border: none; mso-border-bottom-alt: dotted windowtext 3.0pt; padding: 0cm; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;-----------------------------------------
2 CONC --------------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 3.75pt; line-height: normal; border: none; mso-border-bottom-alt: dotted windowtext 3.0pt; padding: 0cm; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-fami
2 CONC ly: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;The following article was printed in the Dundee Courier 23rd April 1870: -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;"Presentation of the Fre
2 CONC edom of the Burghof Montrose to Hercules Scott, Esquire."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 3.75pt; line-height: normal; border: none; mso-border-bottom-alt: dotted windowtext 3.0pt; padding: 0cm; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 0
2 CONC cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;------------------------------------------------------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 3.75pt; line-height: normal; bo
2 CONC rder: none; mso-border-bottom-alt: dotted windowtext 3.0pt; padding: 0cm; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;"&gt;Lathallan School online:-" Lathallan School was origi
2 CONC nally located next to Lathallan Farm just south of the hamlet of Largoward in Fife. However, following a fire in the early hours of 2nd September 1949 the school with 74 boys, moved to Brotherton Castle which was then owned by Charles Alexander
2 CONC , a parent.The Castle was built in 1867 by Hercules James Scott, who had married Anna Moon the daughter of a Liverpool cotton merchant. On Hercules Scott's death in 1897 his eldest daughter, Anna Katherine (the last Scott to live at Brotherton Cast
2 CONC le) succeeded to the estate. The estate had its own gas-works, as well as five gardeners, five foresters and three gamekeepers who kept the grounds in order. Inside the Castle there was a housekeeper, butler, footman, hall boy, cook, kitchen maid
2 CONC s and scullery maids. There was also the Castle's own laundry employing two maids. With the advent of the car two chauffeurs were employed, and in North Lodge, the house at the top of the main driveway, there lived a gatekeeper. During the Second W
2 CONC orld War Brotherton Castle was turned into a maternity hospital. Miss Scott died in July 1948 and Brotherton was left to her niece, Mrs Freda Gell, who in turn sold the estate to Mr Charles Alexander.In 1950 he sold the castle and its grounds to th
2 CONC e school governors. In 1976 the school finally became co-educational. A nursery department followed and in 2004 the school opened an adjacent 'Lathallan Nursery', which offers nursery care and education all year round. Lathallan's biggest step forw
2 CONC ard was still to come, however, as in 2004 the school announced its intention to continue its own unique brand of education to senior school pupils. The first senior school pupils joined the school in September 2006, with the senior school housed i
2 CONC n the main castle building."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 3.75pt; line-height: normal; border: none; mso-border-bottom-alt: dotted windowtext 3.0pt; padding: 0cm; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&
