1 _DSCR Farndale is a valley located in the North York Moors National Park in North Yorkshire, England. The nearest town is Kirkbymoorside located some 5 miles to the south. Pickering is some 13 miles to the south east and Helmsley 12 miles to the south we
2 CONC st. Farndale is surrounded by some of the most wild moorland in England, and is sandwiched between Bransdale and Rosedale. To the north east sits Blakey Ridge at over 400 m above sea level, and to the north west, Cockayne Ridge reaching up to 45
2 CONC 4 m above sea level is one of the highest points of the North York Moors. Around the north of Farndale, between Bloworth Crossing and Blakey is the track bed of the old Rosedale Ironstone Railway (Rosedale Branch) which forms part of two Long Dista
2 CONC nce Footpaths these being Wainwright's Coast to Coast Walk and The Lyke Wake Walk.
