2 TITL Lucile Moon Steele
1 _OID aff43d53-4dee-4310-8b80-f7bb5a84e279
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Lucile Moon Steele&lt;br&gt; October 5, 1928 &amp;ndash; June 12, 2017&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; Lucile Moon Steele returned home to her loving Heavenly Father on Monday, June 12, 2017. Lucile was born October 5, 192
2 CONC 8 in Mesa, Arizona as the first child of Charles Irwin and Beth McClellan Moon. She graduated from Venice High School, California in January 1946. Soon after, she and her family moved to Orem, UT. While waiting for college to start in the fall, sh
2 CONC e re-enrolled at Lincoln High School and received a second high school diploma. It was here that she met the love of her life, Robert Que Steele. &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; Lucile and Que were married in the Manti, Utah LDS temple on April 19, 1948. Luc
2 CONC ile adored Que. He could do no wrong in her mind and she supported him in everything. Que and Lucile had 10 children together. &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; She worked at various places throughout the years, including Utah Valley University, where she hel
2 CONC d many positions and worked until the age of 80. She took several classes at the college including a wood working class and machining class. She was an active life learner and even learned how to swim at the age of 50. One of her proudest accomplis
2 CONC hments was serving as an Orem City Councilwoman.&lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; Lucile was an active member of the LDS church and served faithfully in many church callings. She loved working with the Young Women serving 18 years at Girl's Camp. She also ha
2 CONC d the opportunity to serve as a missionary with Que in the England London Mission after their children were grown. &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; Lucile's heart was centered on family. She was a hardworking and devoted wife, mother and grandmother. She wa
2 CONC s fun, kind, accepting, and loving to all. A constant highlight in her life was the cabin that she and Que built with their family in Lava Hot Springs, Idaho. The Steele Family has had many family reunions at this cabin and shared many special time
2 CONC s together there. Lucile looked forward to visiting "Steeleaway" even up until the last years of her life. &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; Lucile is preceded in death by her husband, Robert Que Steele, her father and mother, Charles Irwin and Beth McClella
2 CONC n Moon, her infant son, Mathew, her son-in-law, Val Mortenson, and two granddaughters&amp;mdash;Whitney Steele and Michele Tucker. She is survived by her children Coreyne Mortenson, Lorraine (Gayle) Davis, Brigg (Janet), Erwin (Barb), David (JoDee)
2 CONC , Beth (Brad) Gale, Robert (Laurel), Frost (Marie), and Samuel (Keri) Steele. She is also survived by her siblings, Clarence (Ann) Moon, Tom Moon, and Karen (Mike) Mitchell. She will be fondly remembered by her 51 grandchildren, 131 great-grandchil
2 CONC dren, and three great-great grandchildren. &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; The family would like to express heartfelt thanks to Axis Home Care and Horizon Hospice Care. &lt;br&gt; &lt;br&gt; There will be a viewing Friday, June 16 at the LDS Sunset Heights S
2 CONC take Center located at 1260 S 400 W, Orem, from 6 p.m. to 8 p.m. Funeral services will begin Saturday, June 17, 2017 at 11 a.m. at the same location. Friends may visit with the family from 9:30 a.m. to 10:30 a.m. prior to the funeral.&lt;/p&gt;</li
2 CONC ne></content></metadataxml>
