1 _DSCR Better rendition of the Winder Crest.  Entire description of the crest from "General Armory of England, Scotland, Ireland and Wales" reads: 'Out of a ducal coronet or (gold) a bull's head erm (black and white) holding in the mouth a cherry branch s
2 CONC lipped (torn or broken off) and fructed (bearing fruit) all ppr (proper, i.e., tinted with colors found in nature.)  Older form of crest would have had the bull's head upon a wreathe rather than the ducal coronet.
