2 CONC : normal; font-family: arial; color: #666666; -webkit-text-stroke-color: #666666; -webkit-text-stroke-width: initial; text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tuesday 25th July 1848&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0px; margi
2 CONC n-bottom: 0px; line-height: normal; font-family: arial; color: #666666; -webkit-text-stroke-color: #666666; -webkit-text-stroke-width: initial;"&gt;&lt;em&gt;S Wind. cool chilly morning &amp;ndash; cool thro&amp;rsquo; the nights[.] Breakfasts cook
2 CONC ing early for to start soon &amp;ndash; Gave Captn. Thomas despatches for E T Benson[,] 1 letter for G A Smith he enclosing copy of Camp journal or Extracts therefrom up to yesterday&amp;rsquo;s date with copy letter Council in the valley to B.Y. a
2 CONC lso copy of B.Y.&amp;rsquo;s &amp;amp; HCK&amp;rsquo;s letter to W. R. &amp;ndash; Dr R&amp;rsquo;s Co.y leads[.] S. Wind. see small herds of Buffalo &amp;ndash; late prenoon start. very windy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-
2 CONC : 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; line-height: normal; font-family: arial; color: #50504f; -webkit-text-stroke-color: #50504f; -webkit-text-stroke-width: initial;"&gt;Augusta Braddock daughter of Sister Ann Braddock aged 14 run over the body both wheels s
2 CONC triking the right shoulder &amp;amp; clear over her breast, thinks her left arm must have been up towards her head for no appearance of its being touched. She was reaching forward from the tongue to buck up the lead cattle when she believes the win
2 CONC d blew her off. after being run over she got up &amp;amp; walked a rod towards the waggon when she fell down &amp;amp; the Teamster having jumped out laid hold of her when her mother &amp;amp; Jane Hall also came out of the wagon to her assistance
2 CONC . The Dr coming up prayed for her &amp;ndash; put her into his carriage. &amp;amp; when Uncle Phineas R[ichards] Came up had him tend to her.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
