1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;St Mary the Virgin Monumental Inscriptions, Eccleston, Lancashire, England compiled by Roy and Grace Lowe 1995/1996&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt
2 CONC ;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;Plot7-Row10-Grave 6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;JOHN and AGNES THRELFALL - AGNES departed this life April 9th 1808 age 30 Her R
2 CONC ace Was Early Run Her Time Soon Or&amp;rsquo;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;She Left Her Husband Dear And Infants Four&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small
2 CONC ;"&gt;Their Loss Was Great They Can Express To Others&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;One Of The Best Wives And Tenderest Mothers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-siz
2 CONC e: small;"&gt;Also interred here the remains of MARY the wife of HUMPHREY RIGBY late of Ulnes Walton and sister to the above JOHN THRELFALL who died Feb 11th 1837 age 30 also in memory of JAMES THRELFALL of Eccleston and brother to the above who de
2 CONC parted this life Nov 24th 1853 age 58 also RICHARD son of the above who died April 29th 1890 age 71 also JANE his wife who died Sep 20th 1890 age 72&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;The Winter Of Tro
2 CONC uble Is Past&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;The Storms Of Affliction Are Or&amp;rsquo;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;The Struggle Is Ended At La
2 CONC st&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: small;"&gt;And Sorrow And Death Are No More&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
