2 TITL Uncle Bill Shoots Three Grizzlies
1 _OID c9de5c12-1b15-44ed-8e81-f461fb2855ce
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 20pt"&gt;Uncle Bill Shoots Three Grizzlies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-fam
2 CONC ily: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt"&gt;The following story as related by Joseph Y. Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;One day in the summer of 1898, Uncle Bill said to the three older boys, &amp;ldquo; Let&amp;#39;s get the tent and bed
2 CONC ding and go to the Head of the Lakes&amp;rdquo;.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This was a distance of about eleven miles from where they lived.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Into the boat that he owned and used a lot they climbed, fathe
2 CONC r and sons were changing at the oars.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family
2 CONC : 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;At the Head of the Lakes on the US side of the line they made camp.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;While the boys put up the tent Bill took his trusted rifle and the seven cartridges held i
2 CONC n the magazine.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo; I&amp;#39;ll see if I can get a deer for supper&amp;rdquo;, was his parting sentence.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;UP the side of No. 1 Goat Mountain he trudged, climbing windfall
2 CONC s and sweating.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;In these early days there were no blazed trails. &lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;You made your own and held to your direction or got lost in the timber.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The bo
2 CONC ys were listening down at camp where they all faithfully stayed.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;No wandering around like modern day youth.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;In a couple of hours they heard a shot, then another and soon another.
2 CONC &lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Following soon they heard four shots in rather rapid succession.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Dad&amp;#39;s in trouble&amp;rdquo;, said David, aged 16 as he grabbed his 30-30 Winchester.&lt;span&
2 CONC gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Oliver, then 13 years old grabbed his 30-30 and Charlie, aged 12, the shot gun.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Up the mountain they went at a very quick march.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo; Dad&amp;#3
2 CONC 9;s shells are gone, anything might happen&amp;rdquo;. He would not be able to defend himself any way nor run fast enough to get away from anything that might be after him.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family
2 CONC : 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Soon they spied him, rifle in hand coming down the mountai
2 CONC n on the run, over windfalls, not looking back, but headed for camp.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They shouted t him.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He shouted back, &amp;ldquo;Head for camp boys: all the bears in the mountains are afte
2 CONC r us.&amp;rdquo;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The boys could not see any, but they came not afraid but as obedient sons.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;When in camp, here is the story that Bill told, still panting for breath from his wil
2 CONC d run down the mountain.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo; Boys, I first saw something between two trees and took a crack at it.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Down flopped a big cub grizzly.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I he
2 CONC ard a noise behind me and looked around to see a whoppin&amp;#39; big she grizzly with a big cub comin&amp;#39; for me on the run.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;She was growling and foaming at the mouth.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;A
2 CONC s I turned the ol&amp;#39; gal heaved to her hind legs.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I let &amp;#39;er have it right between the eyes and down she flopped.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;But the big damn cub kep&amp;#39; a comin&amp;#39
2 CONC ; for me. I dropped to my knee and let &amp;#39;im have it, but only broke a leg.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He kept a comin&amp;#39; and howlin&amp;#39;. I shot again and broke another leg.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He was now u
2 CONC p on a big windfall and yellin&amp;#39; like Hell.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I cracked at the bouncin&amp;#39; cuss and broke another leg.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;I shot again and hit somewhere, but the howlin&amp;#39;, cryin&am
2 CONC p;#39;, yelpin&amp;#39; devil would have got me if he could.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;His yelps echoed through the mountains &amp;#39;til I&amp;#39;ll bet all the bears within 20 miles heard him and was runnin&amp;#39; my way.&lt;span&gt;
2 CONC &amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;And there I was out of shells and afoot.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;You know, I could hear so many bear yellin&amp;#39; I think it would be a good thing for us to move camp across the lake.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;
2 CONC /span&gt;It&amp;#39;s getting&amp;#39; kinda late too.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;What you say boys?&amp;rdquo;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo; Sure it&amp;#39;s all right with us&amp;rdquo;.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&g
2 CONC t;Down came the tent in a flash and into the boat they all scrambled.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Safe camp&amp;rdquo; was established for the night on the eastside of Upper Waterton Lake.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;e
2 CONC m&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp
2 CONC ;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The next morning, much braver by now with gun in hand, all four of them trudged up the mountain to the kill.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/sp
2 CONC an&gt;There they found them.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;First, the big cub laying dead between two trees, the mother grizzly near the windfall - but too close to &amp;ldquo;Uncle Bill&amp;rdquo; before the sure and fatal shot dropped her wi
2 CONC thin 25 feet of him, and the other big cub lying dead on the windfall.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;
2 CONC em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo;The boys wer
2 CONC e a little scared that night&amp;rdquo;, said Bill in reciting the hair-raising bear killing story.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo;Not so&amp;rdquo; said the boys; &amp;ldquo;It was Dad that was scared that time.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ; &lt;/span&gt;But, he got them all.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He&amp;#39;s a dead sure shot and we&amp;#39;d a stood by him &amp;#39;til all our ammunition was gone too.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;You bet your life&amp;rdquo;.&lt;
2 CONC /font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;fon
2 CONC t size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;On one of Bill&amp;#39;s trips to Cardston, he returned with a canoe.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/s
2 CONC pan&gt;They had built other larger and heavier boats that they used to hunt and fish with.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The boys were trying out the canoe that was very tricky to handle.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Bill had laid down f
2 CONC or a sleep after his trip, but when he awoke he pulled on his boots and came out to instruct the boys how to paddle a canoe.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He finally got disgusted at their clumsy efforts and called them to bring the canoe in a
2 CONC nd he would show them what to do.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He jumped in and got a short distance out into deep water when he missed the water with the paddle and the canoe capsized.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He was floundering ar
2 CONC ound in the water and the boys had to take another boat out to rescue him before he drowned.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;After that, he decided the boys were doing just fine.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They became experts at handlin
2 CONC g the canoe, even in rough water.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 't
2 CONC imes new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;During the time they lived at Aldridge Bay, Bill saw signs of o
2 CONC il on Cameron Creek above the falls at high water.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He and Oliver went on a camping trip to search for the source of the oil.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;They made camp across Cameron Creek above the falls a
2 CONC t where Oil City eventually sat.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;When Oliver went to get water, just below a small creek that entered Cameron Creek he noticed some signs of oil in the water.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He saw an animal tr
2 CONC ail leading up this small creek. He noticed there was oil on the bushes and when he followed this he found oil seepage where the animals had been rolling in the oil.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He returned and told his father of his discover
2 CONC y.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Bill smelled it, tasted it and felt it.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;ldquo;That ile boy, that&amp;#39;s ile&amp;rdquo;.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;That was the first commercial oil in Alberta
2 CONC .&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;
2 CONC font size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Bill gathered the oil by putting a dam across the small stream and then soaking the oil up wit
2 CONC h gunnysacks.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;This he would boil to get the water out.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He sold this oil in Cardston and surrounding district. This crude oil was a much used medicine in the early days, particula
2 CONC rly in the family for colds, pneumonia, sores, sunburn, blisters, etc.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;It was a cure-all.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&
2 CONC gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'times new roman','serif'"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;n
2 CONC bsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;At one time Alta was playing by the stove and a kettle boiled over and burned her leg.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;Bill had just brought in a pail of oil.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;He picked her up and se
2 CONC t her foot in it.&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;The leg healed up without leaving a scar.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;font face="System"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/
2 CONC strong&gt;&lt;font face="Arial"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
