1 _OID ce528e89-9629-4b8a-8e47-dbdfb0379b47
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;According to my mother she and Bernard spent quite a bit of time in Mossley when her mother Amelia was having trouble with pregnancies and births. I checked the phone directories for Mossley and came up with Lau
2 CONC ra Nelson who had been married to Gerard Nelson, son of Ernest Valentine. She invited me to her home, and what a lovely lady but sadly she died before I could visit her for a second time.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Apparently my grandfather Hen
2 CONC ry had been a good footballer and was alleged to have played for Mossley FC but I could not find any record of him. Laura told me that Ernie used to be a professional bowler when he lived in Penwortham. He married Sarah (who was said to be quite fi
2 CONC erce) at St Joseph;s RC church in Mossley. Sarah died before Ernie who died c1947 when he was about 63 and he was buried in Mossley cemetery. Laura thought he was a lovely man. She named all the people on a wedding photo I have. The wedding is of E
2 CONC rnie and Sarah's wedding.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
