1 DATE 29 Oct 1959
1 PLAC Vernal Express
1 _DSCR Obituary for Isabell Herbert Southam
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;FUNERAL SERVICES HELD WEDNESDAY FOR MRS. SOUTHAM&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Funeral services were held Wednesday, October 28, at 11 a.m. at Napl
2 CONC es Ward Chapel for Isabell Herbert Southam, 83, who died Saturday afternoon at her home following a long illness.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Mrs. Southam was born September 30, 1876, in Murray to Thomas and Ann Wardell Herb
2 CONC ert. She married G. H. Southam, November 8, 1993 in the Salt Lake LDS Temple. Mr. Soutahm died January 30, 1959.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;She is survived by five sons, three daughters, George H., Clair, Ralph, Grant, Nile
2 CONC s, Mrs. Walter (Elizabeth) Collier, Mrs. Victor (Merle) Wilkins, all of Vernal; Mrs. William F. (Ethel) Morton, Orem; a step-daughter, Mrs. Barnes (Alice) Cook, Cedar Valley, 39 grandchildren, 84 great-grandchildren, 9 great-great-grandchildren
2 CONC , a sister, Mrs. Josephine Foster, Park City.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Burial was in Vernal Memorial Park Cemetery.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;-Vernal Express, October 29, 1959, transcribed by Rho
2 CONC nda Holton&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
