1 _META <metadataxml><content><line /><line>&lt;tbody&gt;</line><line>&lt;tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;td colspan="2" valign="top"&gt;Rowene Riley Call passed away on May 8, 2014.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She was born July 6, 1936, grew up in Bountiful, and graduate
2 CONC d from Davis High School in 1954. She would have attended her sixtieth class reunion this year.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She married her high school sweetheart, Alan Call, on April 28, 1955 in the Salt Lake Temple. They lived in Farmington for forty-si
2 CONC x years.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She is survived by her husband of fifty-nine years, Alan Call; and her children, Vicky (Phil) Wright, Sally (Jeff) Plott, Pam (Rick) Pewtress, and Michael (Corrie) Call. She has fourteen grandchildren and twenty-one grea
2 CONC t-grandchildren. She loved and celebrated the addition of each new family member. She is preceded in death by her parents, L. Glen and Lois B. Riley; brothers, Kay and Leon Riley; sisters Alta Brown and Mary Lynn Coon; and grandson, Lance Pewtress.
2 CONC &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She was a faithful, dedicated member of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, which she loved with all her heart. She served as Ward Primary, Young Women's and Relief Society Presidents, as well as Stake Young Women'
2 CONC s President. She served as a full-time missionary with her husband Alan, in the Denver North Mission. Regardless of her calling, she served with love, joy, and with a servant's heart. Wherever she served, lives were deeply touched and changed for g
2 CONC ood.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For most of her life, she struggled with, and courageously rose above many physical illnesses and challenges. She was ever grateful for her many blessings and the miracles she received. Her faith and love for her Savior alon
2 CONC g with her love for her family brought her great joy and sustained her. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;She was a patient, loving teacher and a great example to all. She truly loved people and had many friends. Her loss will be greatly felt.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt
2 CONC ;The viewing will be held from 6:30 to 8:30 p.m. on Monday, May 12, 2014 at Russon Brothers Farmington Mortuary, 1941 North Main Street, Farmington. Funeral services will be held at 10:00 a.m., with a viewing from 9:00 to 9:30 a.m., on Tuesday, Ma
2 CONC y 13, 2014 in the Farmington Tenth Ward Chapel, 850 North Compton Road, Farmington.&lt;br&gt;Interment: Bountiful Memorial Park Cemetery.&lt;br&gt;Published in the Salt Lake Tribune on May 11, 2014.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tr&gt;</lin
2 CONC e><line>&lt;tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;td colspan="2"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tr&gt;</line><line>&lt;/tbody&gt;</line><line /><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
