1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;His&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times
2 CONC ;"&gt;friend and fellow warden was Thomas Hawkshead,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;the first of the family who settled in Eccleston about&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;1730, and live
2 CONC d at Heskin old hall. In 1745 Moon and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Hawkshead signed the agreement that no expenses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;were to be allowed to the wardens o
2 CONC n sacrament days&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;and for attendance at the consistory courts at Black&amp;shy;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;burn 25. only, and at Chorley ls. Others wh
2 CONC o signed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;this agreement included Nicholas Rigby of Harrock Hall and Alexander Kershaw of Heskin new hall.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Henry Moon was ove
2 CONC rseer of the poor for Eccleston 1747 in which year he signed a memorandum to levy &amp;pound;20 for the use of the church: Thomas Walker was&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;then curate of Eccleston. From time to time h
2 CONC e returns &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;the annual accounts, for Eccleston church, as for example that of 1757, which included payment for 110 loads of flag stones and laying the flags, repairs to the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span st
2 CONC yle="font-family: times;"&gt;church walls, payment for destruction of vermin, such &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;as sparrow hawks, jays, magpies and hedgehogs, re&amp;shy;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;n
2 CONC ewing the whip for whipping dogs from the church, payment for sacrament wine, etc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
