1 _OID d71247e8-c029-475b-9631-ac768b680b8a
1 DATE 4 May 1944
1 PLAC Vernal Express
1 _DSCR Obit for Andrew Dudley Jr.
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;font size="1"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;ANDREW DUDLEY PIONEER OF JENSEN DIES SUNDAY&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Andrew Dudley, pioneer resident of Jensen for the past 57 years, died a
2 CONC t his home Sunday morning at 6 o&amp;#39;clock following a brief illness. Mr. Dudley had been at work in his garden when he was stricken Saturday evening.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Mr. Dudley was born at Spanish Fork, Augu
2 CONC st 8, 1870, a son of Andrew and Lucy Markham Dudley. He married Sina Jensen of Spanish Fork in the Salt Lake LDS Temple January 10, 1900.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;As a member of the Jensen Ward bishopric for several year
2 CONC s Mr. Dudley served as a high priest until the time of his death. At one time he served as justice of the peace in Jensen.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;He is survived by his widow, four sons, A. Demar, Wendell and Lynn Duvall
2 CONC , all of Jensen; Howard J. Dudley, Arlington, Virginia, three daughters, Irene Wankier of Whitney, Nevada; Mrs. Alton Peterson, Boulder City, Nevada and Mrs. Lee Johnson, Los Angeles, California; four brothers, Joseph S. Dudley, Jensen; Stanford Du
2 CONC dley, Grand Junction, Colorado; Stephen M. Dudley, Alberta, Canada and Homer Dudley, Glenwood, Alberta, Canada; three sisters, Mrs. James Campbell, Vernal; Mrs. Jesse Butcher, Ballard; Mrs. Otis Witherall, Salt Lake in addition to 16 grandchildren.
2 CONC &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="4"&gt;Services will be held today (Thursday) at 2 p.m. at the Jensen Chapel under the direction of Bishop Ross Merrell. Burial will be at the Jensen Cemetery.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font si
2 CONC ze="4"&gt;-Vernal Express, May 4, 1944, transcribed by Rhonda Holton&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
