2 CONC aul church, Ormskirk, Lancashire on 22 December 1800. census records etc suggest they lived in Burscough, Lancashire and he was a Farmer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'arial black', 'avant garde'; font-siz
2 CONC e: small;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'arial black', 'avant garde'; font-size: small;"&gt;A different John Forshaw (1780) son of James Forshaw &amp;amp; Ann Pilkington, also married an An
2 CONC n ( possibly Ann Markland (1776) St Peter &amp;amp; St Paul church, Ormskirk, Lancashire on 12 September 1803. census records etc suggest they lived in Chapel Lane, Ormskirk, Lancashire and he was also a Farmer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&
2 CONC lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'arial black', 'avant garde'; font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'arial black', 'avant garde'; font-size: small;"&gt;Ellen Pilkington and An
2 CONC n Pilkington are sisters.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'arial black', 'avant garde'; font-size: small;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'arial black'
2 CONC , 'avant garde'; font-size: small;"&gt;There is such a close similarity between the available records to be positive that the above information is correct, to identify their children and establish dates of death.&amp;nbsp; More research needs to b
2 CONC e done.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
