2 CONC ARIES&lt;br&gt;MARY ASHTON JONES&lt;br&gt;Cherry Creek, Idaho - Mrs. Mary Emma Ashton Jones, 79, of Cherry Creek, died Thursday of natural causes at her home.&lt;br&gt;Mrs. Jones was born Dec. 30, 1890, in Portage, Utah, a daughter of Hyrum and Emm
2 CONC a Ella John Ashton.&lt;br&gt;On March 25, 1914, she was married to Brigham W. Jones in Woodruff, Idaho.&lt;br&gt;She was educated in Woodruff Schools.&lt;br&gt;She was a member of the LDS Church and Relief Society visiting teacher.&lt;br&gt;Survivi
2 CONC ng are her husband, three sons and five daughters, Leland A. Jones, Malad; M. Sgt. Cleland A. Jones, U.S. Air Force (ret.), Sunset; Avon L. Jones, Mrs. Kenneth (Sylvia Marie) Hefflefinger, Mrs. Glen (LaWana Lou) Spiers, all of Ogden; Mrs. Dale (Alt
2 CONC a Mae) Moon, Cherry Creek; Mrs. Ronald (Faye Louise) Jones, Clearfield; Mrs. John (Norma Rae) Everett, Pineville, La.&lt;br&gt;Also surviving are 24 grandchildren, 13 great-grandchildren, three brothers and one sister, Joseph Elias Ashton, Pocatell
2 CONC o; Warren V. Ashton, Cherry Creek; Harvey Willis Ashton, Mrs. Hugh (Merle) McLane, both of Ogden.&lt;br&gt;Funeral services will be held Monday at 1 p.m. in the Cherry Creek Ward Chapel with Bishop Cordell Williams officiating.&lt;br&gt;Friends ma
