2 CONC ectively&amp;rsquo; attain 21 years? Would both had to have been born 1780 onwards to be under 21 at time of will and supposed father died 1783. Convenient death for James of Bretherton 1829 aged 49. Could &lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: no
2 CONC rmal;"&gt;Edward&lt;/strong&gt; have been the Edward, born about 1780, who married Claris Hunter?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
