2 TITL THE SEA CROSSING
1 _OID ebbd5fa4-16de-495a-97e3-281bf6418d89
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;paraphrased from SAINTS ON THE SEAS. Conway B. Sone:&amp;nbsp; The BRITANNIA was a 2 deck, three mast packet ship of Black Ball Line. 630 ton square-rigger.&amp;nbsp; Lost at sea two years later.&amp;nbsp; Unde
2 CONC r Capt Enoch Cook. June 4, 1840. Carrying 41 Mormons. First British contingent.&amp;nbsp; Leader was Elder John Moon.&amp;nbsp; Arrived 44 days later, with three days in quarantine, at New York.&amp;nbsp; They had survived three storms and a lot o
2 CONC f seasickness. (picture of the BRITANNIA on p.44).&amp;nbsp; They went from New York to Pittsburgh, then on April 3&amp;nbsp;took a small sidewheeler called WILLIAM PENN, a 105 ton vessel with just one deck, and arrived at Montrose, Iowa on April 1
2 CONC 6, 1841.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(if they left June 4, 1840, they didn&amp;#39;t leave New York till the next year??)&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
