2 CONC d of Walsham dated 2&lt;sup&gt;nd&lt;/sup&gt; July 1504&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;all previous wills revoked&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to be buried in Christian burial&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Christ Church o
2 CONC f Norwich 12d&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to the high altar of Walsham, for tithes forgotten or not veril
2 CONC y well paid 12d and for the same cause to Sir William Mustarder 20d&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to the Fr
2 CONC iars of the old house of Thetford for my soul and all my friends&amp;rsquo; souls, for a trental 10s&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nb
2 CONC sp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to the Friars of the new house of Thetford for a trental 10s&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&am
2 CONC p;nbsp; to the Friars of Babwell for a trental 10s&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the &lt;strong&gt;townshi
2 CONC p of Walsham to have timber for a gild hall if so be that they intend to make the hall continently&lt;/strong&gt;, or else I will the timber to be sold by my executors to the best use, wherewith that I will have an able priest as far as it will rea
2 CONC ch, to sing for my soul and all my good friends&amp;rsquo; souls in the church of Walsham&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;&amp;nbsp; to Margaret my wife &lt;strong&gt;my tenement now builded at the churchgate&lt;/strong&gt;, with the croft thereto belonging and adjoining, with the &lt;strong&gt;shops&lt;/strong&gt; and the garden there lying nigh by to her and her h
2 CONC eirs at the will of the lord&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Margaret my wife 3 acres of meadow in the &lt
2 CONC ;strong&gt;Little Meadow&lt;/strong&gt; without the hedge, to her and her heirs&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbs
2 CONC p; the same Margaret to have 2 acres in the Little Meadow for her lifetime and after her decease to return again to my son Thomas and his heirs&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;to the same Margaret the over part of &lt;strong&gt;Fishepond Close&lt;/strong&gt; a
2 CONC s it is fenced out, so that the said Thomas shall have a reasonable way to go out of his part in the close lateward purchased of John Say so that the said Thomas shall fence out the said way at his cost and charge, to her and her heirs&lt;/p&gt;  &
2 CONC lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to the same Margaret the lesser part of the close late purchased of John Say of Walsham l
2 CONC ying next to the close lateward of John Malowse of Wattisfield and also next the &lt;strong&gt;Hill Green&lt;/strong&gt;, to her and her heirs&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;
2 CONC nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the said Margaret to have 3 of my best kine with a cow which is dry&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp
2 CONC ;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Margaret my wife all my stuff of household with all manner of instruments to my house in any wise belonging, so that she shall reward Thomas my son which stuff as she thinketh meetest fo
2 CONC r his occupying&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Margaret my wife all corn upon my ground growing, to her a
2 CONC nd her assignes&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; the said Margaret to have one of my best horses&lt;/p&gt;  &l
2 CONC t;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Thomas my son &lt;strong&gt;my tenement clepid Fortowts&lt;/strong&gt; with the croft t
2 CONC hereto adjoining with &lt;strong&gt;Pyes Close&lt;/strong&gt; with the close lying at the gate, free and copyhold, with the nether part of &lt;strong&gt;Fishepond Close&lt;/strong&gt; with the part of the close late purchased of John Say lying in W
2 CONC attisfield, as it is fenced, lying by the land lateward of John Shereve and the close lateward of John Molitons butting up on &lt;strong&gt;Jussards&lt;/strong&gt; with the Little Meadow except that is before excepted and reserved to Margaret my wi
2 CONC fe, to him and his heirs on condition Thomas pay to Margaret my wife 13s 4d by year during her lifetime after he enter the tenement and lands; also Thomas to pay yearly as soon as I am deceased, to my executors &amp;pound;40 and for that payment, T
2 CONC homas to find sufficient surety, bound by obligation ere he take his possession and of the said &amp;pound;40, 26s 8d pa. [to be] paid as long as my wife live and after the decease of my wife 40s pa. until the &amp;pound;40 be paid&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p
2 CONC &gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; of the which &amp;pound;40, I bequeath for an able priest 8 marks to pray for my soul and al
2 CONC l my good friends&amp;rsquo; souls, in Walsham church for a whole year, as it may be had of the &amp;ldquo;purchasetour&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nb
2 CONC sp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 10 coombs of mexstelyn and 5 cade of herring to be dealt by my executors, every Lent one part, until the sum be spent to poor people in the town of Walsham&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; for a &lt;strong&gt;cope to the church&lt;/strong&gt; of Walsham &amp;pound;10 as it may be had of the purchaser&lt
2 CONC ;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; for a vestment and &amp;ldquo;tonekiphill&amp;rdquo; with the albs thereto 10 m
2 CONC arks as it may be had of the purchaser&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Margaret Hoxne my daughter 5 mark
2 CONC s as it may be had of the purchaser&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; if Margaret decease ere this dutie be pai
2 CONC d, the said 5 marks to be equally departed among the children of the said Margaret by my executors&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp
2 CONC ;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to Thomas my son 6 horses with a shod cart and harness thereto and 3 kine with a dry cow with plough and harness&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&am
2 CONC p;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; to each of my godchidren 12d&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&
2 CONC amp;nbsp; Margaret my wife to have my shod cart&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Alice Cooke the wife of Rober
2 CONC t Cooke of Walsham to have my &lt;strong&gt;little cok horse&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbs
2 CONC p;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;the residue of all my timber, the works that I have taken before this date full finished and ended to go to the fulfilling of my will&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;n
2 CONC bsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;the residue of all my goods together with my debts to the disposition of my executors to dispose etc.&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;Executors: Thomas Rolfe of Wals
2 CONC ham and Stephen Rampoly of the same town&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;Witnesses: Sir James parish priest of the same town, Richard Neele and &lt;strong&gt;Robert Cooke carpenter&lt;/strong&gt; of Walsham&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;!--[if !supportEmptyParas]--&
2 CONC gt;&amp;nbsp;Proved at Norwich before Master Thomas Hare LLD, the official of the consistory court 15&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; March 1504 by Stephen Rampoly of Walsham executor. Power reserved to the other executor when he comes&lt;/p&gt;</line></c
