2 TITL marriage announcement, The Salt Lake Tribune
1 _OID ef966ce3-cd04-40b2-9ab6-d7a51a675537
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;The Salt Lake Tribune&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sunday morning, January 16, 1927&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;**SOCIETY**&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size
2 CONC ="5"&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman" size="5"&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;Bishop J.C. Duncan&lt;br&gt;Married to Miss&lt;br&gt;Leona Yorgason&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;ANNOUNCEMENT is made of the marriage of Bishop John C
2 CONC . Duncan, assistant manager of the wholesale notions department of the Z. C. M. I. to Miss Leona L. Yorgason, formerly of the retail sales department of the same institution.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&
2 CONC gt;The marriage was solemnized Thursday morning in the Salt Lake temple, with President George F. Richards officiating.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;The bishop and his bride left immediately for an extended tri
2 CONC p in the east, during which time they will visit Chicago, Niagara Falls, New York City, Washington, D.C., St. Louis and Independence, Mo.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;For the past fifteen years the bishop has pre
2 CONC sided over the First ward of Liberty stake.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;Mrs. Duncan is the daughter of James S. and Ellen Aagard Torgason of Burlington, Wyo., and the granddaughter of A. J. Aagard, founder of Fo
2 CONC untain Green, Utah.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p align="left"&gt;&lt;font size="3"&gt;They expect to return to Salt Lake on or about Washington&amp;#39;s birthday, and will be at home at&amp;nbsp;823 East Seventh South street after that date.&lt;/fo
2 CONC nt&gt;&lt;font face="Times New Roman"&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
