2 TITL Church of St Wilfrids in Ribchester
1 _OID f0a0eb42-7e5e-4d2f-9755-44c94d59c08a
1 DATE 1720
1 PLAC Ribchester, Lancashire, England
1 _DSCR St Wilfrid's dates from the 13th century, built on a site close to that of a Roman fort, Bremetennacum.[2] A chapel and porch were added in the 14th century. A tower was added to the west in the late 15th century. In the 16th century, the roofs wer
2 CONC e removed in order to increase the height of the chancel walls and new windows were added to the aisle wall. Major repairs to the building took place in 1685–6 and 1711. A west gallery was added in 1736. 
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription /></metadataxml>
