2 TITL Temperance Westwood short biography
1 _OID f1f051cb-0ac2-4010-900f-98ead3bec8f8
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr id="sRes-0" class="tblrow record keySelect" valign="top" style="border-bottom: 1px solid #cdc7be"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table border="0" width="100%" style="border-bottom: medium none"&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;
2 CONC tr valign="top"&gt;&lt;td class="body" align="left" style="border: medium none"&gt;Mrs.  Temperance Moon, residing at Farmington, is the widow of Bishop Henry  Moon and was born in Worcestershire, England, August 19, 1839, being a  daughter of Jose
2 CONC ph W. and Ann (Webley) Westwood, who were natives of  England and came to America in 1849. They settled in St. Louis,  Missouri, and both died there within a week after their arrival, cholera  being the occasion of their demise. They left seven chi
2 CONC ldren, who  remained in St. Louis for four years and then came to Salt Lake City in  1853. &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; 	 	 &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr id="sRes-1" class="tblrowalt record" valign="top" style="border-bottom: 1
2 CONC px solid #cdc7be"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table border="0" width="100%" style="border-bottom: medium none"&gt; 	&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr valign="top"&gt;&lt;td class="body" align="left" style="border: medium none"&gt;Mrs.  Moon was one of the seven and continu
2 CONC ed her residence in Salt Lake City  until after her marriage in 1856 to Henry Moon. A month later he was  ordained a bishop under Brigham Young and filled that office in the  first ward of the Salt Lake stake for fourteen years. He next removed t
2 CONC o  North Farmington and was ordained high priest. He also filled a mission  to Iowa and as the years passed he put forth earnest and effective  labor to advance the interests of the church and uphold the cause in  which he so firmly believed. He di
2 CONC ed in that faith in 1894. &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; 	 	 &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr id="sRes-2" class="tblrow record" valign="top" style="border-bottom: 1px solid #cdc7be"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table border="0" width="100%" sty
2 CONC le="border-bottom: medium none"&gt; 	&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr valign="top"&gt;&lt;td class="body" align="left" style="border: medium none"&gt;To  Mr. and Mrs. Moon were born thirteen children: Robert H., deceased;  Joseph Hyrum, who resides at Woodland
2 CONC , Utah; Hannah, who has passed  away; Elnora, the wife of Bishop Hess; Rowane, the wife of Thomas Udy;  Henry M.; Edmund, deceased; Phillip, who follows farming at Farmington;  Olive, the wife of William Potter; Eveline, the wife of George Udy;  Lo
2 CONC uise, the wife of Joseph Moon, who though of the same name was not a  relative; Albert, of Farmington E., deceased. &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; 	 	 &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr id="sRes-3" class="tblrowalt record" valign="top
2 CONC " style="border-bottom: 1px solid #cdc7be"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table border="0" width="100%" style="border-bottom: medium none"&gt; 	&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr valign="top"&gt;&lt;td class="body" align="left" style="border: medium none"&gt;When  death calle
2 CONC d Mr. Moon he was laid to rest in the Farmington cemetery.  He had three wives and twenty-six children, three children being born of  his first marriage, thirteen of the second marriage and ten of the  third marriage. &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; 	 	 &lt
2 CONC ;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr id="sRes-4" class="tblrow record" valign="top" style="border-bottom: 1px solid #cdc7be"&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;table border="0" width="100%" style="border-bottom: medium none"&gt; 	&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;t
2 CONC r valign="top"&gt;&lt;td class="body" align="left" style="border: medium none"&gt;At  her husband&amp;#39;s death Mrs. Temperance Moon received from him a farm which  she afterward sold to her children and she now makes her home in  Farmington, whe
2 CONC re she owns and occupies a nice residence. She has for  many years lived in this state, witnessing its growth and development,  and is classed with the pioneer women of Utah. &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&
2 CONC lt;/tbody&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
