1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;lds.org/ldsorg is source for material:&amp;nbsp; SEAGOING SAINTS by Fred E. Wood, Ensign, Sept 2001:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;First mission to England was 1837.&amp;nbsp; British Mission in Liverpool established.&amp;n
2 CONC bsp; First group of Saints embarked on the BRITANNIA in June 1840.&amp;nbsp; Hugh Moon recalled that he found Brigham Young and Heber C. Kimball on the ship. &amp;quot;They had stretched a curtain across our cabin and commenced blessing the company
2 CONC .&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;See also THE BOOK OF THE LIFE OF HUGH MOON. Historial Dept Archives.&amp;nbsp; Church of JC of LDS.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;See www.scribd.com/doc/16235111/writingsofearlylatterdaysaintsbyvariousauthors&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&am
2 CONC p;nbsp;- couldn&amp;#39;t access it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;See mormonhistoricsitesfoundation.org/publications:&amp;nbsp; GATHERING TO NAUVOO:&amp;nbsp; mormon immigration 1840-46.&amp;nbsp; Fred E. Woods. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;6 June 1840, English conver
2 CONC t John Moon and 40 Saints left Liverpool - brothers Hugh and Francis too. Before 1846 a quarter of the Saints in Nauvoo were British.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
