1 _OID f464e7a6-99e2-42d0-aed2-4b8d72a55aa2
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;Pugsley Street (700 North to Ouray Ave.) in SLC is named after Philip Pugsley.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;1886 Philip built a house at 574 North 300 West. This became Moore&amp;#39;s Market and Marsh Auto year
2 CONC s and years later before it was finally torn down in 2005. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1884-1892 James Alonzo Raleigh and Sarah Isabel Pugsley occupied the home at 271 West 300 North. Joseph Smith Barlow and Clarissa Pugsley lived in the home by 1900, wit
2 CONC h their six children and Clarissa&amp;#39;s mother, Clarissa Ames Pugsley. The house was also torn down in 2005.&lt;/p&gt; 		 	 	&lt;font face="TimesNewRomanPS"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
