2 TITL Obit of Alta Jones Moon
1 _OID f7d4166b-d6d9-42e5-a43c-c83aca202529
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Alta J. Moon passed away due to causes incident to age, on Tuesday, December 13, 2011, at the age of 95.&amp;n
2 CONC bsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800
2 CONC 000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;She was born October 6, 1916, to Brigham W. and Mary Ashton Jones in Cherry Creek, Idaho. Alta married Dale Moon on August 19, 1936, in Ogden, Utah. They made their home in Henders
2 CONC on Creek, Idaho. Their marriage was later solemnized in the Logan, Utah LDS Temple. Dale died in September of 1995.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br styl
2 CONC e="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Alta was an active member of the Church of Jesus Christ o
2 CONC f Latter-day Saints, serving in many capacities. She especially enjoyed serving in the Young Womens program.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.
2 CONC 800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;She worked at Crowther Bros. Milling Company and the Oneida County Nursing H
2 CONC ome in Malad. Alta always had such a zest for life and was always so much fun. She really had a great sense of humor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br st
2 CONC yle="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Growing up on a farm, Alta was a hard worker and taught h
2 CONC er children a great work ethic. She mowed her own lawn while living on her farm in Henderson Creek until she was 91 years of age. At that time, she moved to Malad and lived in the South Apartments where she enjoyed her wonderful neighbors and cit
2 CONC y life.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font
2 CONC -size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Alta was a wonderful cook and homemaker and was an excellent mother to the end. Her priority was her children and grandchildren - her posterity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br sty
2 CONC le="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height
2 CONC : normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Alta was preceded in death by her parents; sisters, Faye and Sylvia and brothers, Avon and Leland.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color
2 CONC : #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;She is survived by her children C
2 CONC onnie Kelso, of Sandy, Utah; Dalene (Varnell) Bench, of Brigham City, Utah; Brent (Alicia) Moon, of Fielding, Utah; Sharon (Terry) Williams, of Pocatello, Idaho and Cindy Moon, of Helena, Montana; 18 grandchildren; 49 great-grandchildren (with on
2 CONC e more on the way); nine great-great-grandchildren; brother, Cleland (Neva) Jones, of Cherry Creek; sister, Norma (John) Everett, of Pineville, Louisiana and sister, Lawana Klontz, of Ogden, Utah.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.80000019073
2 CONC 4863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #
2 CONC dcd0cf;"&gt;A special thanks is given to Mindy Allen from Oneida Home Health and to Access Home Care and Hospice.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;br style="font-size
2 CONC : 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;Funeral services will be held Saturday, December 17, 2011 at 1:00 p.m
2 CONC . at the 2nd/4th/5th LDS Ward building. A viewing will be held from 11:00 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. at the church, prior to the services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&
2 CONC gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-size: 12.800000190734863px; line-height: normal; background-color: #dcd0cf;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-s
