2 TITL Pioneer Overland Tavel - Trail Excerpts by Hugh Moon
1 _OID f9b1ee54-a4ba-4401-b150-dfb04698eb9c
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;span&gt;Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847&amp;ndash;1868&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source of Trail Excerpt:&lt;/strong&gt;Moon, Hugh, The book of the life of Hugh Moon, 4.&lt;strong&gt;Read Trail Excerpt
2 CONC :&lt;/strong&gt;October 21, 1847&amp;mdash;Hugh Moon Jr., son of Hugh and Maria Moon was born. There was a man by the name of Robert Wilson working near to where we lived in a Copper Shop. I went and engaged with him to learn me the copper trade i
2 CONC n order to make a fit out to go to Salt Lake Valley where a company of pioneers had gone the year before. I made sufficient to buy tires, iron, etc., for a wagon, the timber of which I had got out while at Nauvoo. &lt;p&gt;Hyrum Mott, uncle to my w
2 CONC ife, paid for the blacksmithing which was a great blessing to us, for we were poor in consequence of sickness. Maria, my wife, had a yoke of small steers and two cows, or rather a cow with a broken hip bone and a heifer. I made my wagon myself. W
2 CONC e hitched up our little team and put our little duds into the wagon and in company with Moses Whitter [Whitaker] started for Salt Lake Valley, 1848&amp;mdash;May 15th. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;June 1&amp;mdash;We got Pisgah. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;June 14&am
2 CONC p;mdash;We reached Council Bluffs. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;July 2&amp;mdash;We started for Salt Lake. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;July 6&amp;mdash;Crossed Elkhorn &amp;ndash; We overtook Amasey [Amasa Mason] Lyman&amp;rsquo;s company under the command of Captai
2 CONC n [James Madison] Fleak [Flake]. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;July 8&amp;mdash;We camped on the Plat[t]e river &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;July 16&amp;mdash;We crossed the Loppefork [Loup Fork]. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;July 28th&amp;mdash;A pleasant day, hard drive. Abou
2 CONC t 6 o&amp;rsquo;clock we drove up between the Platte River and chain of Sant Hills, stopped a little while, then was turned back by Captain Fleak. We went &amp;frac34; of a mile and camped. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;July 30th&amp;mdash;Touched at the Plat
2 CONC te, had meeting, divided the company into three divisions; brother A. Lyman gave some good instruction, etc. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;August 7th&amp;mdash;Met a war party of Sioux Indians. They stopped the company, held a council, we gave a small donatio
2 CONC n then they let us go on. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;August 19th&amp;mdash;Crossed the Laramie forks at the fort. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;August 29th&amp;mdash;Came to Deer Creek&amp;mdash;stopped a week to recruit the stock. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;September 28th&a
2 CONC mp;mdash;Crossed Green River. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;October 11th&amp;mdash;Came to Weber. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;October 19th&amp;mdash;Got to Salt Lake Valley. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hugh Moon, Jr., son of Hugh and Maria Moon died on the 7th of November, 184
2 CONC 8, being one year and seventeen days old. He died in consequence of the hardships of coming over the plains to Salt Lake.&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
