2 TITL Religious Preamble to the Will of Robert Moon
1 _OID f9f6dd8a-e6bb-4dec-bf74-d5d6c12bfc43
1 DATE 19 May 1691
1 PLAC Woodplumpton, Lancashire, Kingdom of England
1 _DSCR An extract from The Moons of Amounderness
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: medium;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Robert Moon was buried at Woodplumpton on 29 May, 1691. Th
2 CONC e religious outlook of the Moon family is strongly emphasised by the preamble to his will made 19 May, 1691, which states that &amp;lsquo;I Robert Moon of Catforth within Woodplumpton, yeoman, being sicke in body but of good and perfect memory, tha
2 CONC nks be to almighty God for the same, and calling to remembrance &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;the uncertain state of this transitory life, and that all &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;flesh must yield unt
2 CONC o death when it shall please God &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;to call, doe make, constitute, ordaine and declare this &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;my last will and testament in manner and forme fol&am
2 CONC p;shy; lowing (that is to say) first and specifically I commend my soule unto the hands of Almighty God, my Saviour and Redeemer, in whom, and by the merits of Jesus Christ, I trust and believe assuredly to be saved, and to have full remission an
2 CONC d foregiveness of all my sins, and that my soule with my body at the general day of resurrection shall rise again with joy, and though the merits of Christ&amp;rsquo;s death and passion, possess and inherit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family
2 CONC : times;"&gt;the Kingdom of Heaven prepared for his elect and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;chosen, and my body I commit to the earth to be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;buried at the Chappell of Woodpl
2 CONC umpton, at the dis&amp;shy; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;cretion of my executors hereafter mentioned . . . &amp;rdquo;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/di
2 CONC v&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
