1 _DSCR The contents of this website are no longer available in our Freedom of Information World. Perhaps ancestry.com is the last bastion of democracy? Fortunately I saved it to an independent file:    First of all, allow me to explain the current situati
2 CONC on by exploring historical truths.  From the earliest history of instrumental music and “symphony”, we learn from archeological evidence uncovered primarily in the “fertile crescent” of ancient Ur of the Chaldees that the contemporaries of Father A
2 CONC braham created specific musical instruments and tuned them to a “keynote” pitch of 432 hz.  A number of metallic “tuning triangles” have in fact been unearthed in modern-day Iraq, that were used to “tune” various stringed instruments to a keynote p
2 CONC itch of 432 hz – known today as “Concert A” pitch.    There exists in antiquity early Chaldean “Tuning” Triangle the original form of today’s “Tuning Forks” – emitting 432 hz tone.    Why did the early Chaldeans tune their various stringed instrume
2 CONC nts to 432 hz??   The biblical record explains the most probable reason.   At the age of 99,  we learn that Abraham was engaged in studying the stars in the night sky when he discovered the reality of God and eventually received a series of “revela
2 CONC tions” concerning God’s plan of salvation and of course a SAVIOR (Messiah) which would eventually come to the world from Abraham’s numerous seed.   That is the central core message of the entire Old Testament, (as well as the New Testament) – and i
2 CONC t all began thousands of years ago, with Abraham studying the movements of the night sky.  Consider that modern astronomical science has verified what Abraham likely already knew – that the heavens themselves testify of the base number 432.  For in
2 CONC stance, it takes exactly 72 years for the stars to travel a mere one degree around the 25,920 year grand procession of the equinox through the 12 “star constellations” cycles.   There are 360 degrees in a complete circle.  72 years x 360 degrees o
2 CONC f a circle = 25,920 total years.    The number 432 multiplied by the number 60 equals the 25,920 year procession of the equinox, as well as all of the planetary and stellar “processions” which also just happen to perfectly align with the base numbe
2 CONC r 432.   Is it just a coincidence that Abraham’s culture, the ancient Chaldees, produced instruments tuned to this base number of 432 hz vibrations?  The salient question is, which came first, Abraham’s covenant with God, the Creator of the Univers
2 CONC e, or Abraham’s knowledge of the 432 connection to the Creator of the Uni (one) Verse (song) that lent him the process to find and access God?   The other question I have to ask is: How can the “grand procession” of the stars from an “observatory
2 CONC ” on earth be true, if the the earth is billions of “light years” away from the nearest “star” – while hurtling through the “galaxy” at 66,600 mph???  Psalms 19:1 The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament (where the stars are placed
2 CONC ) sheweth his handywork.  Psalms 150:1 Praise ye the LORD. Praise God in his sanctuary: praise him in the firmament of his power.  Following the starting point of Abraham’s covenant with God the Creator, we learn from the Biblical record that Abrah
2 CONC am’s miraculous posterity became inter-twined with that of Egypt.  For over four hundred years, Abraham’s seed served as servants to the Egyptians – until Moses came upon the scene.  Consider that Moses’ sister Miriam was, according to the Bible
2 CONC , a highly skilled dancer and singer very much in demand in the royal courts of Egypt.  See Exodus 15:20-21.   What musical songs and frequency pitch did she dance and sing to?  Once again, archeological evidence tells us that the vast majority o
2 CONC f ancient Egyptian instruments were also tuned to the base frequency of 432 hz.  From the hand of Moses came the safety-net called the LAW, and during their subsequent sojourn in the wilderness to their establishment as a nation in Palestine, musi
2 CONC c clearly became an integral part of their sublime worship and oblations to their God.   In clear distinction from that of the bedouin nations surrounding them, the music of the ancient Hebrews was not sensuous in nature, but was in fact a true sac
2 CONC ramental oblation to their God.  Clearly, to the ancient Hebrew, music was not an art form, but very much a part of their religion.  Biblical historians and archeologists have surmised that David, the shepherd-boy, was skilled in the use of three p
2 CONC rimary instruments – ALL TUNED TO 432 hz.   First was a simple reed flute instrument consisting of a seven-note, chromatic scale with “A” being tuned as the “keynote” to 432 hz.   Second was an early form of the Scottish “bagpipes” called a “sympho
2 CONC nia”, and third, a stringed instrument called a Psanterin (that music from it was named “psaltery” or today’s biblical Psalms).    An example is an early Hebrew “pipe” instrument called a “symphonia” – circa 10th Century B.C.E.    David, the Shephe
2 CONC rd, played his reed flute to calm the sheep. In europe we often care for the farm animals by putting them in barnes. In Australia they seek out trees. Have we not lost the medieval interconnectedness of being "my brothers keeper". The Christ refer
2 CONC s to caring for his people like a shepherd caring for his sheep. This instrument had the power to keep away evil spirits from both people and sheep and keep demons and wolves abated and at bay.    Ishmael’s Pipe is a common musical instrument of Ch
2 CONC aldeans resonating at 432 hz.    The Hebrew “Priests” played a “Psanterin”  inscription dated 10th century BCE.    The Bible then details that during the time of the Prophet Jeremiah, the nation of Israel was once again conquered and “taken captiv
2 CONC e into Babylon”.   Psalm 137 reads: “By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion. 2 We hanged our harps (psanterins) upon the willows in the midst thereof. (They quit playing their sacred songs) 3 For there th
2 CONC ey that carried us away captive required of us a song; and they that wasted us required of us mirth, saying, Sing us one of the songs of Zion. 4 How shall we sing the LORD’S song in a strange land?”  Indeed, what exactly is the “LORD’S SONG”??   Co
2 CONC uld the “Lord’s Song” be specifically singing and playing instruments in the tuning of 432 hz?   The evidence that follows says  the answer to that question is an emphatic YES!  The “12 Tribes” of Israel eventually became scattered over the face o
2 CONC f the earth, but the record shows that Six (Roman Number VI) Kings (i.e the posterity of the Six Sons of Leah) went into the Northern (Norse) Lands and eventually became know as the  “VI (six) Kings” – or what we call today the “Vikings.”   Once ag
2 CONC ain the archeological record shows that 432 hz music was also an integral part of the VI (Six) Kings of the North and their culture.    The first part of this paper provides a brief overview of the origins of western Religious Music – which clearl
2 CONC y from the time of David until the mid 20th Century, was pretty much uniformly played with “Concert A” being tuned to the “keynote” of 432 hz.   Just as the ancient Hebrews were extremely strict in the preservation of their sacred written texts, (b
2 CONC ecause they revered them as “God-Breathed”) so too, I submit, did they preserve their sacred music “keynote” tone of 432 hz even through the “Dark Ages” as well as the “Renaissance” years up until the year 1953.    Today, however, the “standard” Co
2 CONC ncert A pitch is no longer “432” but has been raised 8 hz by the United Nations’ “International Standards Organization”  (ISO) to 440 hz.   The remainder of this expose will consider the questions: Why was this done, by whom, and more importantly
2 CONC , does a mere 8 hz. change even matter at all?  As we explore these questions, consider the words of the Prophet Isaiah: “The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent m
2 CONC e to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound.   (Isaiah 61:1)   I submit this is exactly what Christian “pastors” and “worship teams” are supposed to do for Christ – use C
2 CONC hrist’s WORDS (which are vocalized frequencies of sound) as prompted by the Holy Spirit, as well as pure MUSIC (Tone Frequencies of Sound) to 1. bring “good tidings” (the Gospel message) unto the humble, meek hearts who will accept it, 2. to HEAL T
2 CONC HE BROKEN AND HOPELESS  who need the Hope of Christ in their lives, 3. to proclaim LIBERTY to those held captive by the DARK IGNORANCE of the Adversary of Christ, and 4. OPEN UP THE PRISON DOORS TO THEM THAT ARE BOUND.   (To me, that means the goo
2 CONC d Mormon people and their false “heliocentric” priesthood of Baal that “Binds (make people’s souls bound or imprisoned) on Earth as well as in Heaven”).  Is it just a coincidence that the entire complete ARAMAIC/HEBREW text of Isaiah 61:1 has a pre
