2 CONC olor: #444444; font-size: 9pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt;"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;; freeman, Exeter 1643; commr. for oyer and terminer, Western circuit July 1660; dep
2 CONC . lt. Cornw. 1661-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt;"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;s
2 CONC pan style="color: #13a8c9; font-size: 8pt; text-decoration: none; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; text-underline: none;"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 18pt; margin: 0cm 0cm 14.4pt;"&
2 CONC gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;Col. of horse (royalist) 1642-6; gov. St. Mawes 1644-6, June 1660-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt; mso-bidi-fon
2 CONC t-size: 12.0pt;"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #13a8c9; font-size: 8pt; text-decoration: none; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; text-underline: none;"&gt;3&l
2 CONC t;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 18pt; margin: 0cm 0cm 14.4pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;Master of the mint (royalist) 1642-6; asst. So
2 CONC c. of Mines Royal 1656-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt;"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;
2 CONC ; member Soc. of Mineral and Battery Works 1663-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt;"&gt;d.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444
2 CONC 444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="color: #13a8c9; font-size: 8pt; text-decoration: none; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; text-underline: none;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="line-height: 13.5pt; margin: 11.25p
2 CONC t 0cm 3.75pt; mso-outline-level: 3;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: dinweb; color: #495965; font-size: 12.5pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial;"&gt;Biography&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;
2 CONC p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 18pt; margin: 0cm 0cm 14.4pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;Vyvyan&amp;rsquo;s family was established in Cornwall by the 13th century and first represented H
2 CONC elston in 1421. Vyvyan inherited a considerable estate, including St. Mawes Castle and ex-monastic property; and when he had cleared off his father&amp;rsquo;s debts and legacies, his income may have reached &amp;pound;1,200 p.a. Of a scholarly dis
2 CONC position he was more interested in theology and the arts than in politics; nevertheless he raised a regiment on the outbreak of the Civil War, and agreed to act as master of the Mint in the West for Charles I. Disabled in 1644, he sat in the Oxfor
2 CONC d Parliament, and compounded on the Exeter articles on a fine of &amp;pound;600. He was treated with unusual severity by the county committee, however, who proceeded to sequestrate his estate and seize his stock and other goods, and he did not obta
2 CONC in a discharge until 1651. Altogether, he computed that he had lost &amp;pound;9,982 in the King&amp;rsquo;s service.&lt;span style="color: #13a8c9; font-size: 8pt; text-decoration: none; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; text-underline: none;"&gt;5&lt;/
2 CONC span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-align: justify; line-height: 18pt; margin: 0cm 0cm 14.4pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: verdana; color: #444444; font-size: 9pt;"&gt;At the Restoration, which he commemorated by erec
2 CONC ting two granite pillars in Trelowarren Park bearing his initials, Vyvyan was rewarded with the governorship of St. Mawes, carrying the rank of captain in the army and a salary of &amp;pound;182 p.a. In November 1660 he petitioned unsuccessfully fo
2 CONC r a lease of Dartmouth and Plymouth harbours, the tithes of Bradninch, and repayment of &amp;pound;1,500 spent on fortifying Dennis Head for Charles I. But the garrison of St. Mawes was strengthened, and he was given &amp;pound;239 to repair the ca
2 CONC stle. He stood for the borough at the general election of 1661, and was involved in a double return with &lt;span style="color: #13a8c9; text-decoration: none; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; text-underline: none;"&gt;(Sir) William Tredenham&lt;/span&g
2 CONC t;. An order of the House of 3 May 1662 for hearing his petition on the merits of the election produced no result; but Tredenham died nine days later, and Vyvyan was returned at a by-election in the following year. An inactive Member of the Cavalie
2 CONC r Parliament, he was appointed to only eleven committees, including in the 1663 session those to prevent meetings of sectaries, to consider the additional bill for the relief of loyal and indigent officers, and to recover arrears of the excise. H
2 CONC e was added to the committee of elections and privileges on 7 Feb. 1665, and later in the month acted as teller against a proviso to the bill enabling the Government to pay over the legal rate of interest. He died on 3 Oct., leaving portions of &am
2 CONC p;pound;1,000 each to his five surviving daughters, and was buried at Mawgan in Meneage.&lt;span style="color: #13a8c9; font-size: 8pt; text-decoration: none; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; text-underline: none;"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&g
2 CONC t;</line><line>&lt;p style="line-height: 13.5pt; margin: 0cm 0cm 0pt; mso-outline-level: 3; mso-margin--alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: dinweb; color: #495965; font-size: 13.5pt;"&gt;&lt;span s
2 CONC tyle="font-family: arial;"&gt;Ref Volumes: 1660-1690&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="line-height: 13.5pt; margin: 7.5pt 7.5pt 0pt -9pt; mso-outline-level: 3;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family
2 CONC : dinweb; color: #495965; font-size: 13.5pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: arial;"&gt;Author: Eveline Cruickshanks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
