2 TITL Margaret Whittle/Cross 1648 - 1730 - Siblings.
1 _OID ff5ab711-9c84-4b7f-ad35-c2645d50c9f2
1 DATE 1678
1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;There is a document held at Lancs. Archives (DDSH 25/15) which gives some useful evidence as to the parentage of Margaret.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Dated 20&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; March 1678.&lt;/p&gt;</
2 CONC line><line>&lt;p&gt;It is an indenture of lease between &lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;Ralph Whittle&lt;/strong&gt; of Whittle-le-Woods, nephew and heir of &lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;William Whittle,&lt
2 CONC ;/strong&gt; &lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;deceased husbandman of Whittle-le-Woods, &lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;on one part &lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span
2 CONC &gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;and Robert Dicconson, linen draper of Chorley, Robert Halliwell, gent of Whittle, and Ralph Lowe, &lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;gent of Whittle on the other part.&lt;/p&gt;</line><
2 CONC line>&lt;p&gt;Regards a messuage and tenement in Whittle-le-Woods.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;To have and hold for use of Ralph Whittle - and after his death to his heirs male - &lt;span style="mso-spacerun: yes;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;in d
2 CONC efault of such to heirs female - in default of such for use and behoof of:&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;"&gt;&lt;!--[if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: symbol; mso-fareast-font-f
2 CONC amily: symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: symbol;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-list: ignore;"&gt;&amp;middot;&lt;span style="font: 7.0pt 'times new roman';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;
2 CONC /span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;Elizabeth, wife of William Houghton, alias Gill, husbandman of Chorley&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;"&gt;&lt;!--[if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="f
2 CONC ont-family: symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: symbol;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-list: ignore;"&gt;&amp;middot;&lt;span style="font: 7.0pt 'times new roman';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
2 CONC &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;MARGARET&lt;/strong&gt;, wife of &lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;RICHARD CROSS&lt;/strong&gt; o
2 CONC f &lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;Bretherton&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;"&gt;&lt;!--[if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: symbol; mso-fareast-f
2 CONC ont-family: symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: symbol;"&gt;&lt;span style="mso-list: ignore;"&gt;&amp;middot;&lt;span style="font: 7.0pt 'times new roman';"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt
2 CONC ;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;Ann Whittle spinster and Jane Whittle spinster&amp;nbsp; .....and their heirs&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;"&gt;Aforesaid Elizabeth, Ann, Margaret, Jan
2 CONC e being sisters of aforesaid Ralph Whittle.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;Same to be equally divided between them share and share alike and for no other intent or purposes.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;..... provisos regarding rig
2 CONC hts of R Dicconson, R Halliwell and R Lowe.&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="mso-margin--alt: auto; margin-bottom: .0001pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%;"&gt;Comments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="mar
2 CONC gin-: 0cm; margin-right: 0cm; margin-bottom: 6.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%;"&gt;The siblings Ralph, Elizabeth, Margaret, Ann and Jane fit neatly as being children of John Whittle and Elizabeth Wrenno/Wrennal of Cho
2 CONC rley - though no baptism record for Margaret!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="mso-margin--alt: auto; margin-bottom: 6.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%;"&gt;Seems Ralph married and had lots of kids - so M
2 CONC argaret and sisters would not habe benefited.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></content></metadataxml>
