1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: large;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Appointed his nephews Richard and Robert&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&g
2 CONC t;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Moon and his great nephew Ralph Brocklebank,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;junior, executors. He bequeathed to his sister-in&amp;shy;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family
2 CONC : times;"&gt;law. Jane Anne Holland for her life an annuity of &amp;pound;300.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;To his &amp;lsquo;valued clerk&amp;rsquo;, Samuel Frodsham, an annuity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style
2 CONC ="font-family: times;"&gt;of &amp;pound;300. To William Hudson Twire, who was husband&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;of his late niece Mary Twire &amp;pound;50. To Mrs. Moon, wife&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=
2 CONC "font-family: times;"&gt;of his brother William Moon, &amp;pound;50. To Henry Garcia, husband of his niece Anne Gertrude Garcia &amp;pound;50. To&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;his brother, William Moon, &amp;pound;10
2 CONC 0, and to his latter&amp;rsquo;s son, Henry William Moon, &amp;pound;100. To his brother&amp;mdash;in&amp;shy; law, Samuel Martin. &amp;pound;100, his great nephew, Edward Moon, eldest son of his nephew, Richard Moon &amp;pound;500. To his godson
2 CONC , Edward Robert Pacey Moon, eldest son of his nephew, Robert Moon, &amp;pound;500. To his goddaughter&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;Alice Ann Edwards, the wife of James Bevin Edwards, a Lieutenant Colonel in the Roya
2 CONC l Engineers, &amp;pound;500.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;To his niece Anne Gertrude Garcia, &amp;pound;1000; his niece Elizabeth Ann Brocklebank &amp;pound;2000; his niece Isabella&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span st
2 CONC yle="font-family: times;"&gt;Aspinall &amp;pound;2000; his niece Mary Elizabeth Wood &amp;pound;2000; his nephew Samuel Iohn Martin &amp;pound;2500; his great nephew Ralph Brocklebank, junior, &amp;pound;10,000; his nephew Richard Moon &amp;pound;3
2 CONC 0,000; and to his nephew Robert Moon &amp;pound;35,000. The legacy of &amp;pound;15.000 to his niece Anna Scott if she were living, but if dead to her husband Hercules Scott.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&g
2 CONC t;He gave to his trustees legacies of &amp;pound;25,000 and &amp;pound;10,000 upon certain trusts. &amp;pound;10,000 held for the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;benefit of his niece Margaret Wrigley and her children &lt;/span&
2 CONC gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;was revoked because his brother William Moon, father &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;of Margaret \Vrigley, and the said Margaret Wrigley had both died, and the children were amply prov
2 CONC ided &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;for by the will of his late brother.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times; font-size: large;"&gt;He also bequeathed to his niece Isabella Aspinall, in addition to the leg
2 CONC acy an annuity of &amp;pound;600 for life, and to his clerk Charles Newman, an annuity of &amp;pound;150 for life.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: times;"&gt;The trustees were to pay to the four daughters of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;spa
2 CONC n style="font-family: times;"&gt;his deceased niece Margaret VVrigley when they at&amp;shy; tained the age of 21 years, &amp;pound;100, and to WilliamMoon, grandson of his deceased brother William Moon, when he attained the age of 21 years &amp;pou
2 CONC nd;100 free of legacy duty. Other legacies were to be free of legacy duty.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;/div&gt;</line><line>&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;</line></content></m
